window.TOEIC_SUDU={"6-1":{"tree":"【6-1 交通運輸服務：機場接駁與租車服務 Airport Shuttle & Car Rental】\n │\n ├── 🔴 S - Situation (情境確認：提出接駁需求與詢問步行距離／情境確認：航班起飛延誤 25 分鐘與接駁車說明／情境確認：網訂中型轎車與航廈接駁體驗)\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **Shuttle service** (接駁服務), **Within walking distance** (步行可達距離), **Car rental** (租車服務), **Midsize sedan** (中型轎車), **Heavy traffic on the route** (跑道路線交通擁堵)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── \"Excuse me, I need the shuttle service to downtown. Is it within walking distance?\" / \"Yes, just outside Terminal B. We also have car rental services. Did you reserve a midsize sedan?\" / \"Good afternoon, passengers. Due to heavy traffic on the route to the runway, our departure is delayed by 25 minutes.\"\n │\n ├── 📋 T - Task (任務說明：詢問租車保險項目與里程政策／任務說明：提醒地面交通選項與車型、GPS 里程確認／任務說明：導航輔助行駛與市區還車便捷度)\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **Unlimited mileage** (無限里程), **Pickup location** (取車地點), **Ground transportation** (地面交通), **Real-time traffic updates** (即時交通更新), **Downtown drop-off location** (市中心還車/降落地點)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── \"Yes, I did. Does it include GPS and unlimited mileage?\" / \"Correct. The pickup location is in Terminal A.\" / \"While waiting, let me remind you about ground transportation at your arrival city. We offer shuttle service and car rental with midsize sedans available. All vehicles include GPS and unlimited mileage.\"\n │\n ├── 💡 A - Action (行動方案：更換取車地點與提供免費轉運／行動方案：快速接駁時間、取車地點 C 航廈／行動方案：指出唯一缺點、漏發通知延遲)\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **Drop-off** (還車/放人下車), **Free for customers** (顧客免費), **Every 15 minutes** (每 15 分鐘一班), **Outside Terminal C** (C 航廈外面), **Free transportation** (免費交通)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── \"But I can change it to our downtown office near your hotel for easier drop-off. Transportation between locations is free for customers.\" / \"Perfect! How much would the bus cost without your service?\" / \"Our express service shuttles run every 15 minutes to downtown hotels not within walking distance. The pickup location is outside Terminal C, with the drop-off location clearly marked.\"\n │\n ├── ✅ R - Result (結果確認：確認快速服務與公車票價對照／結果確認：提供交通折價券給常客／結果確認：管理層改善標示、補償 500 點)\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **Bus cost** (公車費用/票價), **Express service** (快速服務), **Transportation vouchers** (交通折價券/乘車券), **Frequent flyers** (飛行常客), **Improved our shuttle signage** (改善接駁車標示)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── \"The city bus is $3.50, but you won't need it. Our express service covers that route.\" / \"Staff can answer questions like 'How much would the bus cost?' and provide transportation vouchers for frequent flyers.\" / \"Management Response: Thank you, Ms. Chen. We've improved our shuttle signage. We've added 500 bonus points to your account.\"\n │\n ├── 🔄 同義轉換 (Paraphrase Map)\n │    ├── **Shuttle service** ── transfer service = transportation service\n │    ├── **Within walking distance** ── nearby = close by\n │    ├── **Car rental** ── rental car = vehicle rental\n │    ├── **Unlimited mileage** ── no mileage restriction = drive as much as needed\n │    ├── **Pickup location** ── collection point = where to get the car\n │    └── **Drop-off** ── returns = returning the vehicle\n │\n └── ⚠ 高頻防雷陷阱 (Common Traps)\n      ├── 1. **Within walking distance** ── 如果「步行無法到達（not within walking distance）」，則多益聽力與閱讀中必考「需要交通工具（transportation required）」！\n      ├── 2. **Pickup location** ── 航廈位置區分：取車點（Terminal A）與接駁點（Terminal B）屬於不同地點，不可混淆。\n      ├── 3. **Heavy traffic on the route** ── 此航班延誤是因為「地面交通擁堵（heavy traffic）」，而非飛機「機械故障（mechanical problem）」或「天氣惡劣（weather conditions）」，常設原因干擾！\n      ├── 4. **Outside Terminal C** ── 請看清航廈位置！這裡是 Terminal C ➔ 絕對不是 A 航廈或 B 航廈！聽力常考細節定位。\n      └── 5. **20-minute wait** ── 等待時間與航班延誤時間對應：接駁車等待為 20 分鐘，而廣播航班延誤為 25 分鐘，數據細節不可混淆。","quiz":[{"q":"The express shuttle runs to downtown hotels that are not ________ walking distance from the airport terminal.","o":[["A","among"],["B","within"],["C","beside"],["D","toward"]],"a":"(B) within","zh":"快捷接駁車開往那些不在機場航廈「步行可達距離」內的市區飯店。","e":"固定搭配題。「步行可達距離」之慣用語為 within walking distance；一旦出現 not within walking distance，即為「需要交通工具（transportation required）」之訊號，本篇兩處皆用此句型。"},{"q":"According to the boarding announcement, the express shuttle pickup location is outside ________.","o":[["A","Terminal A"],["B","Terminal B"],["C","Terminal C"],["D","Terminal D"]],"a":"(C) Terminal C","zh":"根據登機廣播，快捷接駁車的上車地點在 C 航廈外面。","e":"地點細節干擾題。本單元出現三個航廈：接駁站牌在 Terminal B（對話）、租車取車點在 Terminal A（對話）、廣播中的接駁上車點則在 Terminal C。題目問「廣播」即應選 (C)。"},{"q":"The flight departure was delayed by 25 minutes because of ________.","o":[["A","a mechanical problem"],["B","severe weather conditions"],["C","heavy traffic on the route to the runway"],["D","a missing crew member"]],"a":"(C) heavy traffic on the route to the runway","zh":"該班機延誤 25 分鐘，是因為前往跑道的路線上交通擁堵。","e":"原因干擾題。多益最愛以「機械故障」「天候不佳」作為誘答；本篇明確指出係 due to heavy traffic on the route to the runway，屬地面交通因素。"},{"q":"In the rental agreement, the phrase \"unlimited mileage\" is closest in meaning to which of the following?","o":[["A","free fuel for the entire trip"],["B","no restriction on the distance driven"],["C","an unlimited rental period"],["D","insurance without a deductible"]],"a":"(B) no restriction on the distance driven","zh":"在租車合約中，「unlimited mileage」與下列何者意思最接近？","e":"同義代換題。unlimited mileage＝no limit on distance／no restriction on the distance driven，指里程不限，與油資、租期或保險自負額均無關。"},{"q":"According to the customer review, how long did the reviewer have to wait for the shuttle?","o":[["A","15 minutes"],["B","20 minutes"],["C","25 minutes"],["D","45 minutes"]],"a":"(B) 20 minutes","zh":"根據顧客評論，這位評論者等接駁車等了多久？","e":"數據混淆題。本單元三個數字必須分清：接駁車「每 15 分鐘一班」、評論者「等了 20 分鐘」、班機「延誤 25 分鐘」。題目問評論者的等待時間，選 (B)。"}],"say":["Excuse me, I need the shuttle service to downtown. Is it within walking distance?","Yes, I did. Does it include GPS and unlimited mileage?","But I can change it to our downtown office near your hotel for easier drop-off. Transportation between locations is free for customers.","The city bus is $3.50, but you won't need it. Our express service covers that route.","Good afternoon, passengers. Due to heavy traffic on the route to the runway, our departure is delayed by 25 minutes.","While waiting, let me remind you about ground transportation at your arrival city. We offer shuttle service and car rental with midsize sedans available. All vehicles include GPS and unlimited mileage.","Our express service shuttles run every 15 minutes to downtown hotels not within walking distance. The pickup location is outside Terminal C, with the drop-off location clearly marked.","Staff can answer questions like 'How much would the bus cost?' and provide transportation vouchers for frequent flyers.","I used QuickMove for my Chicago trip. I reserved a midsize sedan online with unlimited mileage. The pickup location wasn't within walking distance from my terminal, so I took their shuttle service.","The vehicle was clean with an excellent GPS showing the best routes with real-time traffic updates. This saved me time during rush hour transportation. Their express service for returns was convenient. I used the downtown drop-off location instead of returning to the airport.","When I asked 'How much would the bus cost?' back to the airport, they arranged free transportation through their partner shuttle. My only issue: the shuttle departure time from the terminal wasn't posted, causing a 20-minute wait.","Management Response: Thank you, Ms. Chen. We've improved our shuttle signage. We've added 500 bonus points to your account."]},"6-2":{"tree":"【6-2 行程規劃與預定：商務差旅核心溝通 Travel Planning & Booking】\n │\n ├── 🔴 S - Situation (情境確認：提出會議室預訂與海外培訓需求／情境確認：航班機械故障更換，更改起飛時間／情境確認：整合式平台節省 35% 旅費與自動改期)\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **Make a reservation** (進行預訂), **Corporate training session** (企業培訓課程), **Reservation change request** (預訂變更請求), **Mechanical issue** (機械故障), **Corporate booking platform** (企業預訂平台)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── \"Good morning. I'd like to make a reservation for the executive meeting room next Tuesday. We're hosting a corporate training session for our overseas partners.\" / \"Let me check our schedule. I see the room is available from 2 PM. Will that work for you?\" / \"Attention all passengers on Flight 382 to Singapore. We have received and processed your reservation change request due to the mechanical issue with our original aircraft.\"\n │\n ├── 📋 T - Task (任務說明：調整時間、確認整天 9-5 行程表／任務說明：通知 3:45 登機、發送修訂行程表／任務說明：實例分析：每晚 175 美元，訂 2)\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **Entire day** (整天), **Itinerary** (行程表、旅行路線), **Gate B12** (B12 登機門), **Revised itinerary** (修改後的行程表), **CFO** (財務長 (Chief Financial Officer))\n │    └── 必考句型 ── \"Actually, we need it for the entire day. The itinerary shows the training runs from 9 AM to 5 PM. Is there any other room available?\" / \"Your new departure time is 3:45 PM from Gate B12. Please have your confirmation number ready when you board. The revised itinerary has been sent to your registered email addresses.\" / \"CFO James Peterson reported significant savings: 'Our expense reports show we've saved over $45,000. The system automatically applies our negotiated corporate rate of $175 per night at partner hotels, and when we book more than 20 rooms, it triggers an additional group discount of up to 25 percent off the total fare.'\"\n │\n ├── 💡 A - Action (行動方案：提供高級房型全天租用、20% 團體折扣／行動方案：提供商務差價退款、30% 未來折價券／行動方案：靈活取消政策，48 小時前取消免)\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **Premium conference room** (高級會議室), **Corporate rate** (企業優惠價), **Group discount of 20 percent** (20% 的團體折扣), **Full refund of the fare difference** (差價全額退款), **30 percent discount voucher** (30% 折扣券)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── \"The premium conference room is free all day. The corporate rate is $450, but since you're booking for eight hours, I can offer you a group discount of 20 percent.\" / \"As an apology for the inconvenience, we're offering a full refund of the fare difference between economy and business class for passengers who were originally booked in business. Additionally, all passengers will receive a 30 percent discount voucher for future bookings.\" / \"While traditional booking methods often charge hefty cancellation fees, TravelSmart allows changes to be made at least 48 hours in advance without any penalties. 'You must do so at least 48 hours in advance to avoid fees, but that's very reasonable,' said Maria Rodriguez, Travel Coordinator.\"\n │\n ├── ✅ R - Result (結果確認：發送確認信、48 小時前取消政策／結果確認：在客服櫃台領取調整後的企業費率收據／結果確認：自動生成確認號碼與全額退款)\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **Confirmation number** (確認號碼), **Cancellation policy** (取消政策), **48 hours in advance** (提前 48 小時), **50 percent of the total fare** (總費用的 50%), **Expense reports** (費用報銷報告)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── \"That sounds reasonable. Please send me the confirmation number by email. Also, what's your cancellation policy?\" / \"You must do so at least 48 hours in advance to avoid the cancellation fee. Otherwise, you'll be charged 50 percent of the total fare.\" / \"For those who need to submit expense reports to their companies, updated receipts showing the corporate rate adjustments are available at the customer service desk.\"\n │\n ├── 🔄 同義轉換 (Paraphrase Map)\n │    ├── **Make a reservation** ── book = reserve\n │    ├── **Itinerary** ── schedule of events = program = travel plan\n │    ├── **Corporate rate** ── business discount price = negotiated fare\n │    ├── **Confirmation number** ── booking reference = reservation code\n │    ├── **48 hours in advance** ── two days ahead = prior to 48 hours\n │    └── **Reservation change request** ── modification of booking = itinerary adjustment\n │\n └── ⚠ 高頻防雷陷阱 (Common Traps)\n      └── 1. **Gate B12** ── 原登機門被變更，乘客需前往新登機門 B12 登機。","quiz":[{"q":"To avoid the cancellation fee, the customer must cancel the booking at least ________ hours in advance.","o":[["A","24"],["B","36"],["C","48"],["D","72"]],"a":"(C) 48","zh":"為避免被收取取消費用，客戶必須在至少 48 小時前取消預訂。","e":"時限題。對話與閱讀文章兩處均出現 at least 48 hours in advance；請與 6-3 客服公告之「24 小時退款處理期」作區隔，二者數字不同。"},{"q":"If the customer fails to cancel within the required period, he will be charged ________ of the total fare.","o":[["A","25 percent"],["B","50 percent"],["C","75 percent"],["D","the full amount"]],"a":"(B) 50 percent","zh":"若客戶未在規定期間內取消，將被收取總費用的百分之五十。","e":"比例數據題。本篇為 50 percent of the total fare；6-3 鐵路公告則有 75% 的退款級距，兩個百分比不可互換。"},{"q":"Passengers on Flight 382 should now board at Gate ________.","o":[["A","B12"],["B","B23"],["C","C15"],["D","B382"]],"a":"(A) B12","zh":"382 號班機的乘客現在應該在 B12 登機門登機。","e":"登機門變更題。本單元為 Gate B12；6-5 單元則是由 B23 改為 C15。跨單元的登機門數字極易互相干擾，作答時務必確認題幹所指之班機。"},{"q":"Why was the departure time of Flight 382 changed?","o":[["A","Because of heavy traffic on the runway"],["B","Because of a mechanical issue with the aircraft"],["C","Because of a crew shortage"],["D","Because of poor weather at the destination"]],"a":"(B) Because of a mechanical issue with the aircraft","zh":"382 號班機的起飛時間為何變更？","e":"原因對比題。本篇為 mechanical issue（機械問題），與 6-1 之 heavy traffic（交通擁堵）、6-5 之 weather conditions（天候）恰成三組對照，是本章最常設的干擾組。"},{"q":"According to the article, TravelSmart's corporate booking platform has helped over ________ companies reduce travel expenses.","o":[["A","45"],["B","382"],["C","450"],["D","500"]],"a":"(D) 500","zh":"根據該文章，TravelSmart 的企業預訂平台已協助超過 500 家公司降低差旅支出。","e":"數據辨識題。本篇出現多組數字：500 家公司、節省超過 $45,000、會議室企業價 $450。題目問「公司家數」，應選 (D)。"}],"say":["Good morning. I'd like to make a reservation for the executive meeting room next Tuesday. We're hosting a corporate training session for our overseas partners.","Actually, we need it for the entire day. The itinerary shows the training runs from 9 AM to 5 PM. Is there any other room available?","The premium conference room is free all day. The corporate rate is $450, but since you're booking for eight hours, I can offer you a group discount of 20 percent.","That sounds reasonable. Please send me the confirmation number by email. Also, what's your cancellation policy?","Attention all passengers on Flight 382 to Singapore. We have received and processed your reservation change request due to the mechanical issue with our original aircraft.","Your new departure time is 3:45 PM from Gate B12. Please have your confirmation number ready when you board. The revised itinerary has been sent to your registered email addresses.","As an apology for the inconvenience, we're offering a full refund of the fare difference between economy and business class for passengers who were originally booked in business. Additionally, all passengers will receive a 30 percent discount voucher for future bookings.","For those who need to submit expense reports to their companies, updated receipts showing the corporate rate adjustments are available at the customer service desk.","TravelSmart Solutions announced yesterday that their revolutionary corporate booking platform has helped over 500 companies reduce travel expenses by an average of 35 percent since its launch six months ago. The platform automatically applies corporate rates and group discounts.","CFO James Peterson reported significant savings: 'Our expense reports show we've saved over $45,000. The system automatically applies our negotiated corporate rate of $175 per night at partner hotels, and when we book more than 20 rooms, it triggers an additional group discount of up to 25 percent off the total fare.'","While traditional booking methods often charge hefty cancellation fees, TravelSmart allows changes to be made at least 48 hours in advance without any penalties. 'You must do so at least 48 hours in advance to avoid fees, but that's very reasonable,' said Maria Rodriguez, Travel Coordinator.","The confirmation numbers are instantly generated for our accounting department's expense reports, and we can even get a full refund if plans change unexpectedly. The platform charges no booking fees."]},"6-3":{"tree":"【6-3 旅遊場景-服務中斷與客服 Service Disruption & Customer Support】\n │\n ├── 🔴 S - Situation (情境確認：服務中斷與急迫會議時間／情境確認：飛機機械故障、起飛延誤 3 小時／情境確認：軌道維修與號誌系統故障暫停)\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **Service suspension** (服務暫停/中斷), **Technical issue** (技術問題), **Mechanical problem** (機械故障), **Delayed by approximately three hours** (延誤約三小時), **Urgent track maintenance** (緊急軌道維護)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── \"Good morning, I'm calling about my internet service. There's been a service suspension since yesterday afternoon, and I have an important video conference in two hours.\" / \"I apologize for the inconvenience, ma'am. Let me check your account... I see there's a technical issue affecting your area. Our team is working on a mechanical problem at the main distribution center.\" / \"Good afternoon, passengers. This is an announcement from the customer service desk at Terminal 3. We regret to inform you that Flight 782 to Singapore has experienced a mechanical problem and will be delayed by approximately three hours.\"\n │\n ├── 📋 T - Task (任務說明：詢問服務恢復預估時間／任務說明：轉機乘客更改預訂、免收手續費／任務說明：乘客更改行程與免手續費規則)\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **Estimated time** (預估時間), **Service restoration** (服務恢復), **Connecting flights** (轉機/聯程航班), **At Platform 1** (在 1 號月台)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── \"This is really frustrating. I specifically chose your premium plan to avoid these kinds of delays. Can you at least give me an estimated time for service restoration?\" / \"For passengers who have connecting flights, please approach our service counter immediately to discuss change request options. Our staff will help you reschedule your connections at no additional assessment fee.\" / \"Passengers holding tickets for affected services may reschedule their journey at no additional assessment fee. Submit any change request forms at our customer service desk located at Platform 1, or call our hotline.\"\n │\n ├── 💡 A - Action (行動方案：申請兩日服務抵免、提交正式申訴／行動方案：24 小時退款處理、發放 20 美元餐券／行動方案：階梯式退款與免費替代接駁)\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **Disruption** (中斷、干擾), **Compensation** (補償、賠償), **Formal complaint** (正式申訴/客訴), **Meal vouchers** (餐飲券/餐券), **Travel voucher** (旅行折價券/代金券)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── \"According to our system, service should be restored within the next hour. As compensation for this disruption, we'll be applying our refund policy – you'll receive a credit for two days of service. Would you also like to submit a formal complaint to our customer service desk?\" / \"Unfortunately, if you choose to cancel your trip entirely, please note that our refund policy requires a 24-hour processing period for full cancellation refunds. Meal vouchers worth $20 will be distributed to all affected passengers as we work to resolve this service suspension.\" / \"In accordance with our refund policy, passengers with valid tickets for cancelled services will receive: Full refund if requested before April 17; 75% refund plus a travel voucher if cancelled on April 18. Local shuttle buses will operate every 30 minutes.\"\n │\n ├── ✅ R - Result (結果確認：重新安排路由器安裝、豁免 25 美元手續費／結果確認：系統技術問題修復、提供正式申訴管道／結果確認：處理中斷申訴與旅客滿意)\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **Assessment fee** (評估費/手續費), **Waive** (豁免、免除（費用）), **File a complaint** (提出申訴/客訴), **Service disruption** (服務中斷/干擾)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── \"Yes, please. And I'll need to reschedule my installation appointment for the new router that was supposed to happen tomorrow. There's also a change request I submitted last week – can you check on that?\" / \"Certainly. I can reschedule your appointment for next Tuesday at 2 PM. Regarding your change request, there's an assessment fee of $25 that wasn't processed yet. Would you like me to waive that fee given today's service issues?\" / \"This delay is due to a technical issue with our booking system that we're currently addressing. We understand this situation is frustrating, and we encourage anyone with concerns to file a complaint through our mobile app or at the customer service desk.\"\n │\n ├── 🔄 同義轉換 (Paraphrase Map)\n │    ├── **Service suspension** ── service interruption = temporary outage\n │    ├── **Technical issue** ── system error = network glitch\n │    ├── **Mechanical problem** ── hardware malfunction = equipment breakdown\n │    ├── **Estimated time** ── expected time of completion = ETA\n │    ├── **Service restoration** ── re-establishing the connection = resuming service\n │    └── **Disruption** ── interruption = interference\n │\n └── ⚠ 高頻防雷陷阱 (Common Traps)\n      └── 1. **At Platform 1** ── 實體改簽地點是在 1 號月台的客服櫃台，不要與 2 號或 3 號月台搞混，常設地點細節干擾！","quiz":[{"q":"In the announcement, the phrase \"service suspension\" is closest in meaning to which of the following?","o":[["A","a permanent cancellation of the route"],["B","a temporary halt of the service"],["C","an upgrade of the equipment"],["D","a reduction in the fare"]],"a":"(B) a temporary halt of the service","zh":"在公告中，「service suspension」與下列何者意思最接近？","e":"同義代換題。suspension 為「暫停」而非「永久取消」；本篇並明言 temporary service suspension due to urgent track maintenance，故選 (B)。"},{"q":"The customer service representative said that the internet service should be restored ________.","o":[["A","within the next hour"],["B","within 24 hours"],["C","by next Tuesday"],["D","after the installation appointment"]],"a":"(A) within the next hour","zh":"客服人員表示網路服務應會在一小時內恢復。","e":"細節時點題。「一小時內恢復服務」與「改約安裝時間為下週二下午 2 點」是兩件事，選項 (C) 即以改約時間作為誘答。"},{"q":"How much is the assessment fee mentioned by the representative?","o":[["A","$15"],["B","$25"],["C","$35"],["D","$50"]],"a":"(B) $25","zh":"客服人員提到的評估費用是多少？","e":"金額題。本篇之 assessment fee 為 $25；請與 6-1 之市區公車票價 $3.50、6-2 之會議室企業價 $450 區隔。"},{"q":"Where should passengers submit their change request forms?","o":[["A","At the ticket machine"],["B","At the customer service counter on Platform 1"],["C","At Platform 2"],["D","Through the mobile application only"]],"a":"(B) At the customer service counter on Platform 1","zh":"乘客應該到哪裡遞交改期申請表？","e":"地點細節題。原文明確為 1 號月台之客服櫃台；月台號碼是本章反覆設陷之處（6-5 之托運櫃台則在 Platform 3）。"},{"q":"Passengers holding valid tickets will receive a full refund only if the request is made ________.","o":[["A","before April 17"],["B","after April 17"],["C","within 75 days"],["D","at the time of travel"]],"a":"(A) before April 17","zh":"持有有效車票的乘客，只有在四月十七日之前提出申請才能獲得全額退款。","e":"條件式退款題。本篇為級距式規定：4/17 前全額退款、之後僅退 75%。看到 full refund 必須同時抓住其時間條件，否則即落入 (B)。"}],"say":["Good morning, I'm calling about my internet service. There's been a service suspension since yesterday afternoon, and I have an important video conference in two hours.","This is really frustrating. I specifically chose your premium plan to avoid these kinds of delays. Can you at least give me an estimated time for service restoration?","According to our system, service should be restored within the next hour. As compensation for this disruption, we'll be applying our refund policy – you'll receive a credit for two days of service. Would you also like to submit a formal complaint to our customer service desk?","Yes, please. And I'll need to reschedule my installation appointment for the new router that was supposed to happen tomorrow. There's also a change request I submitted last week – can you check on that?","Good afternoon, passengers. This is an announcement from the customer service desk at Terminal 3. We regret to inform you that Flight 782 to Singapore has experienced a mechanical problem and will be delayed by approximately three hours.","For passengers who have connecting flights, please approach our service counter immediately to discuss change request options. Our staff will help you reschedule your connections at no additional assessment fee.","Unfortunately, if you choose to cancel your trip entirely, please note that our refund policy requires a 24-hour processing period for full cancellation refunds. Meal vouchers worth $20 will be distributed to all affected passengers as we work to resolve this service suspension.","This delay is due to a technical issue with our booking system that we're currently addressing. We understand this situation is frustrating, and we encourage anyone with concerns to file a complaint through our mobile app or at the customer service desk.","Pacific Railways regrets to announce a temporary service suspension on the North Coast Express line due to urgent track maintenance. A mechanical problem has been detected in our signaling system that requires immediate attention to prevent future technical issues.","Passengers holding tickets for affected services may reschedule their journey at no additional assessment fee. Submit any change request forms at our customer service desk located at Platform 1, or call our hotline.","In accordance with our refund policy, passengers with valid tickets for cancelled services will receive: Full refund if requested before April 17; 75% refund plus a travel voucher if cancelled on April 18. Local shuttle buses will operate every 30 minutes.","Passengers wishing to file a formal complaint regarding this service disruption may do so through our website or by visiting any Pacific Railways station office."]},"6-4":{"tree":"【6-4 旅遊場景-住宿與旅遊體驗 Accommodation & Travel Experience】\n │\n ├── 🔴 S - Situation (情境確認：入住一小時與臨時延長住宿兩晚／情境確認：主樓電梯維修、臨時停用 2 小時／情境確認：一週海灘度假與乾淨住宿)\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **Checked into** (辦理入住), **Extend my reservation** (延長預訂/延住), **Unexpected business meeting** (突發的商務會議), **Out of service** (暫停服務/損壞), **Accommodation** (住宿、住處)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── \"Good morning, welcome to the Grand Vista Hotel. I see you have a reservation with us?\" / \"Yes, I just checked into the hotel an hour ago, but I need to extend my reservation for two more nights. I have an unexpected business meeting on Friday.\" / \"Good afternoon, guests. This is an announcement from the Paradise Resort management. Due to unexpected maintenance work, our main accommodation building's elevators will be temporarily out of service from 3 PM to 5 PM today.\"\n │\n ├── 📋 T - Task (任務說明：查詢可用房型與確認免費早餐／任務說明：客房服務照常、行李搬運實體協助／任務說明：尖峰時段前台延住手續延誤)\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **Complimentary breakfast** (免費早餐), **Room service** (客房服務), **Overwhelmed** (應接不暇、手忙腳亂的)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── \"Let me check our system... We do have rooms available. Would you like to keep the same room with the complimentary breakfast included?\" / \"That would be perfect.\" / \"We apologize for any inconvenience this may cause. During this time, room service will still be available, and our staff will assist any guests who need help with their luggage.\"\n │\n ├── 💡 A - Action (行動方案：諮詢當地觀光與索取導覽小冊／行動方案：補償免費植物園導覽、特色紀念品／行動方案：歷史古蹟免費導覽、特色大廳畫廊)\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **Sightseeing** (觀光、遊覽), **Hotel lobby** (飯店大廳), **Guided tours** (有導覽的行程), **Gift shop** (禮品店), **Hotel lobby doubles as an art gallery** (飯店大廳兼作藝廊)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── \"Also, can you recommend any local attractions for sightseeing tomorrow afternoon? I'll have some free time.\" / \"Certainly! Our hotel lobby has brochures for guided tours of the historic district.\" / \"As an apology, we're offering all affected guests a complimentary guided tour of our botanical gardens at 5:30 PM, which includes a visit to our gift shop where you can purchase unique souvenirs.\"\n │\n ├── ✅ R - Result (結果確認：預告步行導覽終點與禮品店購物／結果確認：夜間 6 點後辦理入住前台領取鑰匙／結果確認：禮品店選購紀念品與深夜入住流程優化)\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **Souvenir** (紀念品), **Late check-in** (深夜入住/晚到辦理入住), **Late check-in after 10 PM** (晚上 10 點後的深夜入住)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── \"The walking tour includes all the major monuments and ends at the souvenir shops on Market Street.\" / \"For those planning late check-in after 6 PM, please stop by the hotel lobby to collect your room keys from the front desk.\" / \"The gift shop offered reasonably priced souvenirs... The only area for improvement would be the late check-in process. Guests arriving after 10 PM must wait longer than expected as there's limited staff available.\"\n │\n ├── 🔄 同義轉換 (Paraphrase Map)\n │    ├── **Extend my reservation** ── prolong my stay = lengthen the booking = keep the room longer\n │    ├── **Complimentary breakfast** ── free morning meal = breakfast included at no extra cost\n │    ├── **Sightseeing** ── visiting local attractions = exploring historical sites\n │    ├── **Guided tours** ── conducted sightseeing = escorted excursions\n │    ├── **Souvenir** ── keepsakes = mementos = gifts from gift shop\n │    └── **Out of service** ── broken = out of order = temporarily unavailable\n │\n └── ⚠ 高頻防雷陷阱 (Common Traps)\n      └── 1. **Out of service** ── 維修持續時間：從下午 3 點到 5 點，共計 2 小時（two hours）。不要與航班延誤時間混淆！","quiz":[{"q":"Why does the guest need to extend the reservation?","o":[["A","Because his flight was cancelled"],["B","Because of an unexpected business meeting on Friday"],["C","Because the room was not ready"],["D","Because he wants to join the guided tour"]],"a":"(B) Because of an unexpected business meeting on Friday","zh":"這位房客為什麼需要延長住宿？","e":"原因題。對話中為「週五臨時有商務會議」；閱讀文章中的評論者則是因「班機異動」而延住一天，兩者原因不同，不可互換。"},{"q":"In the passage, the word \"complimentary\" is closest in meaning to which of the following?","o":[["A","free of charge"],["B","highly praised"],["C","additional but chargeable"],["D","optional and refundable"]],"a":"(A) free of charge","zh":"在本文中，「complimentary」與下列何者意思最接近？","e":"字義陷阱題。complimentary（免費招待）與 complementary（互補的）拼字極近；本篇之 complimentary breakfast、complimentary guided tour 均指免費提供。"},{"q":"The maintenance work at the resort will last for approximately ________.","o":[["A","one hour"],["B","two hours"],["C","three hours"],["D","the whole afternoon"]],"a":"(B) two hours","zh":"渡假村的維修工程大約會持續兩個小時。","e":"時間計算題。公告為「下午 3 點至 5 點」，需自行相減得出 two hours；此類「給時段、問時長」是多益 Part 4 的固定考法。"},{"q":"What is offered to the affected guests as an apology?","o":[["A","A full refund of the room rate"],["B","A complimentary guided tour of the botanical gardens"],["C","A free upgrade to a suite"],["D","A voucher for the gift shop"]],"a":"(B) A complimentary guided tour of the botanical gardens","zh":"渡假村提供什麼給受影響的房客作為賠罪？","e":"補償內容題。原文為「下午 5 點 30 分的免費植物園導覽，並包含參觀禮品店」；(D) 以文中確有提及之 gift shop 作為誘答，但禮品店只是導覽行程的一站，並非另行贈券。"},{"q":"Guests planning a late check-in after 6 PM should ________.","o":[["A","call the front desk in advance"],["B","stop by the hotel lobby to collect their room keys"],["C","use the self-service kiosk at the entrance"],["D","wait for a staff member at the room door"]],"a":"(B) stop by the hotel lobby to collect their room keys","zh":"計畫在下午六點後晚到登記入住的房客應該到飯店大廳領取房卡。","e":"指示動作題。注意本單元有兩個 late check-in 時間：公告為 after 6 PM 到大廳領鑰匙，評論則提到 after 10 PM 另有程序，題目問公告即選 (B)。"}],"say":["Good morning, welcome to the Grand Vista Hotel. I see you have a reservation with us?","Let me check our system... We do have rooms available. Would you like to keep the same room with the complimentary breakfast included?","Also, can you recommend any local attractions for sightseeing tomorrow afternoon? I'll have some free time.","The walking tour includes all the major monuments and ends at the souvenir shops on Market Street.","Good afternoon, guests. This is an announcement from the Paradise Resort management. Due to unexpected maintenance work, our main accommodation building's elevators will be temporarily out of service from 3 PM to 5 PM today.","We apologize for any inconvenience this may cause. During this time, room service will still be available, and our staff will assist any guests who need help with their luggage.","As an apology, we're offering all affected guests a complimentary guided tour of our botanical gardens at 5:30 PM, which includes a visit to our gift shop where you can purchase unique souvenirs.","For those planning late check-in after 6 PM, please stop by the hotel lobby to collect your room keys from the front desk.","I recently stayed at the Sunset Beach Resort for a week-long vacation, and overall, it was a wonderful experience. The accommodation was clean and spacious. The beachfront location made sightseeing effortless.","The complimentary breakfast was exceptional. However, I was disappointed to learn that I needed to extend my reservation by one day due to a flight change, and the front desk staff seemed overwhelmed during peak hours.","Despite this minor issue, the guided tour of the nearby historical sites was expertly conducted. One highlight was the hotel lobby, which doubles as an art gallery.","The gift shop offered reasonably priced souvenirs... The only area for improvement would be the late check-in process. Guests arriving after 10 PM must wait longer than expected as there's limited staff available."]},"6-5":{"tree":"【6-5 旅遊資訊與公告：機場與交通場景應對策略 Travel Information & Announcements】\n │\n ├── 🔴 S - Situation (情境確認：登機門變更與登機證核對／情境確認：航班起飛安全提示與氣流波動／情境確認：新行李政策與頭頂置物架限制)\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **Departure board** (出發航班看板), **Boarding pass** (登機證), **Safety procedures** (安全程序), **Overhead compartment** (頭頂上方行李置物箱), **Platform counter** (月台櫃台)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── \"Excuse me, I'm looking for Gate B23 for my flight to Singapore. The departure board shows it's been changed, but I can't see the new gate number.\" / \"Let me check for you. What's your flight number? W: It's Pacific Airways 512. My boarding pass still shows the old gate.\" / \"Attention, passengers on Flight 206 to Vancouver. We'd like to inform you about some important safety procedures before we depart. Please ensure your seatbelts are fastened and review the safety card in your seat pocket.\"\n │\n ├── 📋 T - Task (任務說明：告知航廈轉乘 C15 登機門與登機手續／任務說明：安全期間保持就座、電子設備飛航模式／任務說明：登機手續流程更新：45分鐘前出示登)\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **Gate C15** (C15 登機門), **Shuttle train** (機場捷運/接駁電車), **Turbulence** (亂流、氣流顛簸), **Boarding pass** (登機證), **15 minutes before departure** (起飛前 15 分鐘)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── \"I see. Your flight has been moved to Terminal 2, Gate C15. You'll need to take the shuttle train from here.\" / \"Due to weather conditions at our destination, we're expecting some turbulence during the flight. The captain has requested that all passengers remain seated... Please note that once you're seated on the plane, you must keep your electronic devices in airplane mode.\" / \"Updated Boarding Process: Starting next month, all passengers must present their boarding pass at least 45 minutes before departure. The final boarding call will now occur 15 minutes before scheduled departure time. Passengers are permitted to board only after their zone number is called.\"\n │\n ├── 💡 A - Action (行動方案：提醒手提行李箱置物限制與櫃台托運／行動方案：即時路線更新與航班狀態延遲 20 分鐘／行動方案：數位加強服務：即時路線更新與狀態簡訊)\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **Luggage restrictions** (行李限制), **Overhead compartment** (頭頂上方置物箱), **Counter near Platform 3** (Platform 3 旁邊的櫃台), **Flight status** (航班狀態), **Live route updates** (即時航線更新)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── \"Also, please note there are new luggage restrictions - only one carry-on bag is allowed in the overhead compartment.\" / \"Oh, I didn't know about that. I have two bags with me.\" / \"You can check one at the counter near Platform 3.\"\n │\n ├── ✅ R - Result (結果確認：發出最後登機廣播與開始登機／結果確認：降落後至第 1 航廈提領行李／結果確認：行李提領區擴建、20分鐘內送達)\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **Final boarding call** (最後登機廣播), **Permitted to board** (允許登機), **Baggage claim area** (行李提領區), **Arrive within 20 minutes** (20 分鐘之內送達)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── \"Just be quick - they've already made the final boarding call for your flight. Passengers are now permitted to board.\" / \"When we land, please proceed to the baggage claim area in Terminal 1. Thank you for your cooperation.\" / \"Baggage Claim Improvements: We have expanded our baggage claim area to reduce waiting times. Luggage from international flights will now arrive within 20 minutes of landing. Please review all safety procedures before your flight.\"\n │\n ├── 🔄 同義轉換 (Paraphrase Map)\n │    ├── **Departure board** ── digital display screen = flight information monitor\n │    ├── **Luggage restrictions** ── carry-on limits = baggage size and quantity regulations\n │    ├── **Final boarding call** ── last call for boarding = boarding closing soon\n │    ├── **Permitted to board** ── allowed to get on the plane = boarding process active\n │    ├── **Safety procedures** ── emergency protocols = seatbelt instructions\n │    └── **Live route updates** ── real-time flight tracking = route details on screen\n │\n └── ⚠ 高頻防雷陷阱 (Common Traps)\n      ├── 1. **Gate C15** ── 新登機門為 C15，位於第 2 航廈（Terminal 2）➔ 不要誤選原本的 B23 登機門！\n      ├── 2. **Counter near Platform 3** ── 托運行李的地點在 Platform 3 櫃台 ➔ 絕對不是門禁處（security desk）或登機門！\n      ├── 3. **Baggage claim area** ── 航廈區分：降落提領行李是在 Terminal 1 ➔ 與對話中新變更的 C15 登機門（Terminal 2）屬於不同航廈，注意數字細節！\n      └── 4. **15 minutes before departure** ── 最後登機廣播時間由 30 分鐘前縮短至 15 分鐘前（15 minutes before departure）。","quiz":[{"q":"The passenger's flight has been moved to Gate ________.","o":[["A","B23"],["B","B12"],["C","C15"],["D","C23"]],"a":"(C) C15","zh":"這位乘客的班機已改到 C15 登機門。","e":"登機門變更題。原登機門為 B23，新登機門為 Terminal 2 的 C15；(A) 即以登機證上的舊登機門作為誘答，(B) 則來自 6-2 單元。"},{"q":"Where can the passenger check the extra bag?","o":[["A","At the security desk"],["B","At the boarding gate"],["C","At the counter near Platform 3"],["D","At the baggage claim area"]],"a":"(C) At the counter near Platform 3","zh":"這位乘客可以在哪裡託運多出來的行李？","e":"地點細節題。原文明確為 Platform 3 附近的櫃台；安檢處與登機門均為干擾選項，(D) 之行李提領區則是「抵達後」才使用的區域。"},{"q":"According to the new policy, each passenger is permitted ________ in the overhead compartment.","o":[["A","one carry-on bag"],["B","two carry-on bags"],["C","one checked bag"],["D","unlimited hand luggage"]],"a":"(A) one carry-on bag","zh":"依照新政策，每位乘客在頭頂置物櫃只被允許放置一件隨身行李。","e":"數量限制題。對話中乘客帶了兩件行李而超出規定，正是本題之情境來源；請注意 carry-on（隨身）與 checked（託運）之區別。"},{"q":"Under the updated boarding process, the final boarding call will be made ________ before departure.","o":[["A","45 minutes"],["B","30 minutes"],["C","20 minutes"],["D","15 minutes"]],"a":"(D) 15 minutes","zh":"依照更新後的登機流程，最後登機廣播將於起飛前十五分鐘進行。","e":"新舊制對比題。本篇有三個時間：登機證須於起飛前 45 分鐘出示、最後登機廣播由原本的 30 分鐘前縮短為 15 分鐘前。題目問「最後登機廣播」，應選 (D)，(B) 即為舊制誘答。"},{"q":"Upon landing, passengers should proceed to the baggage claim area in ________.","o":[["A","Terminal 1"],["B","Terminal 2"],["C","Terminal 3"],["D","the arrival lounge"]],"a":"(A) Terminal 1","zh":"降落後，乘客應前往第一航廈的行李提領區。","e":"航廈區分題。本單元同時出現 Terminal 2（新登機門 C15 所在）與 Terminal 1（行李提領區）；(C) 之 Terminal 3 則來自 6-3 之客服櫃台，屬跨單元干擾。"}],"say":["Excuse me, I'm looking for Gate B23 for my flight to Singapore. The departure board shows it's been changed, but I can't see the new gate number.","I see. Your flight has been moved to Terminal 2, Gate C15. You'll need to take the shuttle train from here.","Also, please note there are new luggage restrictions - only one carry-on bag is allowed in the overhead compartment.","Just be quick - they've already made the final boarding call for your flight. Passengers are now permitted to board.","Attention, passengers on Flight 206 to Vancouver. We'd like to inform you about some important safety procedures before we depart. Please ensure your seatbelts are fastened and review the safety card in your seat pocket.","Due to weather conditions at our destination, we're expecting some turbulence during the flight. The captain has requested that all passengers remain seated... Please note that once you're seated on the plane, you must keep your electronic devices in airplane mode.","Our flight status has been updated, and we now expect to arrive 20 minutes later than scheduled. You can check live route updates on the screen in front of you throughout the flight.","When we land, please proceed to the baggage claim area in Terminal 1. Thank you for your cooperation.","Skyway Airlines will be implementing new policies regarding carry-on luggage and boarding procedures. Each passenger is permitted one carry-on bag (maximum 7kg) for the overhead compartment. Any additional bags must be checked at the platform counter before proceeding to your gate. Oversized items will incur a fee of $75.","Updated Boarding Process: Starting next month, all passengers must present their boarding pass at least 45 minutes before departure. The final boarding call will now occur 15 minutes before scheduled departure time. Passengers are permitted to board only after their zone number is called.","Enhanced Services: Live route updates are now available through our mobile app; Flight status notifications will be sent via SMS to all registered passengers; Digital departure boards have been installed throughout the terminal.","Baggage Claim Improvements: We have expanded our baggage claim area to reduce waiting times. Luggage from international flights will now arrive within 20 minutes of landing. Please review all safety procedures before your flight."]},"8-1":{"tree":"【Ch8-1 檔案歸檔與報銷流程 Document Filing & Reimbursement】\n │\n ├── 🔴 S - Situation (情境確認：了解分類與專案時程)\n │    ├── 歸檔分類 ── 外部信件用藍色資料夾 (blue) vs 內部專案文件用綠色 (green)\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **filing system** (歸檔系統), **correspondence** (往來信件), **deadline** (截止日)\n │    └── ⚠ 專案截止 ── Johnson 專案截止日期為下週一 (next Monday)\n │\n ├── 📋 T - Task (任務說明：詢問報銷報告之審核狀態)\n │    ├── 查詢項目 ── 費用報銷報告 (expense report) 之審批狀態\n │    └── 核心字彙 ── **expense report** (費用報告), **approved** (批准)\n │\n ├── 💡 A - Action (行動方案：核對入帳時間與報銷工作天)\n │    ├── 撥款天數 ── 昨天處理完畢 (processed yesterday) ➔ 5-7 個工作日 (business days) 內入帳\n │    ├── 報銷變革 ── 線上系統提交取代紙本表格，保留原始發票 (original invoices) \n │    └── ⚠ 加總地雷 ── 3-5天審批 + 5-7天撥款 = 實際取得款項需 8-12 個工作日\n │\n └── ✅ R - Result (結果確認：特定專案報銷條件與HR求職窗口)\n      ├── 限制條件 ── 專案相關費用必須先提交「交付成果 (deliverables)」才可申請報銷\n      ├── 實施效益 ── 檔案數位化，處理時間從 10-12 天縮短至 5-7 天 (省下大約5天)\n      └── 求助管道 ── 實體諮詢前往「三樓人力資源部 (third floor HR)」，下週舉辦培訓","quiz":[{"q":"Under the new administrative guidelines, all _______ correspondence must be organized in blue folders, while internal documents go in green ones.","o":[["A","confidential"],["B","temporary"],["C","external"],["D","financial"]],"a":"(C) external","zh":"根據新行政指南，所有**外部**往來信件必須整理在藍色資料夾中，而內部文件則放入綠色資料夾中。","e":"對照 Part 3 對白：「All external correspondence goes in the blue folders. Internal project documents go in green ones.」，因此應選 (C) external。"},{"q":"Please be reminded that the project deadline for the Johnson account has been scheduled for ________.","o":[["A","this Friday"],["B","next Monday"],["C","tomorrow morning"],["D","next Wednesday"]],"a":"(B) next Monday","zh":"請注意，Johnson 專案的截止日期已被排定在**下週一**。","e":"對話明確指出「the project deadline for Johnson is next Monday.」，故選 (B)。(A) 為多益常設的干擾選項。"},{"q":"To receive reimbursement for project-related expenses, employees must first submit all necessary ________ to the system.","o":[["A","credentials"],["B","deliverables"],["C","applications"],["D","categories"]],"a":"(B) deliverables","zh":"若要獲得專案相關費用的報銷，員工必須首先將所有必要的**交付成果**提交至系統中。","e":"對照 Part 4 獨白：「For project-related expenses, remember that all deliverables must be submitted before filing for reimbursement.」，因此選擇 (B) deliverables（交付成果）。"},{"q":"According to the document management memo, the new digital filing system will be implemented on ________.","o":[["A","March 15"],["B","next Monday"],["C","April 1"],["D","May 10"]],"a":"(C) April 1","zh":"根據文件管理備忘錄，新數位歸檔系統將於**4 月 1 日**實施。","e":"備忘錄日期為 March 15 (發文日)，但系統實施生效日為「starting April 1」，因此正確答案為 (C)。"},{"q":"By transitioning to digital submissions, the company expects to reduce the expense report processing time by ________.","o":[["A","3 to 5 days"],["B","5 to 7 days"],["C","approximately 5 days"],["D","10 to 12 days"]],"a":"(C) approximately 5 days","zh":"藉由過渡到數位提交，公司預計能將費用報告處理時間縮短**大約 5 天**。","e":"此題考查「數據對比與計算」。舊制需要 10-12 個工作日，新制縮短至 5-7 個工作日。10天減5天=5天；12天減7天=5天。因此，處理時間縮短了「大約 5 天」，故選 (C)。"}],"say":["Hi Tom, did you receive the memo about the new filing system?","Thanks. By the way, has my expense report been approved?","Let me check... Yes, it was processed yesterday. The reimbursement should appear within 5-7 business days.","Certainly. Your order has been processed, and I'll send you all the details within the hour. The tracking number is TRK-45892.","Good morning, everyone. This is a notification from HR regarding our new reimbursement process. Starting next month, all expense reports must be submitted through our online system instead of paper forms.","Please keep all original invoices and receipts - these must be attached to your digital submissions.","The new timeline for processing is 3-5 business days for approval, then another 5-7 business days for the reimbursement to reach your account.","For project-related expenses, remember that all deliverables must be submitted before filing for reimbursement. If you need help with the new filing system or organizing your paperwork, please email me or visit HR on the third floor.","We are implementing a new digital filing system starting April 1 to address delays in processing paperwork.","All correspondence, including internal memos and emails, must be uploaded to appropriate folders in our cloud system."]},"8-2":{"tree":"【Ch8-2 會議室預訂與跨部門協調 Conference Room Booking & Coordination】\n │\n ├── 🔴 S - Situation (情境確認：大會議室衝突與替代方案)\n │    ├── 預訂衝突 ── 週四跨部門會議與董事會會議 (board meeting) 整天衝突 ➔ 大會議室已被佔用 (taken)\n │    ├── 替代方案 ── 改訂「五樓小會議室 (fifth floor)」，可用時間段為「下午 2 點至 4 點」\n │    └── 臨時變更 ── 董事會會議因日程衝突，改至「二樓 A 會議室 (second floor Room A)」，9 AM 準時開始\n │\n ├── 📋 T - Task (任務說明：確保跨部門溝通順暢，指派紀錄)\n │    ├── 討論主旨 ── 新的合作專案 (collaboration project) ➔ 改善跨部門協調與配合\n │    └── 會議要求 ── 部門主管強制出席，且必須指派專人記錄「會議紀錄 (take minutes/notes)」\n │\n ├── 💡 A - Action (行動方案：天數限制規則與資料核對)\n │    ├── 預訂天數 ── 一般會議室 ➔ 提前 48 小時預訂；董事會或有「特殊設備」簡報 ➔ 強制提前一週 (7天) 預訂\n │    ├── 標準規範 ── 會議通知一律隨附議程 (agenda)，且會議結束後 24 小時內必須上傳會議紀錄至共享雲端\n │    └── 財務資料 ── 領取財務預估單 (financial projections)，必須去「會計部 (accounting)」找「珍妮特 (Janet)」\n │\n └── ✅ R - Result (結果確認：緊急狀況求助管道)\n      ├── 緊急求助 ── 遇到「緊急預訂 (urgent bookings)」或有程序疑問，一律聯繫「行政團隊 (administrative team)」\n      └── 後續公告 ── 下週將於布告欄 (bulletin) 張貼詳細指令，此通報 (circular) 須全員傳閱","quiz":[{"q":"The interdepartmental meeting scheduled for Thursday had to be moved to the smaller conference room because the large boardroom was _______ all day by the board of directors.","o":[["A","decorated"],["B","renovated"],["C","occupied"],["D","canceled"]],"a":"(C) occupied","zh":"排定於週四的跨部門會議必須移至較小的會議室，因為大會議室整天都被董事會**佔用**。","e":"對照 Part 3 對白：「Sorry, it's taken. There's a board meeting scheduled there all day.」中 taken 的同義代換即為 occupied（被佔用的），故選 (C)。"},{"q":"According to the administrative broadcast, tomorrow's board meeting will take place in ________.","o":[["A","the main boardroom on the third floor"],["B","Conference Room A on the second floor"],["C","the fifth-floor small meeting room"],["D","Janet's office in the accounting department"]],"a":"(B) Conference Room A on the second floor","zh":"根據行政廣播，明天的董事會會議將在**二樓的 A 會議室**舉行。","e":"此為新舊地點干擾題。廣播提到：「The meeting will now be held in Conference Room A on the second floor, not in the main boardroom as originally planned.」因此選 (B)。(A) 為原定計劃，(C) 為 Sandra 預訂的跨部門會議室，皆屬干擾。"},{"q":"If a department head needs to book a presentation room that requires a smart projector and audio system, they must submit the request ________.","o":[["A","at least 48 hours in advance"],["B","no later than tomorrow noon"],["C","at least one week in advance"],["D","within 24 hours after the event"]],"a":"(C) at least one week in advance","zh":"如果部門主管需要預訂一間需要智慧投影機與音響系統的簡報室，他們必須**至少提前一週**提交申請。","e":"此題為預訂天數配對地雷。備忘錄指出：「For board meetings and presentations requiring special equipment, please submit requests one week ahead.」投影機與音響屬於特殊設備（special equipment），故適用「提前一週」條款，選 (C)。一般會議才是 (A)。"},{"q":"Under the new meeting procedures, designated staff must upload the completed meeting minutes to the shared drive within ________.","o":[["A","12 hours"],["B","24 hours"],["C","two business days"],["D","one week"]],"a":"(B) 24 hours","zh":"根據新會議程序，指派的人員必須在**24 小時**內將完成的會議紀錄上傳至共享雲端硬碟。","e":"備忘錄明文規定：「Minutes from all meetings should be uploaded to the shared drive within 24 hours.」，故 (B) 為唯一正確選項。"},{"q":"Who should employees contact if they need to arrange an urgent conference room booking or have questions about the new circular?","o":[["A","Michael Chen"],["B","Janet in accounting"],["C","The administrative team"],["D","Sarah Martinez"]],"a":"(C) The administrative team","zh":"如果員工需要安排緊急會議室預訂，或對新通報有任何疑問，他們應該聯絡誰？","e":"對照 Part 7 閱讀最後一句：「For urgent bookings or questions about the new procedures, contact the administrative team.」因此選 (C)。Michael Chen 是發文者，Janet 負責分發財務 projections，皆非解答緊急預訂的人選。"}],"say":["Hi Sandra, I need to book a conference room for Thursday's interdepartmental meeting. Is the large one available?","That should work. We're discussing the new collaboration project, so we'll need good coordination between departments. Can you help me send an internal memo to all team leaders?","Sure, I'll draft it now. What should be on the agenda?","Good afternoon. This is an announcement regarding tomorrow's board meeting. Due to scheduling conflicts, we've had to change the conference room booking. The meeting will now be held in Conference Room A on the second floor, not in the main boardroom as originally planned.","Please note that we'll be discussing interdepartmental coordination for the upcoming merger. All department heads must attend, and we'll need someone to take detailed minutes.","The meeting will still start at 9 AM sharp. Please review the briefing materials beforehand, especially the sections on collaboration strategies. If you haven't received the circular with the financial projections, please see Janet in accounting. Thank you.","Dear Team, Effective May 1, we're implementing new procedures for booking conference rooms and coordinating meetings to improve interdepartmental collaboration.","All conference room bookings must now be made through the online system at least 48 hours in advance. For board meetings and presentations requiring special equipment, please submit requests one week ahead.","We're also standardizing our internal communication. All meeting announcements should be distributed via internal memo, with the agenda attached. Department heads must ensure proper coordination when scheduling interdepartmental meetings to avoid conflicts. Minutes from all meetings should be uploaded to the shared drive within 24 hours.","A bulletin will be posted next week with detailed instructions. For urgent bookings or questions about the new procedures, contact the administrative team. This circular should be shared with all team members. Best regards, Michael Chen"]},"8-3":{"tree":"【Ch8-3 設備維護與辦公設施 Equipment Maintenance & Facilities】\n │\n ├── 🔴 S - Situation (情境確認：卡紙故障、連線中斷與冷氣修復)\n │    ├── 影印卡紙 ── 本層影印機卡紙 (jammed) ➔ 備用設備位於「二樓檔案櫃旁」，但面臨「網路問題」\n │    ├── 定期維護 ── 上一次 IT 設備全面檢查是在「上個月 (last month)」\n │    └── 冷氣完工 ── 會議室冷氣安裝「終於完成 (finally complete)」；設施部「主辦公室冷氣維修」亦已完工\n │\n ├── 📋 T - Task (任務說明：電腦升級停機、按月提交維護、簽收鑰匙)\n │    ├── 升級工程 ── 週一起升級「三樓電腦及工作站」，工程需「三天」➔ 期間三樓印表與影印機「無法使用 (unavailable)」\n │    ├── 定期申報 ── 所有部門即日起必須「按月提交維護申請 (monthly requests)」\n │    └── 鑰匙簽收 ── 檔案櫃鑰匙因鎖死問題，新鑰匙週五前到貨，下週一律前往「前台/接待處 (reception)」親自簽收\n │\n ├── 💡 A - Action (行動方案：每週預防性檢查、引進工單系統、新大樓施工)\n │    ├── 預防措施 ── IT 支援將進行「每週檢查 (weekly checks)」以防網路連線中斷 (connectivity issues)\n │    ├── 報修規則 ── 設備故障「不准直接打電話 (calling directly)」，必須透過「線上系統提交工單 (submit a ticket)」\n │    └── 擴建大樓 ── 新翼大樓 (new wing) 冷氣安裝排定於「6 月 1 日 (June 1)」正式展開\n │\n └── ✅ R - Result (結果確認：溫度預警與關機規定)\n      ├── 施工預警 ── 冷氣施工期間部分辦公區會出現「溫度波動 (temperature fluctuations)」，總務先行致歉\n      └── 保養規範 ── 為「延長設備壽命 (extend lifespan)」，下班前全體員工必須配合「妥善關機 (proper shut down)」","quiz":[{"q":"When a computer at a workstation fails to connect to the network, the user should submit a service ticket online instead of ________.","o":[["A","checking the blueprint"],["B","calling IT directly"],["C","notifying Janet in accounting"],["D","waiting until next month"]],"a":"(B) calling IT directly","zh":"當工作站的電腦無法連線到網路時，使用者應該在線上提交服務工單，而不是**直接打電話給 IT**。","e":"對照 Part 7 閱讀：「submit a ticket through the online system rather than calling directly.」因此選 (B)。其他選項如 (A) 查藍圖、(C) 聯絡 Janet 均無關。"},{"q":"The facilities department announced that the office computers on the third floor will be upgraded starting Monday, and the project will take ________.","o":[["A","exactly 24 hours"],["B","approximately three days"],["C","no more than one week"],["D","until Friday afternoon"]],"a":"(B) approximately three days","zh":"設施管理部門宣布，三樓的辦公電腦將自週一開始升級，該專案將耗時**大約三天**。","e":"對照 Part 4 獨白：「Starting Monday, we'll be upgrading all computers and workstations on the third floor. The installation will take approximately three days.」故正確答案為 (B)。"},{"q":"Where should employees go next week to sign for and collect the redistributed filing cabinet keys?","o":[["A","The security desk at the main entrance"],["B","The administrative manager's office"],["C","The reception desk"],["D","The IT support office on the third floor"]],"a":"(C) The reception desk","zh":"員工下週應該去哪裡簽名並領取重新分配的檔案櫃鑰匙？","e":"對照 Part 7 閱讀：「The filing cabinet keys will be redistributed next week - please see reception to sign for your new keys.」reception 對應的就是前台/接待處，故選 (C)。"},{"q":"Due to the upcoming air-conditioning installation for the new wing on June 1, employees should be prepared for temporary ________ in the office temperature.","o":[["A","cancellations"],["B","fluctuations"],["C","restorations"],["D","evaluations"]],"a":"(B) fluctuations","zh":"由於即將於 6 月 1 日在新建大樓展開冷氣安裝，員工應為辦公室溫度的暫時**波動**做好準備。","e":"對照 Part 7 閱讀：「During installation, some areas may experience temperature fluctuations.」因此應選名詞 (B) fluctuations（波動、起伏）。"},{"q":"In the equipment updates circular, the phrase \"extend its lifespan\" is closest in meaning to ________.","o":[["A","improve the efficiency of printing"],["B","increase the daily output of computers"],["C","prolong the useful life of the hardware"],["D","submit requests within 24 hours"]],"a":"(C) prolong the useful life of the hardware","zh":"在設備更新通報中，短語 \"extend its lifespan\" 與下列何者意思最接近？","e":"字彙代換考點。extend 代換為 prolong（延長），lifespan 代換為 useful life（使用壽命），equipment 代換為 hardware。故 (C) 爲最完美、最高質量的同義代換選項。"}],"say":["Excuse me, Lisa. The photocopier on our floor is jammed again, and I need to make copies for the meeting.","That's frustrating. We really need better maintenance for our equipment. When was the last time IT support checked everything?","Oh, by the way, the air-conditioning installation in the conference room is finally complete. At least that's working now.","Attention all staff. This is a reminder from the facilities department about our equipment maintenance schedule. Starting Monday, we'll be upgrading all computers and workstations on the third floor. The installation will take approximately three days.","During this time, the printer and photocopier on that floor will be unavailable. Please use the equipment on other floors. If you experience any network problems during the upgrade, contact IT support immediately.","Also, we've received several reports about the filing cabinets in the storage room being locked without keys available. New keys have been ordered and should arrive by Friday.","Finally, the air-conditioning repair in the main office has been completed, so the temperature should be more comfortable now.","Due to increasing network problems and equipment failures, we're implementing a comprehensive maintenance program for all office equipment.","Effective immediately, all departments must submit monthly maintenance requests for their equipment. This includes printers, photocopiers, scanners, and computers. The filing cabinet keys will be redistributed next week - please see reception to sign for your new keys.","The IT support team will conduct weekly checks of all workstations to prevent connectivity issues. If your computer or other equipment needs immediate repair, submit a ticket through the online system rather than calling directly. Additionally, the air-conditioning installation for the new wing will begin June 1."]},"8-4":{"tree":"【Ch8-4 安全協定與訪客管理 Security Protocols & Visitor Management】\n │\n ├── 🔴 S - Situation (情境確認：訪客報到與佩戴證件位置)\n │    ├── 訪客會議 ── 上午 10 點與強森先生 (Mr. Johnson) 會議 ➔ 前往主入口旁「安全櫃台 (security desk)」登記簽到\n │    └── 佩戴位置 ── 自即日起全員強制佩戴識別證，位置必須在「腰部以上 (above the waist) 且正面朝前」\n │\n ├── 📋 T - Task (任務說明：遺失申報、補發天數與訪客強制手續)\n │    ├── 識別證損毀 ── 遺失或損壞必須「立即 (immediately)」通報，新卡將在「24 小時內」核發，急用可領「臨時卡」\n │    └── 訪客強制 ── 所有來賓（含快遞/貨運司機）皆須「強制登記 (mandatory)」，員工必須「全程陪同 (at all times)」\n │\n ├── 💡 A - Action (行動方案：快遞存放地點大更換與收發時段)\n │    ├── 實體地點 ── 包裹存放地點從 舊制前台 (reception) ➔ 變更為「收發室 (mail room)」存放\n │    ├── 快遞合夥 ── 獨白合作快遞為 QuickShip (11 AM & 3 PM 收件) vs 閱讀合夥快遞為 Global Express\n │    └── 領取期限 ── 訪客證 (visitor pass) 效期「僅限簽發當天 (valid only for date issued)」，離開時必須交還保全櫃台\n │\n └── ✅ R - Result (結果確認：包裹發放政策與私件禁止)\n      ├── 配送時效 ── 中午 (noon) 前送達之包裹，一律於 下午 2 點前 發放完畢；緊急件前台將立即通知\n      ├── 嚴格禁令 ── 「嚴格禁止個人私件 (personal packages)」寄送到公司，有安全疑問撥打「分機 100」\n      └── 緊急物流 ── 遇上緊急快遞，主動向「保全警衛 (security guard)」說明，以利調度引導","quiz":[{"q":"According to the building safety guidelines, all employees must display their ID badges prominently ________.","o":[["A","inside their wallets"],["B","above the waist and facing forward"],["C","on their carry-on luggage"],["D","only when leaving the premises"]],"a":"(B) above the waist and facing forward","zh":"根據大樓安全指南，所有員工必須將其識別證醒目地展示在**腰部以上且正面朝前**。","e":"對照 Part 7 閱讀原文：「All employees must display their ID badges above the waist and facing forward.」此為標準的細節配對題，故選 (B)。"},{"q":"If an employee accidentally loses their security badge, a replacement one will be issued by the security desk ________.","o":[["A","within 24 hours"],["B","on the following Monday"],["C","within 3 to 5 business days"],["D","after April 1st"]],"a":"(A) within 24 hours","zh":"如果員工不慎遺失安全識別證，安全櫃台將於**24 小時內**核發替代用新證。","e":"對照 Part 7 閱讀：「Replacement badges will be issued within 24 hours.」故選 (A)。(C) 是報銷審核的時間，屬於跨區干擾。"},{"q":"Under the updated shipping rules, employee packages must now be dropped off at ________ instead of the reception desk.","o":[["A","the main entrance security desk"],["B","the mail room"],["C","HR on the third floor"],["D","Conference Room A"]],"a":"(B) the mail room","zh":"根據更新後的遞送規定，員工包裹現在必須放在**收發室**，而不是前台接待處。","e":"此為高頻地點變更地雷題。獨白指出：「All packages should now be dropped off at the mail room instead of reception.」因此 (B) mail room（收發室）為唯一正確選項。"},{"q":"Which of the following statement is true regarding the building's visitor management policy?","o":[["A","Visitors are permitted to walk to Mr. Johnson's office unescorted."],["B","Delivery personnel are exempt from guest registration."],["C","Visitor passes remain valid for an entire week."],["D","Hosting employees must accompany their guests at all times."]],"a":"(D) Hosting employees must accompany their guests at all times.","zh":"關於大樓的訪客管理政策，下列哪一項敘述是正確的？","e":"選項 (A) 與「必須全程陪同」衝突；選項 (B) 錯誤，快遞送貨員也強制登記（mandatory for everyone, including delivery personnel）；選項 (C) 錯誤，訪客證僅當天有效（valid only for the date issued）。故只有 (D) 「接待員工必須全程陪同訪客」完全正確。"},{"q":"If a commercial package from Global Express arrives at the building at 11:30 AM, when can the recipient expect it to be distributed?","o":[["A","Within 24 hours of arrival"],["B","By 2 PM the same day"],["C","Punctually at 3 PM"],["D","Before noon the following business day"]],"a":"(B) By 2 PM the same day","zh":"如果一件來自 Global Express 的商務包裹於上午 11:30 送達大樓，收件人預計何時能拿到發放的包裹？","e":"此題考查「時間運算與截止條件」。包裹於 11:30 AM 送達，符合「中午前送達（arriving before noon）」的條件。根據閱讀指南：「Packages arriving before noon will be distributed by 2 PM.」因此，該包裹將在「當天下午 2 點前」發放，正確答案為 (B)。"}],"say":["Excuse me, I'm here for a 10 AM meeting with Mr. Johnson. Where can I get a visitor pass?","Thank you. Also, I have a package that needs to be sent urgently. Do you have a courier service?","Perfect. One more thing - I left my ID badge at home. Will that be a problem?","Good morning, everyone. This is an important announcement about our new security protocol. Starting next Monday, all employees must wear their ID badges visibly at all times. The security desk will no longer allow entry without proper identification.","For those expecting visitors, please notify reception in advance with the visitor's name and arrival time. All visitors must register at the security desk and receive a visitor pass before entering the building. Guest registration is now mandatory for everyone, including delivery personnel.","Also, we've changed our courier service provider to QuickShip. All packages should now be dropped off at the mail room instead of reception. The courier service will make pickups at 11 AM and 3 PM daily.","If you're expecting an urgent delivery, please inform the security guard so they can direct the courier properly.","Effective immediately, we are implementing enhanced security measures throughout the building. ID Badge Requirements: All employees must display their ID badges above the waist and facing forward.","Lost or damaged badges must be reported to the security desk immediately. Replacement badges will be issued within 24 hours. Temporary access cards are available at the security desk for emergency situations.","Visitor Management: All visitors require a visitor pass, which must be obtained from reception after signing in. Visitor passes are valid only for the date issued and must be returned to the security desk upon departure. Employees hosting visitors are responsible for escorting them at all times."]},"8-5":{"tree":"【Ch8-5 辦公室搬遷與系統升級 Office Relocation & System Upgrade】\n │\n ├── 🔴 S - Situation (情境確認：大樓搬遷時程與電梯故障現狀)\n │    ├── 搬遷日期 ── 辦公室搬遷確認於「8 月 20 日 (August 20)」進行，地點為港口街 450 號 (450 Harbor Street)\n │    ├── 機械故障 ── 當前大樓電梯今天又停用 (out of service)；廣播宣布「西翼電梯故障將持續到週三」\n │    └── 垂直替代 ── 在西翼修復前，員工必須搭乘「東翼電梯」或「走樓梯」\n │\n ├── 📋 T - Task (任務說明：關閉時程、標籤截止日與資料備份)\n │    ├── 辦公關閉 ── 因系統升級，週五下午 (2 PM 起) 至週日辦公室「暫時關閉」，週一恢復正常\n │    ├── 標籤截止 ── 專業搬家公司處理設備，員工必須於「8 月 15 日 (August 15)」前為私人物品貼好標籤 (搬家前5天)\n │    └── 資料備份 ── 強制全體員工於「週四晚間前 (Thursday evening)」完成個人檔案備份\n │\n ├── 💡 A - Action (行動方案：專案管理系統上線與漸進式導入)\n │    ├── 軟體升級 ── 新專案管理系統排定「9 月 1 日 (September 1)」正式實施，升級需要進行「數據遷移」\n │    ├── 訓練要求 ── 所有員工都必須強制參加 (mandatory) 系統訓練；對話指出第一場在「週四」舉行\n │    └── 導入策略 ── 系統上線採「漸進式推出 (gradual rollout)」，各部門「分開進行過渡 (separately)」\n │\n └── ✅ R - Result (結果確認：新大樓應變設施與說明會)\n      ├── 預防措施 ── 舊樓故障凸顯應變規劃 (contingency planning) 重要性；新大樓配有「3部客梯+1部貨梯 = 4部電梯」\n      └── 說明諮詢 ── 搬遷與系統升級疑問說明會：時間為「週二下午 3 點」，地點在「B 會議室 (Conference Room B)」","quiz":[{"q":"The IT department announced a temporary office closure on Friday afternoon because they will perform a critical ________ over the weekend.","o":[["A","client correspondence sorting"],["B","system upgrade"],["C","courier provider evaluation"],["D","air-conditioning repair"]],"a":"(B) system upgrade","zh":"IT 部門宣布週五下午暫時關閉辦公室，因為他們將在週末進行一項關鍵的**系統升級**。","e":"對照 Part 4 獨白：「Due to a system upgrade this weekend, there will be a temporary office closure on Friday afternoon.」故正確答案為 (B)。"},{"q":"To ensure that personal possessions are successfully transported during the office relocation on August 20, employees must label their items no later than ________.","o":[["A","Friday afternoon"],["B","August 15"],["C","next Monday"],["D","September 1st"]],"a":"(B) August 15","zh":"為確保在 8 月 20 日的辦公室搬遷中，個人財物能被成功運送，員工必須不遲於**8 月 15 日**為其物品貼上標籤。","e":"此題為「時間截止地雷題」。正式搬家是 8 月 20 日，但私人物品貼標籤截止日為「August 15」，落差 5 天，故選 (B)。"},{"q":"How will the new project management software be implemented across the company's various departments starting September 1st?","o":[["A","All departments will transition simultaneously in a single day."],["B","It will be deployed via paper forms before Thursday evening."],["C","The rollout will be gradual, with departments transitioning separately."],["D","IT will handle all data migration without staff training."]],"a":"(C) The rollout will be gradual, with departments transitioning separately.","zh":"自 9 月 1 日起，新的專案管理軟體將如何在公司各部門中實施？","e":"對照 Part 7 閱讀原文：「The rollout will be gradual, with departments transitioning separately.」這表明系統導入是採漸進式的、各部門分批完成，故選 (C)。(A) 「同時過渡」為經典干擾。"},{"q":"In the office changes memorandum, the operations director notes that the new building at 450 Harbor Street is equipped with ________.","o":[["A","only one freight lift"],["B","two west-wing elevators"],["C","three passenger elevators and one service elevator"],["D","a temporary air-conditioning wing"]],"a":"(C) three passenger elevators and one service elevator","zh":"在辦公室搬遷備忘錄中，營運總監指出港口街 450 號的新大樓配備有**三部客梯和一部服務電梯（客貨梯）**。","e":"對照 Part 7 閱讀：「The new building has three elevators plus a service elevator」這兩者加起來共 4 部，(C) 爲完美吻合的細節敘述。"},{"q":"A manager has questions regarding the upcoming office transition and data migration. According to the guidelines, they should attend the briefing session in ________.","o":[["A","HR office on the third floor"],["B","Conference Room B on Tuesday at 3 PM"],["C","the main boardroom on Thursday afternoon"],["D","the mail room at 11 AM"]],"a":"(B) Conference Room B on Tuesday at 3 PM","zh":"一位經理對於即將到來的辦公室搬遷與數據遷移存有疑問。根據指南，他應該參加在何處舉行的簡報說明會？","e":"此為地點與時間配對題。備忘錄結尾提及：「For questions, attend Tuesday's session at 3 PM in Conference Room B.」因此應選 (B)。"}],"say":["Did you hear about the office relocation next month?","True. Don't forget - there's training for the new system implementation on Thursday.","Attention all staff. Due to a system upgrade this weekend, there will be a temporary office closure on Friday afternoon. The new system implementation begins at 2 PM, and normal operations resume Monday.","Please back up your files before Thursday evening. The IT department has contingency plans for any disruption during the rollout. Report any malfunction on Monday to the help desk immediately.","Also, the west wing elevator is out of service until Wednesday due to mechanical problems. Use the stairs or east wing elevator.","Finally, our office relocation to the new premises is still scheduled for the end of next month.","We have two important updates. First, our office relocation to 450 Harbor Street is confirmed for August 20. The transition occurs over the weekend to minimize disruption.","Professional movers will handle equipment. Label personal items by August 15. There will be a temporary office closure Friday afternoon through Sunday.","Second, we're implementing a new system for project management on September 1. The upgrade requires data migration. Training is mandatory for all staff. The rollout will be gradual, with departments transitioning separately.","The recent elevator breakdown highlighted our need for better contingency planning. The new building has three elevators plus a service elevator, preventing such malfunctions from causing problems. For questions, attend Tuesday's session at 3 PM in Conference Room B. -- David Chen"]},"9-1":{"tree":"【Ch9-1 媒體內容與傳播 Media Content & Communication】\n │\n ├── 🔴 S - Situation (情境確認：了解媒體專案類型與許可證)\n │    ├── 專案主題 ── 關於本地作者的紀錄片 (documentary about local authors)\n │    ├── 許可進度 ── 昨天拿到攝影許可證 (got photography permit yesterday)\n │    └── 設備需求 ── 尚需租借攝影器材 (still need to rent camera equipment)\n │\n ├── 📋 T - Task (任務說明：媒體採訪安排與平台確認)\n │    ├── 採訪單位 ── 格里芬市新聞 (Griffin City News) 明日進行採訪 (interview tomorrow)\n │    ├── 媒體形式 ── 電視新聞廣播 (TV news broadcast) ，非純廣播 (not radio)\n │    └── 延伸合作 ── 完成後將登上其串流平台 (featured on streaming platform)\n │\n ├── 💡 A - Action (行動方案：製作會議事項與歸還規定)\n │    ├── 劇集續訂 ── 《Best Son》續訂下一季，下週五前準備好第一集手稿 (manuscript by next Friday)\n │    ├── 紀錄片播出 ── 今晚 9 點電視播出 (air tonight at 9 PM)，明天串流上架 (streaming tomorrow)\n │    └── 器材維護 ── 拍攝後強制歸還至儲藏室 (return camera equipment to storage room)\n │\n └── ✅ R - Result (結果回報：專案備忘錄與下月首映)\n      ├── 劇集改編 ── 新劇集手稿獲批 (manuscript approved)，6月開拍，作者 David Chen 下週到訪\n      ├── 獨家新聞 ── 週五下午 6 點新聞播出 (Friday at 6 PM)，下週安排廣播節目專訪\n      └── 串流首映 ── 紀錄片《Writers at Work》下月在 3 大串流平台首映 (premiere on 3 platforms)","quiz":[{"q":"What is the woman currently working on according to the conversation?","o":[["A","A news article for a local newspaper"],["B","A documentary about local authors"],["C","A radio show about photography"],["D","A textbook on digital publication"]],"a":"(B) A documentary about local authors","zh":"根據對話，女士目前正在製作什麼？","e":"男聲第一句明確提及：working on a documentary about local authors，故選 (B)。"},{"q":"When did the woman obtain her photography permit?","o":[["A","Yesterday"],["B","This morning"],["C","Next week"],["D","Next month"]],"a":"(A) Yesterday","zh":"女士何時拿到她的攝影許可證？","e":"女聲回答：Yes, I got it yesterday.，故 (A) 為唯一正確答案。"},{"q":"What media format will Griffin City News use for tomorrow's interview?","o":[["A","Radio program"],["B","Newspaper article"],["C","Television"],["D","Podcast"]],"a":"(C) Television","zh":"格里芬市新聞明天的採訪將使用什麼媒體形式？","e":"男聲明確指出：It's for TV.，故選 (C)。"},{"q":"According to the monologue, when is the manuscript for \"Best Son\" due?","o":[["A","Tonight at 9 PM"],["B","Tomorrow morning"],["C","Next Friday"],["D","Next month"]],"a":"(C) Next Friday","zh":"根據獨白，《Best Son》的手稿何時到期？","e":"獨白指出：ready by next Friday，故選 (C)。"},{"q":"Where should camera equipment be placed after filming?","o":[["A","At the production office"],["B","In the storage room"],["C","On the streaming platform"],["D","At Griffin City News"]],"a":"(B) In the storage room","zh":"拍攝結束後，攝影器材應該放在哪裡？","e":"獨白明確規定：returned to the storage room after each shoot，故選 (B)。"}],"say":["Hi Sarah, I heard you're working on a documentary about local authors. Do you have a photography permit yet?","Great. By the way, Griffin City News wants to do a news broadcast about your project. Can you do an interview tomorrow?","Good morning, everyone. Welcome to Channel 5's production meeting. First, I'm pleased to announce that the TV series \"Best Son\" has been picked up for another season. The writing team should have the manuscript for the first episode ready by next Friday.","Our news broadcast team has received several awards this month. The documentary on book publication in the digital age will air tonight at 9 PM. It features interviews with three bestselling authors about their writing process. Finally, remember that all camera equipment must be returned to the storage room after each shoot. Photography permits for next month's outdoor productions are now available. Please check with the production office if you need one. The show will also be available on our streaming platform starting tomorrow.","\"Team, I have several important updates about our media projects.","Yes, I got it yesterday. But I still need to rent camera equipment. The production starts next week.","Sure. Is it for their radio program or TV?","The manuscript for our new TV series has been approved. The author, David Chen, will join us next week to discuss the adaptation. We'll begin production in June, and all camera equipment has been reserved. Please ensure your photography permits are current before we start filming.","It's for TV. They're also interested in featuring your documentary on their streaming platform when it's finished.","Griffin City News has requested an exclusive interview about our upcoming documentary. The news broadcast is scheduled for Friday at 6 PM. Their reporter will also write an article for their online platform. Additionally, their radio program wants a separate interview next week."]},"9-2":{"tree":"【Ch9-2 活動參與體驗 Event Participation Experience】\n │\n ├── 🔴 S - Situation (情境確認：多重活動門票與展期詢問)\n │    ├── 歌劇院演出 ── 今晚 8 點開演 (starts at 8 PM at opera house)，現場有票\n │    ├── 天文特展 ── \"Our Galaxy\" 展出至月底 (until end of month)\n │    └── 藝術節時程 ── 年度 Art Walk 藝術漫步節排定於下週末 (next weekend)\n │\n ├── 📋 T - Task (任務說明：購票管道與附加服務)\n │    ├── 線上購票優勢 ── 網路買博物館門票附贈免費導覽 (guided tours included)\n │    └── 街頭市集特點 ── 市集包含美食攤位 (food vendors) 與手工藝攤位 (craft booths)\n │\n ├── 💡 A - Action (行動方案：藝術中心公告活動)\n │    ├── 爵士音樂節 ── 今晚 7 點進行 (jazz festival at 7 PM)，售票處有售 (box office)\n │    ├── 攝影特展 ── 明天開幕展至下月，工作坊報名需提前 48 小時 (48 hours before)\n │    └── 導覽時段 ── 週六市集期間，10 AM - 4 PM 每小時一班導覽 (every hour)\n │\n └── ✅ R - Result (結果回報：夏季活動優惠細則)\n      ├── 展期截至 ── \"Our Galaxy\" 展至 8 月 31 日，每日 11 AM & 3 PM 有導覽\n      ├── 門票折扣 ── Art Walk 期間歌劇院門票享 8 折 (20% discount)\n      └── 團體優惠 ── 10 人以上享團體折扣 (group discounts for 10+ people)","quiz":[{"q":"Where will tonight's 8 PM performance take place?","o":[["A","At the science museum"],["B","At the opera house"],["C","At the street fair"],["D","At the art gallery"]],"a":"(B) At the opera house","zh":"","e":"對話明確提及：starts at 8 PM at the opera house。"},{"q":"What advantage is mentioned for buying museum tickets online?","o":[["A","It offers a 20% discount"],["B","It includes guided museum tours"],["C","It provides free food vouchers"],["D","It allows entry after 8 PM"]],"a":"(B) It includes guided museum tours","zh":"","e":"男聲指明：offering guided museum tours with the exhibit admission。"},{"q":"When will the annual Art Walk festival take place?","o":[["A","Tonight at 7 PM"],["B","Tomorrow"],["C","Next weekend"],["D","At the end of August"]],"a":"(C) Next weekend","zh":"","e":"對話指出：That's next weekend.。"},{"q":"According to the monologue, how often are museum tours conducted on Saturday?","o":[["A","Every 30 minutes"],["B","Every hour"],["C","Twice a day"],["D","Only at 10 AM and 4 PM"]],"a":"(B) Every hour","zh":"","e":"公告說明：every hour from 10 AM to 4 PM。"},{"q":"By when must workshop registration be completed according to the poster?","o":[["A","24 hours before class"],["B","48 hours before class start date"],["C","On the day of the event"],["D","By July 15"]],"a":"(B) 48 hours before class start date","zh":"","e":"海報明確規定：Workshop registration closes 48 hours before class start date.。"}],"say":["Hi, I'd like to purchase theater tickets for tonight's performance. Are they still available?","Good afternoon, and welcome to the Downtown Arts Center. This week we have several exciting events. Tonight's jazz festival continues at 7 PM with music performances from international artists. Concert tickets are still available at the box office. Tomorrow, we're opening a new exhibit at our art galleries featuring local photographers. The exhibition runs through next month, and workshop registration for photography classes is now open on our website. Finally, don't forget about the annual street fair this Saturday. There will be food vendors, craft booths, and live performances all day. The opera house is also offering discounted theater tickets during the fair. Museum tours will be available every hour from 10 AM to 4 PM.","Let me check... Yes, we have seats available. The show starts at 8 PM at the opera house.","\"Our Galaxy\" exhibit at the Science Museum (through August 31)","Perfect. Also, is the \"Our Galaxy\" exhibit still at the museum? My kids really want to see it.","Daily museum tours at 11 AM and 3 PM","Yes, it's there until the end of the month. But you should get your museum tickets online - they're offering guided museum tours with the exhibit admission.","Special workshop registration available for astronomy classes"]},"9-3":{"tree":"【Ch9-3 活動幕後運作 Behind-the-Scenes Operations】\n │\n ├── 🔴 S - Situation (情境確認：音響就緒但舞台搭建延遲)\n │    ├── 音響進度 ── 音響設備已準備好 (audio equipment ready)\n │    ├── 舞台問題 ── 舞台搭建延遲，技術人員還需 1 小時 (needs another hour)\n │    └── 排練壓點 ── 原定下午 4 點排練 (rehearsal at 4 PM)，時間非常緊迫\n │\n ├── 📋 T - Task (任務說明：職責分工與後台劇本修改)\n │    ├── 男聲分工 ── 負責技術準備工作 (handle technical preparations)\n │    ├── 女聲分工 ── 對接服裝部完成演員量身 (cast measurements for costumes)\n │    └── 劇本改寫 ── 導演要求彩排前由後台人員協助改寫劇本 (script rewriting)\n │\n ├── 💡 A - Action (行動方案：明日拍攝行程調整)\n │    ├── 到達時間 ── 攝影劇組上午 7 點前到達 (crew arrive by 7 AM)\n │    ├── 時程順序 ── 9 AM 服裝量身 ➔ 11 AM 排練 (留時間改劇本) ➔ 2 PM 音響測試\n │    └── 區域規範 ── 所有劇組協調僅限於指定區域 (designated areas only)\n │\n └── ✅ R - Result (結果回報：週末正式開演時間軸)\n      ├── 週六行程 ── 8 AM 架設 ➔ 10 AM 量身 ➔ 1 PM 排練 ➔ 5 PM 協調會\n      ├── 週日行程 ── 9 AM 最終架設 ➔ 11 AM 彩排 ➔ 7 PM 正式開演 (production begins)\n      └── 幕後紀錄 ── 攝影劇組將記錄兩天過程做為幕後花絮 (behind-the-scenes feature)","quiz":[{"q":"What is currently causing a delay for tonight's performance?","o":[["A","Audio equipment failure"],["B","Stage setup issues"],["C","Missing costume department staff"],["D","Director's absence"]],"a":"(B) Stage setup issues","zh":"","e":"男聲提到：having issues with the stage setup。"},{"q":"What task will the woman handle?","o":[["A","Fixing the audio equipment"],["B","Rewriting the script"],["C","Working with the costume department"],["D","Leading the crew meeting"]],"a":"(C) Working with the costume department","zh":"","e":"男聲分工：while you work with the costume department。"},{"q":"Why was tomorrow's rehearsal moved to 11 AM in the monologue?","o":[["A","To allow more time for script rewriting"],["B","Because the film crew will arrive late"],["C","To conduct audio equipment tests first"],["D","Due to venue management requests"]],"a":"(A) To allow more time for script rewriting","zh":"","e":"獨白說明：rehearsal is moved to 11 AM to allow more time for script rewriting。"},{"q":"When is the audio equipment test scheduled in tomorrow's monologue?","o":[["A","At 7 AM"],["B","At 9 AM"],["C","At 11 AM"],["D","At 2 PM"]],"a":"(D) At 2 PM","zh":"","e":"獨白提醒：audio equipment test is at 2 PM。"},{"q":"According to the memo, what time does the production officially begin on Sunday?","o":[["A","11:00 AM"],["B","2:00 PM"],["C","5:00 PM"],["D","7:00 PM"]],"a":"(D) 7:00 PM","zh":"","e":"備忘錄週日行程明確標註：7:00 PM: Production begins。"}],"say":["Tom, how's the equipment setup going for tonight's performance?","Good evening, everyone. This is a reminder about tomorrow's production schedule. The film crew should arrive by 7 AM for equipment setup. Technical preparations will begin immediately, so please don't be late. At 9 AM, we'll have cast measurements in the costume department. All actors must attend. The rehearsal is moved to 11 AM to allow more time for script rewriting. Our writer will be backstage if you have questions about the changes. Theater operations will continue as normal during our preparations. The venue management team asks that all crew coordination happens in the designated areas only. Remember, the audio equipment test is at 2 PM. Make sure everything is ready for tonight's production.","MEMO To: All Production Staff From: Michael Park, Production Manager Date: June 10","The audio equipment is ready, but we're having issues with the stage setup. The technical staff needs another hour.","Subject: Weekend Production Schedule","That's cutting it close. We have a rehearsal at 4 PM, and the cast measurements for costumes aren't done yet.","Team, This weekend's production requires careful coordination. Please review the following schedule:","Don't worry. The crew coordination meeting just ended. Everyone knows their responsibilities. I'll handle the technical preparations while you work with the costume department."]},"9-4":{"tree":"【Ch9-4 導覽與特別活動 Guided Tours & Special Events】\n │\n ├── 🔴 S - Situation (情境確認：參加新翼導覽與今晚頒獎典禮)\n │    ├── 導覽時間 ── 新翼大樓導覽 10 分鐘後開始 (starts in 10 minutes)\n │    ├── 典禮資訊 ── 今晚有在地藝術家頒獎典禮 (award ceremony tonight)\n │    └── 門票包含 ── 包含被提名者見面會 (meet-and-greet) 與特展盛大開幕\n │\n ├── 📋 T - Task (任務說明：導覽亮點與獨家通道權限)\n │    ├── 導覽看點 ── 包含 3 座新雕塑揭幕 (unveiling of three sculptures)\n │    └── 獨家特權 ── 提供平時不對外開放區域的獨家通道 (exclusive access)\n │\n ├── 💡 A - Action (行動方案：明日活動安排與拍照規定)\n │    ├── 明日剪綵 ── 上午 10 點新畫廊剪綵 (ribbon-cutting at 10 AM tomorrow)\n │    ├── 名人現身 ── 藝術家 Maria Santos 晚間 8 點參加見面會\n │    └── 拍照規定 ── 盛大開幕可拍照 (permitted)，但典禮期間禁止拍照\n │\n └── ✅ R - Result (結果回報：年度貴賓晚會行程表)\n      ├── 時間流程 ── 6 PM 雞尾酒會 ➔ 7 PM 導覽 ➔ 8 PM 典禮 ➔ 9 PM 見面會\n      ├── 幕後探訪 ── VIP 可參觀藝術修復實驗室 (restoration laboratory)\n      └── 參加要求 ── 7 月 15 日前需 RSVP 回覆，服裝要求為商務便服 (business attire)","quiz":[{"q":"What is the main purpose of the man's initial inquiry?","o":[["A","To purchase tickets for a concert"],["B","To join a guided tour of the new wing"],["C","To apply for a docent position"],["D","To submit his artwork for an award"]],"a":"(B) To join a guided tour of the new wing","zh":"","e":"男聲第一句：here for the guided tour of the new wing。"},{"q":"What is NOT mentioned as part of the award ceremony ticket?","o":[["A","Meet-and-greet with nominees"],["B","Grand opening of a special exhibit"],["C","Free dinner at the opera house"],["D","Access to prestigious events"]],"a":"(C) Free dinner at the opera house","zh":"","e":"對話提到見面會與開幕展，並未提及免費晚餐。"},{"q":"According to the monologue, when will Maria Santos participate in the meet-and-greet?","o":[["A","At 10 AM"],["B","At 6 PM"],["C","At 8 PM"],["D","At 9:30 PM"]],"a":"(C) At 8 PM","zh":"","e":"獨白指明：meet-and-greet session at 8 PM。"},{"q":"When is photography strictly prohibited according to the monologue?","o":[["A","During the grand opening"],["B","During the inauguration ceremony"],["C","During the docent tour"],["D","During the cocktail reception"]],"a":"(B) During the inauguration ceremony","zh":"","e":"獨白規定：not during the inauguration ceremony。"},{"q":"According to the invitation, by when must guests submit their RSVP?","o":[["A","June 10"],["B","July 15"],["C","August 31"],["D","May 20"]],"a":"(B) July 15","zh":"","e":"邀請函下方註明：RSVP required by July 15.。"}],"say":["Good morning. I'm here for the guided tour of the new wing. Is the docent available?","Good evening, ladies and gentlemen. Welcome to tonight's prestigious award ceremony. Before we begin the recognition of our nominees, I'd like to announce tomorrow's special events. At 10 AM, we'll have the ribbon-cutting for our new gallery, followed by a guided tour led by our senior docent. The itinerary includes exclusive interviews with award winners and a special unveiling of our permanent collection. The highlights of the evening include a celebrity appearance by renowned artist Maria Santos. She'll participate in a meet-and-greet session at 8 PM. Photography is permitted during the grand opening but not during the inauguration ceremony. Thank you for joining us for this memorable occasion.","EXCLUSIVE INVITATION The Metropolitan Arts Center - Annual Recognition Gala","Yes, the tour starts in 10 minutes. But first, did you know there's an award ceremony here tonight? We're recognizing local artists.","You are cordially invited to our prestigious award ceremony honoring excellence in contemporary art.","Really? Can I still get tickets?","There are a few left. It includes a meet-and-greet with the nominees and the grand opening of our special exhibit.","6:00 PM: Grand opening cocktail reception"]},"10-1":{"tree":"【Ch10-1 翻新工程與設施維護 Construction & Maintenance Management】\n │\n ├── 🔴 S - Situation (情境確認：通報緊急維修與結構隱患)\n │    ├── 問題類型 ── 三樓會議室/西翼/四樓儲藏區漏水 (leak)、北側地基水損 (foundation damage)、水管故障 (plumbing issue)\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **building inspector** (建築檢查員), **immediate repair** (立即維修), **water damage** (水損)\n │    └── 📍 地點干擾 ── 對話: 3rd floor conference room vs 獨白: west wing vs 備忘錄: 4th floor storage\n │\n ├── 📋 T - Task (任務確認：確認前置程序與權責)\n │    ├── 必辦前置 ── 所有主要工程開始前必須「申請翻新許可證 (apply for renovation permit)」\n │    ├── 權責分工 ── 維護經理 (maintenance manager) 負責日常協調 vs 承包商 (contractor) 負責執行\n │    └── 核心字彙 ── **renovation permit** (翻新許可證), **plumbing upgrades** (水管升級)\n │\n ├── 💡 A - Action (行動方案：審查藍圖與安排施工)\n │    ├── 執行步驟 ── 聘請莫里森建設 (Morrison Construction)、建築師審查藍圖 (blueprint) 找替代水路\n │    ├── ⏰ 工時大對比 ── 對話估算: **3 days** vs 獨白估算: **3 weeks** vs 備忘錄估算: **4-5 weeks**\n │    └── 審批時間 ── 市規劃局許可證批准需 **5 個工作日 (5 business days)**\n │\n └── ✅ R - Result (結果確認：現場監督與法規合規)\n      ├── 合規檢查 ── 市立檢查員 (city inspector) 全程在場，確保符合當地建築法規 (building codes)\n      └── 最終目標 ── 解決漏水、防止水損擴散至下層樓 (lower floors)、確保建築完整性","quiz":[{"q":"Before commencing any major ceiling replacement or plumbing upgrades, the contractor is required to _______ a renovation permit from the city.","o":[["A","inspect"],["B","obtain"],["C","repair"],["D","construct"]],"a":"(B) obtain","zh":"在開始任何主要的更換天花板或水管升級工程之前，承包商必須從市政府**取得**翻新許可證。","e":"obtain a permit（取得許可證）為多益固定搭配，等同於 apply for / secure a permit。"},{"q":"According to the memorandum, how long is the permit application expected to take for approval?","o":[["A","3 days"],["B","5 business days"],["C","3 weeks"],["D","4 to 5 weeks"]],"a":"(B) 5 business days","zh":"根據備忘錄，許可證申請預計需要多久時間獲得批准？","e":"文章明確指出：「expect approval within 5 business days」，(A) 3 days 為對話中估算的修復天數，(C) 3 weeks 為獨白中的施工時間，(D) 4-5 weeks 為備忘錄中的施工總工期。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"What is the main purpose of reviewing the building's original blueprint?","o":[["A","To submit it to the city building inspector"],["B","To find an alternative water route and plan the renovation"],["C","To calculate the total cost of the electrical inspection"],["D","To train new maintenance technicians"]],"a":"(B) To find an alternative water route and plan the renovation","zh":"審查大樓原始藍圖的主要目的是什麼？","e":"對話與備忘錄均指出建築師審查藍圖（blueprint）是為了規劃替代水路與全面翻修計畫。"},{"q":"The phrase \"complies with\" in the reading passage is closest in meaning to _______.","o":[["A","interferes with"],["B","conforms to"],["C","departs from"],["D","negotiates with"]],"a":"(B) conforms to","zh":"閱讀文章中的短語 \"complies with\"（符合/遵守）與下列哪一個最接近？","e":"comply with = conform to = adhere to（符合/遵守法規）。"},{"q":"Who is responsible for the day-to-day coordination during the construction project?","o":[["A","The city building inspector"],["B","The primary architect"],["C","The maintenance manager"],["D","The department heads"]],"a":"(C) The maintenance manager","zh":"在施工專案期間，誰負責日常的協調工作？","e":"對話、獨白與備忘錄均強調「The maintenance manager will handle the day-to-day coordination」，故選 (C)。"}],"say":["Hi, Jennifer. I just got a call from the building inspector. He said there's a leak in the third-floor conference room that requires immediate repair.","It looks like a plumbing issue this time. The maintenance manager will handle the problem, but we need to apply for a renovation permit before starting any major work.","I see. How long will it take? We have client meetings scheduled there next week.","Good idea. Make sure the technician checks the foundation area too. We don't want any water damage spreading to the lower floors.","Good afternoon. This is the facilities department with an important update. Starting Monday, our contractor will begin renovation work on the building's plumbing and electrical systems.","The maintenance manager will handle the coordination, and we need to apply for a renovation permit before replacing the ceiling on the second floor.","The contractor estimates the work will take three weeks. Please check your email for the full construction schedule and alternate routes.","I am writing to inform you about urgent maintenance issues that have arisen in our main office building and the steps we are taking to address them.","We have hired Morrison Construction as our primary contractor for this project. Their team, led by architect James Morrison, has reviewed our building's original blueprint and developed a comprehensive renovation plan.","Please note that an inspector from the city building department will be on-site throughout the construction period to ensure all work complies with local building codes."]},"10-2":{"tree":"【Ch10-2 物業交易與搜尋 Property Transactions & Search】\n │\n ├── 🔴 S - Situation (情境確認：提出住宅或商業租務需求)\n │    ├── 房產類型 ── 住宅: 2-bedroom apartment (85 sqm) / 3-bedroom house / studio; 商業: 120 sqm office suite (15th floor)\n │    ├── 配備狀態 ── **furnished** (附家具, 可立即入住) vs **unfurnished** (不附家具/清水房, 可自行佈置)\n │    └── 筆誤陷阱 ── 信件經紀人誤將 office space 寫成 three-bedroom apartment，並即時更正 (error correction)\n │\n ├── 📋 T - Task (任務確認：釐清財務條件與估價數字)\n │    ├── 財務計算 ── 月租 $1,800 ➔ 押金 2個月 ($3,600) ➔ 入住首月總需支付 **$5,400**\n │    ├── 估價地雷 ── 對話住宅估價: **$350,000** vs 獨白獨立屋: **$485,000** vs 商業大樓: **$1,200,000 ($1.2M)**\n │    └── 商業條款 ── 辦公室月租 $3,500，提供 2 個指定停車位 (two designated parking spaces)\n │\n ├── 💡 A - Action (行動方案：安排看房與核對租期)\n │    ├── 租期區分 ── 對話公寓: March 1st 開始; 獨白展銷: April 1st - March 31st; 商業信件: March 1st - Feb 28th\n │    └── 看房安排 ── 展示會結束後立即安排看房 (immediately after presentation)\n │\n └── ✅ R - Result (結果確認：完成簽約與房產交接)\n      ├── 簽約要素 ── 支付押金 (pay deposit)、簽署租約 (sign lease)、房東提供客製化微調 (minor modifications)\n      └── 最終目標 ── 確保房產 (property secured)、確認租約 (lease confirmed)、隨時可入住 (move-in ready)","quiz":[{"q":"What error does David Chang correct in his email to Ms. Mitchell?","o":[["A","The monthly rental price of the office suite"],["B","The location of the designated parking spaces"],["C","The description of the commercial property layout"],["D","The expiration date of the lease agreement"]],"a":"(C) The description of the commercial property layout","zh":"David Chang 在給 Mitchell 女士的電子郵件中更正了什麼錯誤？","e":"信中明確寫道：「This three-bedroom apartment includes - excuse me, I meant to write 'This office space includes'」，更正了將商業辦公空間誤寫為住宅公寓的格局描述錯誤。故選 (C)。"},{"q":"For a tenant renting the $1,800 downtown apartment described in Part 3, how much total money is required upfront for rent and the deposit?","o":[["A","$1,800"],["B","$3,600"],["C","$5,400"],["D","$7,200"]],"a":"(C) $5,400","zh":"對於租用 Part 3 中描述的月租 1,800 美元市中心公寓的租客，前期租金加押金總共需要多少錢？","e":"月租為 $1,800，押金為兩個月租金（$1,800 × 2 = $3,600）。前期總費用 = $1,800 + $3,600 = $5,400。故選 (C)。"},{"q":"According to the property showcase monologue, when can prospective buyers view the featured properties?","o":[["A","On March 1st"],["B","Immediately after the presentation"],["C","After paying a 10% mortgage deposit"],["D","Next Friday afternoon"]],"a":"(B) Immediately after the presentation","zh":"根據房產展示獨白，潛在買家何時可以看精選房產？","e":"獨白結尾明確指出：「we can arrange property viewings immediately after this presentation」，故選 (B)。"},{"q":"The word \"furnished\" in the dialogue is closest in meaning to _______.","o":[["A","newly constructed"],["B","with appliances and furniture"],["C","unequipped"],["D","currently occupied"]],"a":"(B) with appliances and furniture","zh":"對話中的單字 \"furnished\"（附家具的）與下列哪一個最接近？","e":"furnished = equipped with furniture and appliances。"},{"q":"What additional amenity is specifically provided to each tenant in the Grandview Tower commercial building?","o":[["A","Free utility management"],["B","Complimentary daily cleaning service"],["C","Two designated parking spaces"],["D","A fully furnished reception desk"]],"a":"(C) Two designated parking spaces","zh":"Grandview Tower 商業大樓為每位租客特別提供什麼額外設施？","e":"信件第四段提及：「The building offers 24-hour security, high-speed internet infrastructure, and two designated parking spaces for each tenant」，故選 (C)。"}],"say":["Hi, I'm calling about the two-bedroom apartment you have listed on your website. I'm looking to rent something in the downtown area for my family.","The monthly rent is $1,800, but you'll need to pay a deposit equal to two months' rent.","Good morning, and welcome to Citywide Real Estate's monthly property showcase. I'm pleased to announce that we have several exciting listings to present today. Whether you're a first-time buyer looking for an unfurnished flat to customize, or an investor seeking furnished properties for rental income, we have options for you.","For those interested in investment opportunities, we also have several studio apartments perfect for tenants in the university area.","Dear Ms. Mitchell, Thank you for your inquiry about our commercial properties. I'm pleased to inform you that we have several options that match your requirements.","The monthly rent is $3,500, with a required deposit of two months' rent. As your broker, I can arrange a viewing at your earliest convenience.","Certainly! That property is still available. It's a furnished apartment with 85 square-metres of space.","I see. We are looking to rent a place starting from March 1st. Can you tell me more about the valuation process? My landlord mentioned I should understand how it works.","Today, we'll be featuring a special three-bedroom house in the Riverside district. The property valuation came in at $485,000, which represents excellent value in today's market.","The lease term runs from April 1st to March 31st for most of our rental properties, providing flexibility for both landlords and tenants. Our experienced brokers are standing by to answer any questions about mortgage options and financing."]},"10-3":{"tree":"【Ch10-3 設施與公用事業管理 Facilities & Utilities Management】\n │\n ├── 🔴 S - Situation (情境確認：電費偏高與停電事故)\n │    ├── 帳單金額 ── 對話個人帳單: **$3,200** (異常高) vs 備忘錄全樓帳單: **$48,000** (因電壓調整調漲 15%)\n │    ├── 停電戶數 ── 對話上週: **12 units** vs 獨白昨日: **15 units** vs 備忘錄上週二: **3樓 8 units**\n │    └── 核心字彙 ── **meter readings** (電表讀數), **power outage** (停電), **generator** (發電機)\n │\n ├── 📋 T - Task (任務確認：釐清公用事業責任與安排檢查)\n │    ├── 責任歸屬 ── **Utilities not included in monthly rent** (租金不含水電，租客須自行向 Regional Power 建戶)\n │    └── 檢查排程 ── 對話: **Next Tuesday** vs 獨白: **Friday afternoon** vs 備忘錄: **April 12th 2:00 PM (持續 3 小時)**\n │\n ├── 💡 A - Action (行動方案：電網升級與線路加固)\n │    ├── 應變措施 ── 停電時持續運轉備用發電機 (running backup generator continuously)\n │    └── 長期改善 ── 升級電力網至節能系統 (upgrade grid system)、加固電路連接 (reinforced circuit connections)\n │\n └── ✅ R - Result (結果確認：電壓穩定與精準計費)\n      ├── 改善效果 ── 電壓成功穩定 (voltage stabilized)、數位電表實施提供精確消耗追蹤 (accurate tracking)\n      └── 最終目標 ── 確保持續供電 (continuous power supply)、降低營運成本","quiz":[{"q":"According to the dialogue in Part 3, why were the electricity charges unusually high for the month?","o":[["A","The elevator inspection required extra high voltage."],["B","The tenant installed new energy-inefficient appliances."],["C","The backup generator was operated continuously following a power outage."],["D","Regional Power Corporation increased its base rate by 15%."]],"a":"(C) The backup generator was operated continuously following a power outage.","zh":"根據 Part 3 的對話，為什麼這個月的電費異常偏高？","e":"對話中 Mr. Thompson 解釋：「We experienced a power outage affecting twelve units last week, so we've been running the generator continuously」，故選 (C)。"},{"q":"What are commercial tenants in the Westfield Commercial Building required to do regarding utilities?","o":[["A","Pay a flat monthly fee directly to the landlord"],["B","Establish an independent account with Regional Power Corporation"],["C","Share the total $48,000 electricity charge equally among all units"],["D","Submit manual meter readings to the Facilities Management Office"]],"a":"(B) Establish an independent account with Regional Power Corporation","zh":"Westfield 商業大樓的商業租客在公用事業方面被要求做什麼？","e":"公告明確指出：「utilities are not included in the monthly rent... Each tenant must establish their own account with Regional Power Corporation」，故選 (B)。"},{"q":"How long is the scheduled elevator inspection expected to last on April 12th?","o":[["A","1 hour"],["B","2 hours"],["C","3 hours"],["D","5 hours"]],"a":"(C) 3 hours","zh":"4 月 12 日排定的電梯檢查預計持續多久？","e":"公告第三段明確寫道：「The inspection will require approximately three hours」，故選 (C)。"},{"q":"The word \"stabilized\" in the monologue is closest in meaning to _______.","o":[["A","disconnected"],["B","made steady"],["C","increased rapidly"],["D","inspected"]],"a":"(B) made steady","zh":"獨白中的單字 \"stabilized\"（穩定）與下列哪一個最接近？","e":"stabilized = made steady = balanced。"},{"q":"Which floor was specifically affected by the power outage mentioned in the reading notice?","o":[["A","Second floor"],["B","Third floor"],["C","Fourth floor"],["D","Fifteenth floor"]],"a":"(B) Third floor","zh":"閱讀通告中提到的停電具體影響了哪一個樓層？","e":"通告指出：「we experienced a power outage affecting eight units on the third floor last Tuesday」，故選 (B)。"}],"say":["Good morning, Mr. Thompson. The electricity charges for this month total $3,200, which seems unusually high.","I see. Also, utilities are not included in the monthly rent for the new tenants, correct?","Thanks for reminding me. Have you looked into more energy-efficient options?","Attention all building residents. This is a notice from the utilities department about upcoming infrastructure improvements.","We experienced a power outage affecting fifteen units yesterday, which required us to switch to our backup generator. The voltage in the circuit system has now been stabilized. Please note that the elevator inspection is scheduled for Friday afternoon.","First, please be advised that utilities are not included in the monthly rent for all commercial units. Each tenant must establish their own account with Regional Power Corporation, our designated electricity provider.","The elevator inspection is scheduled for April 12th at 2:00 PM. The inspection will require approximately three hours, during which time elevator service will be limited.","Let me check the meter readings. We experienced a power outage affecting twelve units last week, so we've been running the generator continuously.","That's right. They'll need to contact the provider directly. Oh, and the elevator inspection is scheduled for next Tuesday.","Yes, the grid system offers special rates for buildings with lower consumption."]},"10-4":{"tree":"【Ch10-4 倉儲與物流服務 Warehouse & Logistics Services】\n │\n ├── 🔴 S - Situation (情境確認：貨運抵達與倉庫容量現況)\n │    ├── 到貨時間 ── 對話: **3:00 PM** vs 獨白: **Noon (中午)** vs 備忘錄: **10:00 AM daily**\n │    ├── 尺寸規格 ── 對話: **20 × 30 ft** vs 獨白: **25 × 40 ft** vs 備忘錄: **30 × 50 ft**\n │    └── 容量狀態 ── 對話: **Full capacity (滿載)** vs 獨白: **80% capacity** vs 備忘錄: **500 pallets capacity**\n │\n ├── 📋 T - Task (任務確認：點收準備與設備指派)\n │    ├── 服務時段 ── 對話: 8 AM - 6 PM; 獨白: 7 AM - 5 PM; 備忘錄: 6 AM - 8 PM (平日延長)\n │    └── 設備預備 ── 堆高機定位於調度區，10點到貨須於 **9:30 AM (提前 30 分鐘)** 充電完畢預備\n │\n ├── 💡 A - Action (行動方案：轉移備用倉庫與標籤記錄)\n │    ├── 滿載應變 ── 將過多棧板移至備用倉庫 (overflow warehouse)\n │    └── 登錄程序 ── 檢查出貨標籤 (check labels)，進港貨物移離碼頭前須先錄入物流資料庫\n │\n └── ✅ R - Result (結果確認：高度容納標準與效率提升)\n      ├── 限高區分 ── 對話限制: **15 feet high** vs 獨白限制: **20 feet high** vs 備忘錄限制: **18 feet high**\n      └── 效率提升 ── 調度流程改善後，每日可多處理 **20% (one-fifth)** 的發貨量 (process 20% more shipments)","quiz":[{"q":"In the dialogue in Part 3, what solution is proposed to handle the storage unit being at full capacity?","o":[["A","Canceling the 3 PM freight delivery"],["B","Moving some pallets to the overflow warehouse"],["C","Increasing the height limit of the storage unit to 20 feet"],["D","Rejecting incoming shipments without climate-control"]],"a":"(B) Moving some pallets to the overflow warehouse","zh":"在 Part 3 的對話中，提出了什麼解決方案來處理儲存單元滿載的問題？","e":"對話中男士詢問：「Can we move some pallets to the overflow warehouse?」，女士回答「That works」，故選 (B)。"},{"q":"According to James Wilson's memo, by what time must forklifts be charged and ready for daily operations?","o":[["A","6:00 AM"],["B","8:00 AM"],["C","9:30 AM"],["D","10:00 AM"]],"a":"(C) 9:30 AM","zh":"根據 James Wilson 的備忘錄，堆高機必須在每天幾點前完成充電並準備就緒？","e":"備忘錄提及每日貨運 10:00 AM 抵達，「so please ensure forklifts are charged and ready for use by 9:30 AM」，故選 (C)。"},{"q":"What is stated about the dispatch improvements in the reading passage?","o":[["A","Delivery hours have been shortened on weekends."],["B","The warehouse can now process 20% more shipments daily."],["C","Forklifts are no longer required at the loading dock."],["D","Climate-control systems have been removed from the main storage unit."]],"a":"(B) The warehouse can now process 20% more shipments daily.","zh":"關於閱讀文章中的調度改進，提及了什麼？","e":"備忘錄最後一段指出：「With the recent dispatch improvements, we can now process 20% more shipments per day」，故選 (B)。"},{"q":"The word \"accommodate\" in the monologue is closest in meaning to _______.","o":[["A","reject"],["B","hold"],["C","transport"],["D","purchase"]],"a":"(B) hold","zh":"獨白中的單字 \"accommodate\"（容納）與下列哪一個最接近？","e":"accommodate = hold = have space for（容納/存放）。"},{"q":"According to the monologue in Part 4, what is the current capacity of the warehouse?","o":[["A","15%"],["B","20%"],["C","80%"],["D","100%"]],"a":"(C) 80%","zh":"根據 Part 4 的獨白，倉庫目前的容量是多少？","e":"獨白明確提到：「and we're currently at 80% capacity」，故選 (C)。"}],"say":["Sarah, the freight delivery is scheduled to arrive at the loading dock by 3 PM. Is the forklift ready?","Can we move some pallets to the overflow warehouse? I need to check the shipment labels first.","Good. Our warehouse can accommodate units up to 15 feet high. Will that be enough?","Attention warehouse staff. This is a reminder about today's logistics operations. The storage unit measures 25 by 40 feet with climate-control features, perfect for our new shipment.","Make sure all forklifts are positioned near the dispatch area. Our warehouse can accommodate units up to 20 feet high, and we're currently at 80% capacity. Please check all labels on incoming inventory.","First, please note that our main storage unit measures 30 by 50 feet with climate-control systems, which is ideal for temperature-sensitive inventory. All incoming shipments must be properly labeled and recorded in our logistics database before being moved from the loading dock.","Delivery service is available from 6 AM to 8 PM on weekdays, extended from our previous schedule. This change will help us better manage the increased freight volume we've been experiencing.","Our warehouse can accommodate units up to 18 feet high, and we currently have a capacity of 500 pallets. With the recent dispatch improvements, we can now process 20% more shipments per day.","Yes, but we have a problem. The storage unit measures 20 by 30 feet with climate-control, but our current inventory is at full capacity.","That works. Delivery service is available from 8 AM to 6 PM today, so we have time for the dispatch."]},"11-1":{"tree":"【Ch11-1 品質管理與產品開發 Quality Management & Product Development】\n │\n ├── 🔴 S - Situation (情境確認：產品未通過品檢)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 發現產品缺陷、樣品批次不合格、出現合規問題\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **failed quality control check** (未通過品管), **defects** (缺陷), **sample batch** (樣品批次)\n │    ├── 📊 缺陷比例 ── **15% of units** (智慧型手機缺陷率) / **20% of samples** (樣品缺陷影響率)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── Lisa, the product failed the quality control check... / The product failed due to defects...\n │\n ├── 📋 T - Task (任務說明：核對技術規格)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 檢查檢驗報告、審查技術規格、找出原型機充電問題\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **inspection report** (檢驗報告), **specification** (規格), **prototype** (原型)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── What did the inspection report say? / The specification doesn't match our criteria...\n │\n ├── 💡 A - Action (行動方案：指示產品召回)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 啟動驗證流程、立即召回不安全產品、檢查客戶回饋\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **recall products** (召回產品), **validation process** (驗證程序), **customer feedback** (客戶反饋)\n │    ├── 🔢 召回數量 ── **Approximately 500 units** (上週已出貨之產品)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── We need to recall products immediately... / Have you checked customer feedback?\n │\n └── ✅ R - Result (結果確認：匯報好評與會議安排)\n      ├── 溝通目標 ── 確認客戶滿意設計（相機與UI），安排明日及下週一會議\n      ├── 核心字彙 ── **largely positive** (大多正面), **comprehensive review** (全面檢討), **validation criteria** (驗證標準)\n      ├── ⏰ 時間時程 ── **tomorrow** (討論驗證標準) / **Friday end of day** (提交測試報告) / **next Monday** (全面審查)\n      └── 必考句型 ── Customer reviews have been largely positive... / Let's schedule another review meeting tomorrow...","quiz":[{"q":"Because the latest production run ________ the strict safety and power consumption guidelines, all shipped units must be recalled immediately.","o":[["A","adhered to"],["B","complied with"],["C","violated"],["D","validated"]],"a":"(C) violated","zh":"由於最新一期的產品違反了嚴格的安全與耗電量指南，所有已出貨的單位必須立即召回。","e":"此題考查動詞詞義。根據講義，產品「未通過品質檢查（failed quality control check）」，意即「不合規（non-compliance）」或「違反（violated）安全指南」，因此必須召回。其餘選項皆表示合規，與 recall 語境相反。"},{"q":"The QA team reported that battery performance defects affect exactly ________ of the smartphone units from last week's batch.","o":[["A","20 percent"],["B","15 percent"],["C","50 percent"],["D","40 percent"]],"a":"(B) 15 percent","zh":"品保團隊回報，電池性能缺陷確切影響了上週批次中百分之十五的智慧型手機。","e":"此處考查精確數據與對象配對。David Martinez 經理的報告（Part 7）指出手機缺陷率為 15% of units；而工廠廣播（Part 4）提到的則是 20% of samples。題目問的是智慧型手機（smartphone units），故選 (B)。"},{"q":"In the internal memo, David Martinez states that the quality issue was caused by a faulty component sourced from a ________.","o":[["A","customer service department"],["B","design validation team"],["C","third-party supplier"],["D","regulatory inspection agency"]],"a":"(C) third-party supplier","zh":"在內部備忘錄中，David Martinez 指出品質問題是由從第三方供應商處採購的缺陷零件所引起的。","e":"細節理解題。備忘錄中明確指出「these issues stem from a supplier's component that doesn't match our criteria」（這些問題源自於不符標準的供應商零件），supplier 對應 third-party supplier，故選 (C)。"},{"q":"All quality control supervisors are required to submit their sample testing reports no later than ________.","o":[["A","tomorrow afternoon"],["B","next Monday morning"],["C","Friday by end of day"],["D","yesterday evening"]],"a":"(C) Friday by end of day","zh":"所有品質控制主管被要求最晚在週五下班前提交他們的樣品測試報告。","e":"時間截點題。報告提交的期限是 by end of day Friday（週五下班前）；而下週一（next Monday）是進行全面審查的會議時間，不可混淆。故選 (C)。"},{"q":"Which of the following parts of the smartphone received largely positive feedback in customer reviews?","o":[["A","Battery life and charging speed"],["B","Camera quality and user interface"],["C","Safety standards and thickness"],["D","Outer casing and component durability"]],"a":"(B) Camera quality and user interface","zh":"智慧型手機的下列哪一部分在客戶評價中獲得了大多正面的反饋？","e":"細節定位題。根據備忘錄，客戶好評的具體內容是「the phone's camera quality and user interface」（手機相機品質與使用者介面），故選 (B)。"}],"say":["Lisa, the product failed the quality control check...","The product failed due to defects...","What did the inspection report say?","The specification doesn't match our criteria...","We need to recall products immediately...","Have you checked customer feedback?","Customer reviews have been largely positive...","Let's schedule another review meeting tomorrow..."]},"11-2":{"tree":"【Ch11-2 設備與材料管理 Equipment & Materials Management】\n │\n ├── 🔴 S - Situation (情境確認：機器運轉緩慢與故障)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 掌握設備異常、停機時間增加、零件等待延遲\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **isn't running as fast** (運轉不夠快), **malfunction** (故障), **downtime** (停機時間)\n │    └── 📊 停機時數 ── 本週因故障已導致 **eight hours of downtime**\n │\n ├── 📋 T - Task (任務說明：監控庫存與安排維護)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 檢查常規維護時間、核對備用零件庫存、準備設備更換\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **last maintenance** (上次維護), **spare components** (備件), **inventory gets low** (庫存變低)\n │    └── ⏰ 延遲時間 ── 因等待材料，導致維修 **delayed by two weeks**\n │\n ├── 💡 A - Action (行動方案：更換為自動化與採購優化)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 啟動自動化更換、精簡原料採購、改採多重供應商策略\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **automated system** (自動化系統), **streamline procurement** (精簡採購), **sourcing** (採購部門)\n │    └── 🔄 採購變更 ── **multiple suppliers** (多個供應商) ➔ 取代 **single provider** (單一提供者)\n │\n └── ✅ R - Result (結果確認：升級成效與專案啟動)\n      ├── 溝通目標 ── 實現效率提升、確認十月啟動日期並提供完整培訓\n      ├── 核心字彙 ── **efficiency increase by 40%** (效率提升40%), **full training** (完整培訓)\n      └── 📅 專案時間 ── 更換專案正式開始於 **October 1st** (下個月開始準備)","quiz":[{"q":"According to Tom, the repair of the malfunctioning machine is currently on hold because ________.","o":[["A","the maintenance check has been cancelled"],["B","the necessary spare parts from the supplier have not arrived yet"],["C","the team is waiting for the operations director's approval"],["D","the automated system is being installed today"]],"a":"(B) the necessary spare parts from the supplier have not arrived yet","zh":"根據 Tom，故障機器的維修目前被擱置，因為來自供應商的必要備用零件尚未抵達。","e":"細節定位題。Tom（Part 3）指出「we're waiting on materials from the supplier... The spare components haven't arrived」（正在等待供應商材料，備件尚未寄達），故選 (B)。"},{"q":"The operations manager noted that the equipment malfunction resulted in ________ of non-productive downtime during this week.","o":[["A","2 hours"],["B","2 weeks"],["C","8 hours"],["D","40 hours"]],"a":"(C) 8 hours","zh":"營運經理指出，設備故障導致本週內有八小時的非生產性停機時間。","e":"數據配對題。廣播（Part 4）中明確提及「The malfunction has resulted in eight hours of downtime this week」（故障導致本週八小時停機），故選 (C)。"},{"q":"In the memo to department heads, Michael Brown states that the new automated equipment will improve efficiency by ________.","o":[["A","15 percent"],["B","20 percent"],["C","30 percent"],["D","40 percent"]],"a":"(D) 40 percent","zh":"在給部門主管的備忘錄中，Michael Brown 指出新的自動化設備將提高百分之四十的效率。","e":"細節定位題。備忘錄（Part 7）中指出「improve efficiency by 40%」，對應選項 (D)。"},{"q":"To prevent future raw material procurement delays, the company’s new strategy is to ________.","o":[["A","rely on a single, trusted local supplier"],["B","reduce the overall production quota"],["C","source materials from multiple providers"],["D","eliminate the need for spare components in inventory"]],"a":"(C) source materials from multiple providers","zh":"為了防止未來的原料採購延誤，公司的新策略是從多個供應商處採購材料。","e":"同義代換題。備忘錄中提到「work with multiple suppliers rather than relying on a single provider」（與多個供應商合作而非依賴單一供應商），multiple suppliers 代換為 multiple providers，故選 (C)。"},{"q":"When is the equipment replacement project officially scheduled to commence?","o":[["A","Next Friday afternoon"],["B","On September 8"],["C","On October 1st"],["D","Sometime next month"]],"a":"(C) On October 1st","zh":"設備更換專案正式安排在何時開始？","e":"專案啟動日期定位。備忘錄結尾指出「The replacement project will begin October 1st」，對應選項 (C)。(D) Sometime next month 是廣播（9月8日發布）中對10月1日的模糊時間指代，但題目要求精確日期，故 (C) 為最優解。"}],"say":["Tom, the machine isn't running as fast as it should.","That's causing too much downtime.","Can you contact sourcing about getting a replacement?","Good afternoon, operations team.","It's time to replace the equipment with an automated system to prevent future issues.","To: All Department Heads | From: Michael Brown, Operations Director | Subject: Equipment Replacement and Materials Management","After careful consideration, it's time to replace the equipment with an automated system.","Additionally, raw materials procurement needs to be streamlined to prevent future delays.","The replacement project will begin October 1st."]},"11-3":{"tree":"【Ch11-3 生產規劃與執行 Production Planning & Execution】\n │\n ├── 🔴 S - Situation (情境確認：生產進度嚴重落後)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 掌握生產線落後、工廠產能飽和狀況\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **behind schedule** (進度落後), **assembly line** (組裝線), **full capacity** (滿載)\n │    └── 📅 延遲天數 ── **behind by 3 days** (Part 3) ➔ **2 days** (Part 4) ➔ **5 days** (Part 7) *惡化趨勢\n │\n ├── 📋 T - Task (任務說明：季度配額與截止期限)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 確立季度配額指標、趕上各階段截止時間\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **meet deadline** (趕上期限), **projected quotas** (預計配額), **output figures** (產出數據)\n │    └── 🎯 季度配額 ── **5,000 units** (Part 3) ➔ **8,000 units** (Part 4) ➔ **12,000 units** (Part 7) *任務增加\n │\n ├── 💡 A - Action (行動方案：增加夜班與工作流程優化)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 實施增班措施（增設夜班）、優化工作流、提升產能\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **add another shift** (增班), **night shift** (夜班), **boost capacity** (提升產能)\n │    └── 🕛 班次時段 ── 安排夜班時間為 **6 PM to 2 AM** (Part 7)\n │\n └── ✅ R - Result (結果確認：達成率檢視與預測提交)\n      ├── 溝通目標 ── 監控每日數據、提交預測、達成季度目標\n      ├── 核心字彙 ── **submit projections** (提交預測), **monitor progress** (監控進度), **workflow** (工作流程)\n      ├── 📊 達成比例 ── 目前處於 **68%** (Part 7) ➔ **75%** (Part 3) ➔ **80% of target** (Part 4) *逐步改善\n      └── ⏰ 報告期限 ── 主管必須在 **by Friday** 之前提交最新的速率預測","quiz":[{"q":"According to the latest Q3 review in the memo, the primary assembly line is currently experiencing a delay of ________.","o":[["A","two days"],["B","three days"],["C","five days"],["D","next Friday"]],"a":"(C) five days","zh":"根據備忘錄中最新的第三季審查，主要組裝線目前正經歷五天的延誤。","e":"此處為多重文章數字陷阱題。對話中提到落後 3 天，廣播提到落後 2 天，但備忘錄（The Memo - Part 7）中明確寫道「behind by five days on our main assembly line」，故答案為 (C)。"},{"q":"What is the total projected quota for this quarter across all product lines as specified in Jennifer Chen’s memo?","o":[["A","5,000 units"],["B","8,000 units"],["C","12,000 units"],["D","15,000 units"]],"a":"(C) 12,000 units","zh":"在 Jennifer Chen 的備忘錄中，所有產品線本季的總預估配額是多少？","e":"細節定位題。請注意題目限制「in Jennifer Chen’s memo」，備忘錄中指出配額為 12,000 units，故選 (C)。(A) 是對話中的數據，(B) 是廣播中的數據。"},{"q":"To resolve the production delays and boost capacity, the plant will immediately implement an additional shift during which hours?","o":[["A","From 9 AM to 5 PM"],["B","From 6 PM to 2 AM"],["C","From midnight to 8 AM"],["D","Sometime next Friday"]],"a":"(B) From 6 PM to 2 AM","zh":"為了理清生產延誤並提升產能，工廠將立即在哪些時間段實施額外的班次？","e":"時間細節定位題。根據備忘錄（Part 7）「Add an additional shift from 6 PM to 2 AM」，故選 (B)。"},{"q":"Currently, the production efficiency is at its lowest recorded level of ________ of the target in the quarterly update memo.","o":[["A","80%"],["B","75%"],["C","68%"],["D","85%"]],"a":"(C) 68%","zh":"目前，季度更新備忘錄中記錄的生產效率處於其最低水平，僅達到目標的百分之六十八。","e":"數字對比題。對話中達成率為 75%，廣播為 80%，而更新備忘錄（Part 7）中指明「we're at 68% of target」，為三者中最低，故選 (C)。"},{"q":"In the memo, what are production supervisors required to submit to Jennifer Chen by Friday?","o":[["A","Operational budget modifications"],["B","Updated rate projections"],["C","Shift coverage requests"],["D","Supplier component validation sheets"]],"a":"(B) Updated rate projections","zh":"在備忘錄中，生產主管被要求在週五前向 Jennifer Chen 提交什麼？","e":"任務確認題。備忘錄結尾指出「Each supervisor must submit updated rate projections by Friday」，故選 (B)。"}],"say":["Mark, the production schedule shows we are behind by three days.","What about adding another shift?","Production figures indicate we're at 75% of target.","Good morning, factory team.","We need to increase the production rate to meet the deadline next Friday.","Production figures indicate we're at 80% of target, which means our output needs improvement.","To: All Production Supervisors | From: Jennifer Chen, Production Manager | Subject: Q3 Production Planning Update","We need to increase the production rate to meet the deadline for our largest client's order by month-end.","To address these challenges, we will implement the following changes immediately: Add an additional shift from 6 PM to 2 AM; Increase assembly line output by optimizing the current workflow; Monitor daily figures more closely to track progress.","Each supervisor must submit updated rate projections by Friday."]},"11-4":{"tree":"【Ch11-4 營運設施與安全 Operations Facilities & Safety】\n │\n ├── 🔴 S - Situation (情境確認：廠房產能擴建)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 宣布工廠產能擴大規劃、要求嚴格遵守安全新規程\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **expanding capacity** (擴產), **safety protocol** (安全規程), **protective eyewear** (護目鏡)\n │    └── 📊 擴建比例 ── **25%** (Part 4) ➔ **30%** (Part 3) ➔ **40% increase** (Part 7) *遞增比例\n │\n ├── 📋 T - Task (任務說明：合規檢查時程與認證要求)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 確定官方檢查時程、要求更新操作員及各部門認證\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **official inspection** (正式檢查), **compliance** (合規), **certification renewals** (認證更新)\n │    └── ⏰ 檢查日期 ── **next Monday** (Part 3) ➔ **October 15th** (Part 4) ➔ **November 20th** (Part 7) *時間遞延\n │\n ├── 💡 A - Action (行動方案：安全培訓與強制性簡報)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 舉辦強制性簡報、完成危險培訓、向團隊傳達新規\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **brief the team** (團隊簡報), **hazard training** (危險培訓), **mandatory briefing** (強制簡報)\n │    └── ⏱ 簡報時間 ── 明天 (Part 3) ➔ 安排在 **November 10th at 2 PM** (Part 7)\n │\n └── ✅ R - Result (結果確認：零容忍政策與諮詢管道)\n      ├── 溝通目標 ── 貫徹安全第一原則、對於違規零容忍、缺席簡報者暫停權限\n      ├── 核心字彙 ── **top priorities** (首要任務), **suspension of access** (暫停權限), **extension 3344** (分機3344)\n      └── 🛑 嚴重後果 ── 缺席簡報將面臨 **suspension of workplace access privileges** (進入特權被暫停)","quiz":[{"q":"During the factory expansion transition, what safety gear is listed as a mandatory requirement for all workers on the floor?","o":[["A","High-visibility vests"],["B","Steel-toed safety boots"],["C","Protective eyewear"],["D","Noise-cancelling headphones"]],"a":"(C) Protective eyewear","zh":"在工廠擴建過渡期間，什麼安全裝備被列為車間所有工人的強制性要求？","e":"細節定位題。對話、廣播和通知中均一致強調「wear protective eyewear」（配戴防護眼鏡/護目鏡），故選 (C)。"},{"q":"According to the Safety Notice written by Rachel Kim, the factory is expanding its production capacity by ________.","o":[["A","25 percent"],["B","30 percent"],["C","40 percent"],["D","50 percent"]],"a":"(C) 40 percent","zh":"根據 Rachel Kim 所撰寫的安全通知，工廠正在將其生產產能擴大百分之四十。","e":"數據對比題。題目限制「Safety Notice written by Rachel Kim」（Rachel Kim 的通知 - Part 7），該文中擴產數據為 40%，故選 (C)。(A) 是廣播數據，(B) 是對話數據。"},{"q":"When is the official compliance inspection scheduled to take place according to the plant-wide staff radio broadcast?","o":[["A","Next Monday morning"],["B","On October 15th"],["C","On November 20th"],["D","Sometime next quarter"]],"a":"(B) On October 15th","zh":"根據全廠員工廣播，官方合規檢查安排在何時進行？","e":"時間定位題。題目限制「staff radio broadcast」（員工廣播 - Part 4），廣播中宣佈的檢查日期是 October 15th，故選 (B)。(A) 是對話中的下週一，(C) 是備忘錄中的11月20日。"},{"q":"What will happen to employees who fail to attend the mandatory safety briefing scheduled for November 10th?","o":[["A","They will be fined fifty dollars."],["B","Their workplace access privileges will be suspended."],["C","They will have to complete ten days of extra training."],["D","Their contract with the supplier will be terminated."]],"a":"(B) Their workplace access privileges will be suspended.","zh":"未能參加安排在 11 月 10 日之強制性安全簡報的員工，會面臨什麼後果？","e":"後果考點定位。安全通知（Part 7）指出「Failure to attend will result in suspension of workplace access privileges」（未能參加將導致工作場所進入權限被暫停），對應 (B)。"},{"q":"If a supervisor has specific questions regarding the certification renewal requirements, they should contact the safety office at ________.","o":[["A","extension 3344"],["B","next Monday"],["C","the construction zone entrance"],["D","the main conference room"]],"a":"(A) extension 3344","zh":"如果主管對認證更新要求有具體問題，他們應該撥打什麼號碼聯絡安全辦公室？","e":"聯絡管道定位題。通知末尾指出「contact the safety office at extension 3344」，故選 (A)。"}],"say":["Susan, the factory is expanding to increase capacity by 30%.","The official inspection for compliance is scheduled for next Monday.","Workplace safety and cleanliness are our top priorities.","This safety update concerns our expansion plans.","The official inspection for compliance is scheduled for October 15th.","Workplace safety and cleanliness are our top priorities during this transition.","To: All Employees | From: Rachel Kim, Safety Director | Subject: Facility Expansion and Safety Requirements","The official inspection for compliance is scheduled for November 20th.","Please attend the mandatory safety briefing on November 10th at 2 PM in the main conference room.","Workplace safety and cleanliness are our top priorities throughout this expansion."]},"11-5":{"tree":"【Ch11-5 成本效益與產品上市 Cost Efficiency & Product Launch】\n │\n ├── 🔴 S - Situation (情境確認：生產成本激增)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 評估原料上漲引起的成本壓力、確保季度利潤率指標\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **costs increased** (成本增加), **profit margin** (利潤率), **total investment** (總投資)\n │    ├── 📈 成本增幅 ── **15%** (Part 3) ➔ **18%** (Part 7) ➔ **20%** (Part 4) *遞增趨勢\n │    └── 💰 投資金額 ── 董事會核准之總投資為 **$5 million total investment** (Part 7)\n │\n ├── 📋 T - Task (任務說明：預算編列與行銷核心焦點)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 劃分推廣及廣告預算、確立行銷活動核心宣傳重點\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **marketing campaign** (行銷活動), **promotion budget** (推廣預算), **advertising costs** (廣告費用)\n │    ├── 💵 預算分配 ── **$2 million advertising** (Part 4) / **$1.5 million promotion** (Part 7, 廣告佔 60%)\n │    └── 🎯 行銷焦點 ── **efficiency** (對話聚焦) ➔ **innovative design** (廣播聚焦) ➔ **sustainability** (閱讀聚焦)\n │\n ├── 💡 A - Action (行動方案：新進同仁培訓與招募)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 招募新血支援產品上市、實施新進同仁培訓課程\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **additional staff** (額外員工), **training program** (培訓計畫)\n │    ├── 👥 招募人數 ── 預計招募 **50 additional staff** (Part 7)\n │    └── ⏱ 培訓天數 ── **3 days** (Part 4) ➔ **10 days** (Part 7) ➔ **2 weeks** (Part 3) *天數差異\n │\n └── ✅ R - Result (結果確認：預購開始與上市發布時程)\n      ├── 溝通目標 ── 召開策略簡報會、開放前置預購、鎖定正式發布日期\n      ├── 核心字彙 ── **pre-orders** (預購), **official release** (正式發布), **strategy briefing** (策略簡報)\n      └── 📅 關鍵時程 ── **April 20th 10 AM** (簡報會) ➔ **June 1st** (預購開始) ➔ **July 15th** (正式發布)","quiz":[{"q":"According to Chief Marketing Officer Linda Chen’s announcement, production costs have increased by ________ due to raw material fluctuations.","o":[["A","15 percent"],["B","18 percent"],["C","20 percent"],["D","60 percent"]],"a":"(B) 18 percent","zh":"根據行銷長 Linda Chen 的公告，由於原料價格波動，生產成本已增加了百分之十八。","e":"數字配對定位題。題目指定「Linda Chen’s announcement」（Linda Chen 的公告 - Part 7），文中成本增幅為 18%，故選 (B)。(A) 是對話數據，(C) 是廣播數據，(D) 是廣告費用佔比。"},{"q":"How much total investment did the board of directors approve for the upcoming product launch?","o":[["A","$1.5 million"],["B","$2 million"],["C","$5 million"],["D","$1.8 million"]],"a":"(C) $5 million","zh":"董事會為即將到來的產品上市核准了多少總投資額？","e":"預算金額定位題。公告中明確指出「The board has approved a total investment of $5 million for this launch」，故選 (C)。(A) 是推廣預算，(B) 是廣告預算。"},{"q":"In the printed promotional materials to be mailed to clients, what specific product feature will the marketing campaign focus on according to Linda Chen’s memo?","o":[["A","High operating speed"],["B","Sustainability features"],["C","Innovative design"],["D","Advanced battery life"]],"a":"(B) Sustainability features","zh":"根據 Linda Chen 的備忘錄，在寄送給客戶的印刷推廣材料中，行銷活動將聚焦於什麼特定的產品特色？","e":"行銷焦點代換題。備忘錄中明確聲明「The marketing campaign will focus on sustainability features」，故選 (B)。(C) 是廣播中強調的設計。"},{"q":"The training program for the 50 newly hired employees is officially scheduled to take ________.","o":[["A","three days"],["B","ten days"],["C","two weeks"],["D","one month"]],"a":"(B) ten days","zh":"針對 50 名新招募員工的培訓計畫，官方安排需要花費多少天？","e":"培訓天數對比題。備忘錄（Part 7）指出新聘員工為 50 人，且「The training program for new employees takes ten days」，故選 (B)。(A) 是廣播中提及的天數，(C) 是對話中提及的天數。"},{"q":"When are the advance pre-orders for the new product line scheduled to begin?","o":[["A","On April 20th"],["B","On June 1st"],["C","On July 15th"],["D","Sometime next week"]],"a":"(B) On June 1st","zh":"新產品線的提前預購安排在何時開始？","e":"預購日期定位。公告指出「pre-orders beginning June 1st」，故選 (B)。(A) 是簡報會日期，(C) 是正式發布日期。"}],"say":["Robert, production costs have increased by 15% this quarter.","The marketing campaign will focus on efficiency features.","The market conditions are challenging, but this launch is crucial.","Let me update you on our product launch plans.","The marketing campaign will focus on innovative design to justify our investment.","The promotion strategy emphasizes efficiency and market leadership.","To: All Marketing and Sales Staff | From: Linda Chen, Chief Marketing Officer | Subject: Product Launch Strategy and Cost Management","We're launching a new product line next quarter, specifically in July.","The training program for new employees takes ten days, and we're hiring 50 additional staff to support the launch.","The expected release date is July 15th, with pre-orders beginning June 1st."]},"12-1":{"tree":"【Ch12-1 訂位與用餐體驗 Reservations & Dining Experience】\n │\n ├── 🔴 S - Situation (情境確認：提出訂位需求)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 確認用餐人數、日期時段與氛圍偏好\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **secure a table** (訂位), **booth** (雅座), **intimate ambiance** (親密氛圍), **peak hours** (尖峰時段)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── \"I'd like to secure a table for six guests next Friday around 7 PM.\"\n │\n ├── 📋 T - Task (任務說明：核對座位狀態)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 說明主用餐區、私人包廂之座位安排與客滿衝突\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **availability** (空位), **main dining area** (主用餐區), **private dining section** (私人包廂區), **full capacity** (客滿)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── \"Unfortunately, all our booths are reserved during peak hours.\"\n │\n ├── 💡 A - Action (行動方案：提供替代座位與時效促銷)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 討論露天座位與天氣因素、提供深夜時段、推出餐酒特惠\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **patio seating** (露天座), **earliest availability** (最早空位), **seasonal wine pairing** (季節餐酒搭配)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── \"The patio is available, but Friday's weather forecast shows possible rain.\"\n │\n └── ✅ R - Result (結果確認：登記候補或確認更改)\n      ├── 溝通目標 ── 加入等候名單以防有人取消、提供回電號碼\n      ├── 核心字彙 ── **waiting list** (等候名單), **cancellation** (取消), **pre-select** (預先選擇)\n      └── 必考句型 ── \"Could you put us on the waiting list for 7 PM in case there's a cancellation?\"","quiz":[{"q":"Because the main dining room has reached full _______ tonight, the host is offering patio seating as an alternative.","o":[["A","capacity"],["B","extension"],["C","compilation"],["D","subscription"]],"a":"(A) capacity","zh":"因為今天晚上主用餐區已經達到**客滿（容納極限）**，領班正在提供露天座位作為替代方案。","e":"此處考查專有名詞搭配。reach full capacity 意為「客滿、達到最大容量」，與講義中 main dining room reached full capacity 完美契合，故選 (A)。"},{"q":"If you would like to secure an indoor booth next Saturday during peak hours, we highly recommend making a _______ at least one week in advance.","o":[["A","reservation"],["B","modification"],["C","cancellation"],["D","prescription"]],"a":"(A) reservation","zh":"如果您想在下週六尖峰時段預訂一個室內雅座，我們強烈建議至少提前一週進行**預約（訂位）**。","e":"在訂位場景中，為了確保有座位（secure an indoor booth），必須提前進行 reservation（預訂），故選 (A)。"},{"q":"According to the catering proposal email, if the client requests for GreenLeaf's completely vegan option, this will represent _______ of the total company lunch offerings.","o":[["A","40%"],["B","30%"],["C","20%"],["D","10%"]],"a":"(C) 20%","zh":"根據外燴提案電子郵件，如果客戶要求 GreenLeaf 的完全純素選項，這將佔整個公司午餐供應量的**百分之二十**。","e":"此題為經典的多益「計算推理」陷阱。提案指出素食比例佔 40%（40% vegetarian），而純素是素食者的一半（half of those completely vegan）。因此，純素比例為：40%  0.5 = 20%，故選 (C)。"},{"q":"The outdoor _______ area is highly popular among regular diners for its lovely garden view, although it is subject to weather conditions.","o":[["A","patio"],["B","basement"],["C","lobby"],["D","pantry"]],"a":"(A) patio","zh":"戶外**露天區（庭院）**因其美麗的花園景致而在常客中非常受歡迎，儘管它容易受到天氣狀況的影響。","e":"對照同義代換與座位描述：outdoor area = patio（露天平台/庭院），且其後面提及天氣因素（subject to weather conditions），最符合的即是 (A)。"},{"q":"In the restaurant's promotional flyer, the word \"patrons\" is closest in meaning to _______.","o":[["A","employees"],["B","supervisors"],["C","customers"],["D","suppliers"]],"a":"(C) customers","zh":"在餐廳的宣傳單中，\"patrons\" 一字與下列何者意思最接近？","e":"根據講義與 Paraphrase 對照：patrons = customers = diners（顧客、用餐者），故選 (C)。"}],"say":["I'd like to secure a table for six guests next Friday around 7 PM.","Unfortunately, all our booths are reserved during peak hours.","The patio is available, but Friday's weather forecast shows possible rain.","Could you put us on the waiting list for 7 PM in case there's a cancellation?","Welcome to The Sterling Bistro.","Let me check our availability for next Friday.","Hmm, what about the patio seating?","That's quite late for some of our patrons.","Hello, this is Marcus Chen, the host at Bellacosta Restaurant.","...but we've reserved an excellent table for you in our newly renovated private dining section.","We can easily accommodate any special dietary requirements your guests may have.","Please call us back at 555-0142 if you need to make any changes to your reservation or if you'd like us to pre-select wines for your meal.","Chen, Thank you for contacting GreenLeaf Catering regarding your upcoming company event on April 25.","Regarding your question about customizable options, we can set up a build-your-own salad station where employees can select their preferred toppings and dressings.","For guests requiring gluten-free options, we'll provide quinoa-based dishes and rice paper wraps as substitutes for traditional bread items.","Are there any plant-based alternatives available for this entrée that you'd particularly like us to include?"]},"12-2":{"tree":"【Ch12-2 點餐與飲食需求 Ordering & Dietary Requirements】\n │\n ├── 🔴 S - Situation (情境確認：說明飲食限制)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 詢問無麩質、素食與去乳製品(去奶油)之菜餚\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **dietary restrictions** (飲食限制), **gluten-free** (無麩質), **vegetarian** (素食), **dairy products** (乳製品)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── \"I have a few questions about dietary restrictions. I'm looking for something gluten-free.\"\n │\n ├── 📋 T - Task (任務說明：確認食材原料)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 推薦烤鮭魚、客製化穀物碗等安全選項\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **customizable grain bowl** (客製化穀物碗), **portion size** (份量), **shellfish** (甲殼類過敏)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── \"For vegetarian options, we have a customizable grain bowl where you can choose toppings.\"\n │\n ├── 💡 A - Action (行動方案：進行客製替換)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 提出配菜替換、醬汁分開、不額外收費服務\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **substitute** (替換), **dressing served separately** (醬汁分開裝), **no extra charge** (不加收費用)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── \"Would it be possible to have the dressing served separately? Can we substitute mashed potatoes?\"\n │\n └── ✅ R - Result (結果確認：索取資訊與預告新菜單)\n      ├── 溝通目標 ── 索取營養指南以追蹤卡路里、預告下週推出季節菜單\n      ├── 核心字彙 ── **nutritional information** (營養資訊), **allergen information** (過敏原資訊), **seasonal menu** (季節菜單)\n      └── 必考句型 ── \"I'll bring you our detailed nutrition guide that lists all ingredients and allergen information.\"","quiz":[{"q":"According to the conversation, the man asks for the dressing to be served _______ so his colleague can control her calorie intake.","o":[["A","separately"],["B","immediately"],["C","internally"],["D","temporarily"]],"a":"(A) separately","zh":"根據對話，男子要求將沙拉醬**分開（單獨地）**供應，以便他的同事能夠控制卡路里的攝取。","e":"此處考查副詞搭配。對話原句為 have the dressing served separately ➔ 在旁邊（on the side），故 (A) 爲正確答案。其他選項如 (B) 立即地、(C) 內部地、(D) 暫時地 皆不符合。"},{"q":"The restaurant provides a detailed nutrition guide for customers who follow a special diet and need to _______ their daily calories.","o":[["A","expand"],["B","track"],["C","ignore"],["D","skip"]],"a":"(B) track","zh":"該餐廳為遵循特殊飲食且需要**記錄（追蹤）**每日卡路里的顧客提供詳細的營養指南。","e":"對照講義中「特殊飲食」常搭配的概念：need to track calories（追蹤卡路里），故選 (B)。"},{"q":"Due to an unexpected shipment delay of shellfish, Chef Rodriguez announced that they are currently _______ to serve three of their regular dishes.","o":[["A","available"],["B","hesitant"],["C","unable"],["D","delighted"]],"a":"(C) unable","zh":"由於意料之外的甲殼類海鮮配送延誤，主廚 Rodriguez 宣布他們目前**無法**供應三道常規菜餚。","e":"根據 Part 4 聽力原句 unable to serve three of our regular dishes，代表菜色目前缺貨不可用（unavailable），故選 (C) unable。"},{"q":"Customers who order the grilled salmon can replace the mashed potatoes with steamed rice or roasted vegetables at _______ extra charge.","o":[["A","no"],["B","any"],["C","much"],["D","some"]],"a":"(A) no","zh":"點烤鮭魚的顧客可以將馬鈴薯泥免費（**不需**額外收費地）更換為蒸米飯或烤蔬菜。","e":"固定片語考點。at no extra charge 代表「免費（at no additional cost）」，(A) 爲唯一正確搭配。"},{"q":"To accommodate diners with food allergies, the kitchen has prepared detailed charts listing all _______ used in every dish.","o":[["A","documents"],["B","ingredients"],["C","instruments"],["D","advertisements"]],"a":"(B) ingredients","zh":"為了配合對食物過敏的用餐者，廚房準備了詳細的圖表，列出了每道菜中所使用的所有**食材（成分）**。","e":"在飲食過敏原確認場景中，列出的必須是菜餚的「食材/成分（ingredients）」，故選 (B)。"}],"say":["I have a few questions about dietary restrictions. I'm looking for something gluten-free.","For vegetarian options, we have a customizable grain bowl where you can choose toppings.","Would it be possible to have the dressing served separately? Can we substitute mashed potatoes?","I'll bring you our detailed nutrition guide that lists all ingredients and allergen information.","I'm ready to take your order.","Our grilled salmon with vegetables is naturally gluten-free, and we can easily prepare it without butter.","Would it be possible to have the dressing served separately?","Oh, one more thing - do you have the nutritional information available?","This is Chef Rodriguez with an important update about tonight's special menu.","However, we've prepared some excellent plant-based alternatives that I'm excited to share with you.","...and we're offering a 15% discount on all customizable salads tonight.","We have detailed charts listing all ingredients in our dishes."]},"12-3":{"tree":"【Ch12-3 行銷與外送服務 Marketing & Delivery Services】\n │\n ├── 🔴 S - Situation (情境確認：了解外燴需求)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 詢問 20 人或 200 人的企業活動外燴細節與客製套餐\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **catering services** (外燴服務), **corporate event** (企業活動), **bulk order** (大量訂購)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── \"I'm calling about catering services for our corporate event next Friday.\"\n │\n ├── 📋 T - Task (任務說明：提供計費與配送範圍)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 介紹基礎起價、大宗報價、擴大外送半徑、免運與佈置服務\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **corporate packages** (企業套餐), **delivery radius** (外送半徑), **waive delivery fee** (免除運費)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── \"Our corporate packages start at $300 for groups of 15 or more, delivery fee waived.\"\n │\n ├── 💡 A - Action (行動方案：說明促銷條件與福利)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 詳述中午前下訂當日送達、滿 $500 折 25%、贈送新客戶折扣券\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **before noon** (中午前限制), **same-day delivery** (當日送達), **discount coupons** (折扣券)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── \"Orders placed before noon qualify for same-day delivery service.\"\n │\n └── ✅ R - Result (結果確認：會員積分與促銷確認截止)\n      ├── 溝通目標 ── 透過 App 賺取雙倍積分、訂立 5/30 前必須回信確認之期限\n      ├── 核心字彙 ── **double points** (雙倍積分), **mobile app** (手機程式), **confirm by** (截止日限制)\n      └── 必考句型 ── \"Please confirm by May 30 to secure this promotional offer.\"","quiz":[{"q":"According to the catering proposal letter, what is the deadline for TechCorp to accept the promotional offer?","o":[["A","April 10"],["B","May 22"],["C","May 30"],["D","June 15"]],"a":"(C) May 30","zh":"根據外燴提案信，TechCorp 接受促銷優惠的截止日期是哪一天？","e":"此處考查時間截止日的配對。信件原句為 Please confirm by May 30 to secure this promotional offer，故 (C) 爲唯一正確答案。(D) June 15 是活動舉辦日期，是典型時間干擾陷阱。"},{"q":"Under the current promotional rules at Romano's Restaurant, how can regular members earn double reward points?","o":[["A","By ordering via the mobile app"],["B","By reserving a private dining section"],["C","By purchasing gift vouchers in bulk"],["D","By dining on Tuesday morning"]],"a":"(A) By ordering via the mobile app","zh":"根據 Romano's 餐廳目前的促銷規則，一般會員如何賺取雙倍獎勵積分？","e":"對照 Part 3 對白原句 Members earn double points on purchases made through our mobile app，故選 (A)。"},{"q":"An corporate event planner who places a bulk order of $600 this week at Romano's Restaurant will qualify for a _______ discount.","o":[["A","15%"],["B","20%"],["C","25%"],["D","30%"]],"a":"(C) 25%","zh":"本週在 Romano's 餐廳下單 600 美元大宗訂單的企業活動策劃人，將有資格獲得**百分之二十五**的折扣。","e":"根據 Part 4 廣告公告：Corporate events booking catering services this week get 25% off bulk orders over $500。因 600 美元超過了 500 美元的門檻，故符合 25% 折扣，選 (C)。"},{"q":"In the catering proposal, Delicious Bites agrees to waive the delivery fee and provide _______ service at no additional cost.","o":[["A","installation"],["B","maintenance"],["C","setup"],["D","training"]],"a":"(C) setup","zh":"在外燴提案中，Delicious Bites 同意免除外送費，並提供免費的**現場佈置（擺盤）**服務。","e":"根據信中 T 段的原句：delivery fee waived, and setup service within our expanded delivery radius，故選 (C) setup。"},{"q":"In the operational document, the phrase \"bulk order\" is closest in meaning to which of the following?","o":[["A","required amount"],["B","large order"],["C","to-go order"],["D","standard package"]],"a":"(B) large order","zh":"在營運文件中，短語 \"bulk order\"（大量訂購）與下列哪個選項的意思最接近？","e":"根據 Paraphrase 同義代換表：bulk order = large order = volume purchase。故 (B) 爲最精準代換。"}],"say":["I'm calling about catering services for our corporate event next Friday.","Our corporate packages start at $300 for groups of 15 or more, delivery fee waived.","Orders placed before noon qualify for same-day delivery service.","Please confirm by May 30 to secure this promotional offer.","Good afternoon, I'm calling about catering services for our corporate event next Friday.","This includes our seasonal menu items and free delivery within our delivery radius.","Orders placed before noon qualify for same-day delivery service, plus you'll receive a 20% discount coupon for your next bulk order.","Do you have a loyalty program for regular customers?","Romano's Restaurant is launching an exciting marketing campaign this month.","Order any seasonal menu item and receive a free dessert with no delivery fee.","Corporate events booking catering services this week get 25% off bulk orders over $500.","Customer feedback shows we're the city's favorite Italian restaurant.","Mitchell, Thank you for considering Delicious Bites for your corporate event on June 15.","Our corporate packages start at $300 for groups of 15 or more, but for your bulk order, we're offering special pricing at $2,800 total.","Orders placed before noon qualify for same-day delivery service, though your advance booking ensures priority scheduling.","Members earn double points on purchases made through our mobile app, which I encourage you to download."]},"12-4":{"tree":"【Ch12-4 餐廳營運管理 Restaurant Operations】\n │\n ├── 🔴 S - Situation (情境確認：突發設備故障)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 召集緊急會議說明洗碗機報廢、手動洗碗應變\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **broke down** (故障), **can't be repaired** (無法修理), **urgent staff meeting** (緊急會議)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── \"Our dishwasher broke down and needs immediate replacement.\"\n │\n ├── 📋 T - Task (任務說明：到貨與排班重組)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 確認週四到貨、農產品清晨送貨、調整手洗班表、穿著舊制服因應粉塵\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **adjusted the scheduling** (調整排班), **dinner shift** (晚班), **wear old uniforms** (穿舊制服)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── \"The shipment is scheduled for Thursday. Dinner shift staff should wear old uniforms.\"\n │\n ├── 💡 A - Action (行動方案：強制會議與衛生認證)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 召集週一 3 點強制會議、週五前完成衛生認證以合規\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **hygiene certification** (衛生認證), **mandatory meeting** (強制會議), **food safety** (食品安全)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── \"Each team member needs to complete the updated hygiene certification by Friday.\"\n │\n └── ✅ R - Result (結果確認：新輪班表生效與聯絡管道)\n      ├── 溝通目標 ── 新班表週一早上生效、提供問題諮詢分機 342\n      ├── 核心字彙 ── **take effect** (生效), **rotation schedule** (輪班表), **extension 342** (分機 342)\n      └── 必考句型 ── \"The new rotation schedule will take effect starting Monday morning.\"","quiz":[{"q":"According to Manager Lopez, why will the restaurant open later than usual on Tuesday?","o":[["A","To install a replacement dishwasher"],["B","To conduct an inventory audit"],["C","To hold a mandatory safety training"],["D","To waiting for a produce delivery"]],"a":"(B) To conduct an inventory audit","zh":"根據經理 Lopez，餐廳週二為什麼會比平時晚開門？","e":"此處考查營運原因。獨白中明確提到 Tuesday we're conducting an inventory audit, so we'll adjust operational hours - opening at noon。因此，晚開門是因為要進行「庫存審核/盤點」，選 (B)。"},{"q":"Why are the dinner shift employees advised to wear old uniforms on Wednesday evening?","o":[["A","The new uniform shipment has been delayed."],["B","They will be assisting with manual vegetable washing."],["C","Kitchen equipment installation will create dust."],["D","The staff laundry facility is undergoing maintenance."]],"a":"(C) Kitchen equipment installation will create dust.","zh":"為什麼建議週三晚班的員工在晚上穿舊制服？","e":"此處考查細節原因。Lopez 經理在留言中指出：maintenance crew installs new equipment Wednesday evening, so dinner shift staff should wear old uniforms due to dust。因為安裝新洗碗機會產生粉塵，故選 (C)。"},{"q":"By what day must all restaurant team members complete the updated hygiene certification?","o":[["A","Monday"],["B","Tuesday"],["C","Wednesday"],["D","Friday"]],"a":"(D) Friday","zh":"所有餐廳團隊成員必須在週幾之前完成更新的衛生認證？","e":"對照 Part 3 對白原句：Each team member needs to complete the updated hygiene certification by Friday。因此截止日為週五，選 (D)。"},{"q":"The operations director confirmed that the new digital scheduling system will _______ starting Monday morning.","o":[["A","call off"],["B","take effect"],["C","carry out"],["D","fall behind"]],"a":"(B) take effect","zh":"營運總監確認新的數位排班系統將從週一早上開始**生效（實施）**。","e":"根據同義代換與必考句型，take effect 意為「生效/開始實施」（become effective / launch），最符合題意，故選 (B)。"},{"q":"Any staff members who have concerns about the new shift rotation schedule should contact the manager at _______ 342.","o":[["A","registration"],["B","department"],["C","extension"],["D","platform"]],"a":"(C) extension","zh":"任何對新輪班表有疑慮的員工，應撥打分機 **342** 聯繫經理。","e":"固定辦公室/餐廳通訊詞彙。extension 342（分機 342），(C) 爲唯一正確搭配。"}],"say":["Our dishwasher broke down and needs immediate replacement.","The shipment is scheduled for Thursday. Dinner shift staff should wear old uniforms.","Each team member needs to complete the updated hygiene certification by Friday.","The new rotation schedule will take effect starting Monday morning.","Thanks for attending this urgent staff meeting.","The shipment is scheduled for Thursday.","How do we maintain hygiene standards during this period?","Hello team, this is Manager Lopez.","Our supplier delivers new kitchen equipment Wednesday, including a replacement dishwasher.","There's a mandatory staff meeting Monday at 3 PM to discuss these changes.","For scheduling concerns about shifts or questions about quality control procedures, contact me at extension 342."]},"12-5":{"tree":"【Ch12-5 美食教育與體驗 Culinary Education & Experience】\n │\n ├── 🔴 S - Situation (情境確認：了解活動性質)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 接待美食評論家、說明烹飪示範與品嚐會之流程\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **cooking demonstration** (廚藝示範), **food critic** (評論家), **culinary school** (學校)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── \"Welcome to the Riverside Culinary School. Are you here for tonight's cooking demonstration?\"\n │\n ├── 📋 T - Task (任務說明：介紹行政主廚與大師課)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 介紹行政主廚、大師課展示三種招牌技術、預告用餐體驗\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **executive chef** (行政主廚), **three signature techniques** (三招牌技巧), **masterclass** (大師課)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── \"Our executive chef will showcase three signature techniques during tonight's masterclass.\"\n │\n ├── 💡 A - Action (行動方案：展現核心優勢)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 詳述法亞融合手法、方圓 50 英里在地採購以支持小農與確保新鮮\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **fusion approach** (融合手法), **sourced within a 50-mile radius** (50英里採購), **local cuisine** (在地料理)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── \"This establishment earned recognition for its innovative fusion approach, correct?\"\n │\n └── ✅ R - Result (結果確認：收穫認可與推出食譜書)\n      ├── 溝通目標 ── 索取餐廳評論、確認提供免費或購買食譜書、期待用餐超出預期\n      ├── 核心字彙 ── **restaurant review** (評論), **complimentary cookbook** (免費食譜書), **exceeds expectations** (超出預期)\n      └── 必考句型 ── \"Dubois's upcoming cookbook will feature recipes from the restaurant.\"","quiz":[{"q":"According to the Part 3 conversation, what will guests receive for free after attending the cooking demonstration?","o":[["A","A discount voucher for a future meal"],["B","A complimentary cookbook with recipes"],["C","A bottle of Chef Martinez's signature wine"],["D","A ticket to next month's masterclass"]],"a":"(B) A complimentary cookbook with recipes","zh":"根據 Part 3 對話，客人在參加完烹飪示範活動後將免費獲得什麼？","e":"此處考查同義代換。對話原句為 receive a complimentary cookbook。complimentary 代換為 free（免費的），故 (B) 爲唯一正確答案。"},{"q":"In the restaurant review, the author mentions that Chef Dubois's cooking method is highly unique because it combined _______ techniques with Asian flavors.","o":[["A","Italian"],["B","French"],["C","Spanish"],["D","German"]],"a":"(B) French","zh":"在餐廳評論中，作者提到主廚 Dubois 的烹飪方法非常獨特，因為它將**法式**技巧與亞洲風味相結合。","e":"對照 Part 7 閱讀原文：combining French techniques with Asian flavors，這也是其 fusion（融合）手法的具體展現，故選 (B)。"},{"q":"In the welcome address, Susan Chen is identified as the _______ of Grandview Culinary School.","o":[["A","executive chef"],["B","director"],["C","food critic"],["D","supplier"]],"a":"(B) director","zh":"在歡迎詞中，Susan Chen 被確認是 Grandview 烹飪學校的**總監（負責人）**。","e":"此處考查人物身分辨識。歡迎詞原句為 I'm Director Susan Chen，代表她是學校負責人（director / head of school），而非主廚，選 (B)。"},{"q":"Both the cooking school and The Garden Table earned significant recognition for their commitment to locally sourced ingredients from within a _______ radius.","o":[["A","15-mile"],["B","30-mile"],["C","50-mile"],["D","150-mile"]],"a":"(C) 50-mile","zh":"烹飪學校和 The Garden Table 餐廳都因承諾從方圓**五十英里**內採購本地食材而獲得了重大認可。","e":"核對數據考點。Part 3、Part 4 和 Part 7 均一致提到 sourced within a 50-mile radius。因此 (C) 爲唯一正確數據。"},{"q":"In the restaurant review, the phrase \"exceeds expectations\" is closest in meaning to which of the following?","o":[["A","falls behind"],["B","meets standards"],["C","passes the limit"],["D","surpasses standard"]],"a":"(D) surpasses standard","zh":"在餐廳評論中，短語 \"exceeds expectations\"（超出預期）與下列哪個選項的意思最接近？","e":"根據同義代換表，exceeds expectations = surpasses standard（超越標準/表現出色），故選 (D)。"}],"say":["Welcome to the Riverside Culinary School. Are you here for tonight's cooking demonstration?","Our executive chef will showcase three signature techniques during tonight's masterclass.","This establishment earned recognition for its innovative fusion approach, correct?","Dubois's upcoming cookbook will feature recipes from the restaurant.","Welcome to the Riverside Culinary School.","Chef Martinez will prepare his award-winning dishes using fresh ingredients from our seasonal menu.","I'm particularly interested in his approach to food preparation.","Your restaurant review would mean a lot to us.","Good evening and welcome to our annual tasting event at the Grandview Culinary School.","Our executive chef will showcase three signature techniques during tonight's masterclass, followed by a special dining experience.","Silva's cookbook, featuring recipes from various cuisines, will be available for purchase.","This establishment earned recognition for its innovative fusion approach to food preparation.","The Garden Table's new executive chef, Antoine Dubois, has transformed this establishment into a must-visit destination.","The seasonal menu showcases fresh ingredients with remarkable creativity.","This establishment earned recognition for its innovative fusion approach, combining French techniques with Asian flavors.","The dining experience exceeds expectations, with impeccable service matching the exceptional food."]},"13-1":{"tree":"【Ch13-1 系統應用與設備管理：IT升級溝通 System Applications & Equipment Management】\n │\n ├── 🔴 S - Situation (情境確認：了解升級需求)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 推出增強安全功能的升級平台，使技術基礎設施現代化\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **launch** (推出), **upgraded platform** (升級平台), **enhanced security features** (增強安全功能)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── Plans to launch the upgraded platform next week. / This major system overhaul will modernize our infrastructure.\n │\n ├── 📋 T - Task (任務說明：安排設備更新與安裝)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 指示分階段安裝軟體與硬體，並回報周邊設備連線障礙\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **software installation** (軟體安裝), **peripheral devices** (周邊裝置), **cloud storage** (雲端儲存)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── We've completed the software installation on all computers. / The printer and scanner aren't connecting properly.\n │\n ├── 💡 A - Action (行動方案：分發門禁設備與網路診斷)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 部署生物識別讀取器，利用診斷工具分析多個地點之網路效能\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **biometric readers** (生物識別讀取器), **access control** (門禁控制), **diagnostic tool** (診斷工具)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── Receive new biometric readers for improved access control. / This diagnostic tool can analyze network performance.\n │\n ├── ✅ R - Result (結果確認：系統測試與資料備份)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 安排週末測試，確保所有同仁在更新開始前完成備份\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **undergo testing** (接受測試), **backup** (備份), **vendor** (廠商)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── Testing during the weekend of April 18-19. / Please ensure your teams backup critical data before the update begins.\n │\n ├── ⏰ 關鍵概念一：系統升級時間表 (Upgrade Timeline)\n │    ├── **具體日期** ── April 20 launch (4月20日正式推出) / April 18-19 (週末測試期)\n │    ├── **截止時程** ── **by Friday** (週五前收到讀取器) / **by 6 AM** (早上6點前升級完成) / **midnight tomorrow** (明天午夜開始，注意 midnight tomorrow ≠ tonight)\n │    └── **階段安排** ── 軟體安裝 ➔ 硬體更換 ➔ 週末測試 ➔ 正式推出\n │\n ├── 🔧 關鍵概念二：設備與連線故障 (Connection Issues)\n │    ├── **問題所在** ── Printers and scanners (周邊裝置) 無法正常連接至 **cloud storage**，電腦 (laptops) 則正常\n │    ├── **解題代換** ── `peripheral devices` = printer / scanner 等外部硬體\n │    └── **解決方案** ── Update device drivers (更新驅動程式) / Contact application vendor (聯繫廠商)\n │\n └── ⚠ 三大高頻防雷陷阱 (Common Traps)\n      ├── 1. 時間混淆 ── **midnight tomorrow** 是明天午夜，選項常設 **tonight** (今天晚上) 進行干擾。\n      ├── 2. 設備錯配 ── 周邊設備 (peripheral devices) 連線失敗不等於電腦或筆電 (laptops) 也斷線。\n      └── 3. 動作誤判 ── 女士 (woman) 負責「聯絡廠商 (contact vendor)」，男士 (man) 負責「準備備份與執行測試」。","quiz":[{"q":"Due to the upcoming major ________, all employee workstations will undergo extensive software updates on Friday night.","o":[["A","limitation"],["B","overhaul"],["C","certification"],["D","evaluation"]],"a":"(B) overhaul","zh":"由於即將進行的大型系統改造，所有員工工作站將在週五晚上接受全面的軟體更新。","e":"情境為系統大規模改造，在同義字代換表中，system overhaul 代表系統全面改造、翻修。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"The IT director requested that all department managers ensure their teams ________ critical documents before the platform migration begins.","o":[["A","launch"],["B","backup"],["C","retrieve"],["D","integrate"]],"a":"(B) backup","zh":"IT 總監要求所有部門經理確保他們的團隊在平台遷移開始前備份關鍵文件。","e":"在系統更新開始前，IT 部門的首要要求是進行預防性的「資料備份」，即 backup。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"According to the memorandum, the newly distributed printers and scanners are classified as ________ and will be connected to the wireless network.","o":[["A","security protocols"],["B","biometric readers"],["C","peripheral devices"],["D","diagnostic tools"]],"a":"(C) peripheral devices","zh":"根據備忘錄，新分發的印表機和掃描器被歸類為周邊裝置，並將連接到無線網路。","e":"印表機 (printer) 與掃描器 (scanner) 在 IT 場景中，皆屬於外部硬體，即「周邊裝置 (peripheral devices)」。故選 (C)。"},{"q":"The IT department has scheduled the comprehensive testing of the database server to take place ________ to avoid affecting weekday productivity.","o":[["A","by Friday"],["B","next week"],["C","over the weekend"],["D","at midnight tonight"]],"a":"(C) over the weekend","zh":"IT 部門已安排在週末對資料庫伺服器進行全面測試，以避免影響工作日的生產力。","e":"對應講義中「April 18-19 weekend testing」以及「週末測試以避免影響生產力」的設定，應選 (C) over the weekend。"},{"q":"In the IT announcement, the phrase \"launch the upgraded platform\" is closest in meaning to ________.","o":[["A","discontinue the old system"],["B","roll out the improved system"],["C","purchase new software licenses"],["D","reset the administrative passwords"]],"a":"(B) roll out the improved system","zh":"在 IT 公告中，短語 \"launch the upgraded platform\"（推出升級平台）的意思最接近下列哪一項？","e":"同義字代換考點。在同義轉換表中，launch = roll out = release，upgraded = improved。故 (B) 為最精準的代換。"}],"say":["Plans to launch the upgraded platform next week.","This major system overhaul will modernize our infrastructure.","We've completed the software installation on all computers.","The printer and scanner aren't connecting properly.","Receive new biometric readers for improved access control.","This diagnostic tool can analyze network performance.","Testing during the weekend of April 18-19.","Please ensure your teams backup critical data before the update begins."]},"13-2":{"tree":"【Ch13-2 技術支援與問題解決：IT協助溝通 Technical Support & Troubleshooting】\n │\n ├── 🔴 S - Situation (情境確認：識別故障異常)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 識別連線失敗、伺服器故障、身份驗證錯誤等系統異常\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **authentication errors** (驗證錯誤), **server malfunction** (伺服器故障), **error message** (錯誤訊息)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── My account keeps displaying authentication errors. / Server malfunction affected multiple users yesterday.\n │\n ├── 📋 T - Task (任務說明：診斷問題原因)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 透過識別碼與密碼檢驗，分析權限過期與登入失敗次數\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **retrieve** (取回), **identification number** (識別碼), **expire** (過期)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── Access was suspended due to multiple failed login attempts. / The server won't allow me to retrieve my stored files.\n │\n ├── 💡 A - Action (行動方案：故障排除與憑證重設)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 提供安全連結與臨時密碼，引導使用者完成密碼重設\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **reset credentials** (重設憑證), **temporary password** (臨時密碼), **security protocols** (安全協定)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── Here's a secure link to create your new credentials. / Please reset the temporary password immediately after you log in.\n │\n ├── ✅ R - Result (結果確認：系統修復與資料還原)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 確定轉換期之備份期限，並引導有需要者聯絡分機還原檔案\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **backup** (備份), **restore** (還原), **help desk** (服務台)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── Any malfunction during the transition should be reported to our help desk. / If you need to restore files, contact me at extension 5544.\n │\n ├── 🔧 關鍵概念一：技術支援的三層級 (Support Levels)\n │    ├── **Level 1: Basic Support** ── 處理基本密碼重設、清除 Cookies / 快取、一般諮詢\n │    ├── **Level 2: Technical Specialist** ── 處理伺服器端錯誤、安全異常、系統性故障排除\n │    └── **Level 3: System Administrator** ── 處理全面網路配置、安全協定修訂、權限控管\n │\n ├── 📋 關鍵概念二：安全認證與密碼管理 (Security Measures)\n │    ├── **臨時密碼安全原則** ── 臨時密碼 (temporary password) 登入後**必須立即變更 (reset immediately)**\n │    ├── **安全連結發送** ── 透過 `secure link` 提供線上重設，避免明文傳輸\n │    └── **身分認證程序** ── IT 人員在處理前，必須先核對病患或同仁的 `identification number` (識別碼)\n │\n └── ⚠ 三大高頻防雷陷阱 (Common Traps)\n      ├── 1. 時間錯配 ── **Sunday night** (密碼失效過期時間) ≠ **Monday morning** (新政策生效時間)。\n      ├── 2. 角色錯配 ── 處理特殊伺服器故障的人員是 **specialist** (專家)，一般基本客服不負責此權限。\n      └── 3. 動作誤判 ── **reset credentials** (重設憑證變更密碼) ≠ **delete account** (刪除帳號)。","quiz":[{"q":"Some employees have reported that they are unable to ________ their daily reports because of a persistent server database error.","o":[["A","expire"],["B","retrieve"],["C","suspend"],["D","malfunction"]],"a":"(B) retrieve","zh":"一些員工報告說，由於持續的伺服器資料庫錯誤，他們無法取回他們的日常報告。","e":"無法取得儲存的檔案，對應同義代換字 retrieve（取回/檢索/讀取），故選 (B)。"},{"q":"According to the IT department email, all existing passwords will ________ on Sunday night, so you must reset your credentials before then.","o":[["A","launch"],["B","expire"],["C","restore"],["D","install"]],"a":"(B) expire","zh":"根據 IT 部門的電子郵件，所有現有密碼將在週日晚上過期，因此您必須在那之前重設您的憑證。","e":"時間截止與權限效期問題。舊密碼會到期失效，對應 (B) expire。"},{"q":"Because of multiple failed login attempts, the automated security system has temporarily ________ Ms. Green’s access to the company database.","o":[["A","expanded"],["B","suspended"],["C","qualified"],["D","implemented"]],"a":"(B) suspended","zh":"由於多次登入失敗，自動化安全系統已暫時中止了格林女士進入公司資料庫的存取權限。","e":"多次嘗試失敗導致帳戶權限被 IT 中止，對應 suspended（暫停/中止），故選 (B)。"},{"q":"If your laptop continues to display ________ during connection attempts, please reset your router or contact technical support immediately.","o":[["A","software installations"],["B","authentication errors"],["C","biometric readers"],["D","training manuals"]],"a":"(B) authentication errors","zh":"如果您的筆記型電腦在嘗試連線期間繼續顯示身份驗證錯誤，請立即重設您的路由器或聯絡技術支援。","e":"連線時顯示的帳密驗證問題，屬於多益 IT 場景最經典的 authentication errors，故選 (B)。"},{"q":"To ensure maximum data protection, the network administrator has implemented new security ________ across all departments.","o":[["A","specifications"],["B","templates"],["C","protocols"],["D","assessments"]],"a":"(C) protocols","zh":"為確保最大程度的資料保護，網路管理員已在所有部門實施了新的安全協定。","e":"實施新的安全規範或制度，在 IT 安全管理中專指 protocols（協定/安全協議），故選 (C)。"}],"say":["My account keeps displaying authentication errors.","Server malfunction affected multiple users yesterday.","Access was suspended due to multiple failed login attempts.","The server won't allow me to retrieve my stored files.","Here's a secure link to create your new credentials.","Please reset the temporary password immediately after you log in.","Any malfunction during the transition should be reported to our help desk.","If you need to restore files, contact me at extension 5544."]},"13-3":{"tree":"【Ch13-3 技術學習與知識傳遞：培訓認證溝通 Technical Learning & Knowledge Transfer】\n │\n ├── 🔴 S - Situation (情境確認：了解培訓需求)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 迎新同仁與學員，確認已收到說明手冊並說明強制培訓性質\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **workshop** (工作坊), **manual** (手冊), **mandatory** (強制性的)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── Welcome to today's technical training workshop. / Your orientation includes essential training sessions.\n │\n ├── 📋 T - Task (任務說明：展示使用者友善功能)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 介紹軟體介面，分段講授基礎、進階程序與測試規程\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **technical specifications** (技術規格), **demonstration** (示範), **user-friendly** (好上手的)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── Guide you through each function of the new interface. / Technical specifications seem complicated.\n │\n ├── 💡 A - Action (行動方案：入口網站資源取得)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 提示線上入口網站資源，供學員課前線上預習及課後複習\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **portal** (入口網站), **documentation** (文件說明), **video tutorials** (影片教學)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── All reference materials are available in our portal. / Please review these before attending.\n │\n ├── ✅ R - Result (結果確認：評估測驗與認證取得)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 通過20或30分鐘的評估，取得證書；未合格者下月重考或安排一對一輔導\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **assessment** (評估), **earn certification** (獲得認證), **one-on-one tutorials** (一對一教學)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── Participants who pass will earn their certification immediately. / Those who aren't yet qualified can retake the test next month.\n │\n ├── 📚 關鍵概念一：培訓課程的三大模組 (Training Structure)\n │    ├── **模組1: Basic Features** ── 基本功能（參與者可能在此部分已合格 `qualified`）\n │    ├── **模組2: Advanced Documentation** ── 進階文件管理程序（學員主要期待學習之內容）\n │    └── **模組3: Testing Protocols** ── 測驗與認證協議\n │\n ├── 💾 關鍵概念二：線上與紙本資源管理 (Resource Locations)\n │    ├── **Printed manual (印刷手冊)** ── 包含詳細的技術規格 (technical specifications)，課堂發放\n │    └── **Online portal (入口網站)** ── 線上平台，包含 documentation、video tutorials 與投影片，供課前預習\n │\n └── ⚠ 三大高頻防雷陷阱 (Common Traps)\n      ├── 1. 位置混淆 ── 課後複習之影音、簡報與文件在 **portal** (網站) 上，不在紙本 **manual** (手冊) 裡。\n      ├── 2. 時間錯配 ── 測驗時間 Part 3 與 Part 7 為 **30 minutes**，Part 4 獨白為 **20 minutes**，不可張冠李戴。\n      └── 3. 對象誤判 ── **qualified** 代表「已合格/符合資格的」，千萬不要誤判成「尚未合格的」。","quiz":[{"q":"Because the new billing interface is designed to be highly ________, employees required minimal training to master it.","o":[["A","mandatory"],["B","user-friendly"],["C","complicated"],["D","proprietary"]],"a":"(B) user-friendly","zh":"由於新帳務介面設計得非常容易上手，員工只需要極少的培訓即可掌握。","e":"訓練時間極少是因為介面容易使用。在同義字代換表中，easy-to-use = user-friendly。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"The new software training program is ________ for all newly hired staff members during their first week of orientation.","o":[["A","qualified"],["B","user-friendly"],["C","mandatory"],["D","certified"]],"a":"(C) mandatory","zh":"新軟體培訓課程對於所有新僱用的員工在入職引導的第一週是強制性的。","e":"入職訓練中規定的必要課程，在多益場景中專用 mandatory（強制性的/必須的），故選 (C)。"},{"q":"To improve future training sessions, please complete the training evaluation form and submit your ________ before leaving the workshop.","o":[["A","specifications"],["B","feedback"],["C","portal"],["D","manual"]],"a":"(B) feedback","zh":"為了改進未來的培訓課程，請在離開工作坊前填妥培訓評估表並提交您的回饋。","e":"填寫 evaluation form 的目的是提交「回饋意見」，即 feedback，故選 (B)。"},{"q":"Those who fail to pass the safety assessment this Friday will be given an option to ________ the test next month.","o":[["A","launch"],["B","retake"],["C","expire"],["D","retrieve"]],"a":"(B) retake","zh":"那些本週五未能通過安全評估的人，將被給予一個在下個月重考的選項。","e":"未通過測驗時，多益常見的 IT/人事補考機制為 retake next month（下月重考），故選 (B)。"},{"q":"All video tutorials and presentation slides can be ________ right away through the resources section of the employee portal.","o":[["A","compiled"],["B","accessed"],["C","undergone"],["D","suspended"]],"a":"(B) accessed","zh":"所有影片教學與簡報投影片皆可透過員工入口網站的資源區立即取得/存取。","e":"在入口網站資源區「取得資料/查閱文件」，多益閱讀常與 available、accessible 互換，動詞為 accessed，故選 (B)。"}],"say":["Welcome to today's technical training workshop.","Your orientation includes essential training sessions.","Guide you through each function of the new interface.","Technical specifications seem complicated.","All reference materials are available in our portal.","Please review these before attending.","Participants who pass will earn their certification immediately.","Those who aren't yet qualified can retake the test next month."]},"13-4":{"tree":"【Ch13-4 技術創新與產業活動：研發突破溝通 Technical Innovation & Industry Events】\n │\n ├── 🔴 S - Situation (情境確認：了解開發現況)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 匯報手機原型開發進程，並鎖定下個月大型技術會議\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **prototype** (原型), **technology conference** (技術會議), **next month** (下個月)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── How's the prototype for the new mobile phone coming along? / The technology conference is next month.\n │\n ├── 📋 T - Task (任務說明：完成設計改進)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 進行穿戴式裝置的突破性設計，並完成相容性修改\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **breakthrough design** (突破性設計), **wearable devices** (穿戴式裝置), **design revisions** (設計修改)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── Engineers are finalizing a breakthrough design. / Revisions based on user feedback have created an intuitive interface.\n │\n ├── 💡 A - Action (行動方案：執行測試驗證)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 召集500名測試者完成測試，並通過嚴格的品質保證\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **beta testing** (測試版測試), **quality assurance** (品質保證), **rigorous** (嚴格的)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── Completed rigorous quality assurance procedures last week. / Beta testing involved 500 users.\n │\n ├── ✅ R - Result (結果確認：產品發布實施)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 宣布下季度實施部署，使處理時間大幅縮短 40%\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **implementation** (實施), **next quarter** (下個季度), **booth** (攤位)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── These advancements could potentially reduce processing time by 40 percent. / Implementation begins next quarter.\n │\n ├── 🔧 關鍵概念一：產品研發生命週期 (Development Stages)\n │    ├── **階段1: Prototype Phase** ── 概念模型、設計修改 (`finalizing breakthrough design` / `design revisions`)\n │    ├── **階段2: Testing Phase** ── 嚴格的 QA 檢驗、測試版測試驗證 (`completed rigorous QA` / `500 users beta testing`)\n │    └── **階段3: Launch & Rollout** ── 產業會議簡報發表、下季度實施 (`moved to main stage 2 PM` / `implementation next quarter`)\n │\n ├── 📊 關鍵概念二：技術指標與效能升級 (Key Metrics)\n │    ├── **40% Reduction** ── 處理時間縮短 40% (注意：**40% 是縮短處理時間，不等於電池效率**)\n │    └── **500 Users** ── 乙版測試 (beta testing) 的用戶人數規模 (注意：**500 人是測試規模，不要與 1000 人混淆**)\n │\n └── ⚠ 三大高頻防雷陷阱 (Common Traps)\n      ├── 1. 時間混淆 ── 科技展覽時間是 **next month** (下個月)，選項常設 **tomorrow** (明天) 作為干擾。\n      ├── 2. 數字錯配 ── **40%** 是處理時間的節省，不等於電池效力或產量增幅。\n      └── 3. 階段誤判 ── **prototype** 指原型或樣機，不等於已經量產並全面普及的最終市售產品。","quiz":[{"q":"TechCorp is proud to showcase its latest ________ for smartwatches at the technology expo next week.","o":[["A","prototype"],["B","protocol"],["C","assessment"],["D","credential"]],"a":"(A) prototype","zh":"TechCorp 很榮幸能在下週的技術博覽會上展示其最新的智慧手錶原型。","e":"展會上展示供大眾預覽、尚未完全上市的測試機型，多益場景中專用 prototype（原型/樣機），故選 (A)。"},{"q":"The software update was approved because beta testing results indicated a ________ decrease in system processing lag.","o":[["A","rigorous"],["B","user-friendly"],["C","significant"],["D","mandatory"]],"a":"(C) significant","zh":"該軟體更新獲得批准，因為測試版測試結果顯示系統處理延遲有顯著減少。","e":"形容升級成效優異（減少40%等顯著數字），用 significant（顯著的/重大的），故選 (C)。"},{"q":"Because the prototype underwent ________ quality assurance checks, the company is confident about its stable functionality.","o":[["A","intuitive"],["B","rigorous"],["C","temporary"],["D","proprietary"]],"a":"(B) rigorous","zh":"由於該原型接受了嚴格的品質保證檢查，公司對其穩定的功能性充滿信心。","e":"品質保證（QA）程序的修飾詞，多益講義與考卷偏好搭配 rigorous（嚴格的/嚴密的）或 stringent，故選 (B)。"},{"q":"The project manager announced that the full ________ of the mobile system overhaul is scheduled for next quarter.","o":[["A","implementation"],["B","malfunction"],["C","specification"],["D","database"]],"a":"(A) implementation","zh":"專案經理宣布，行動系統改造的全面實施計劃安排在下個季度。","e":"計劃「全面推行、實施或部署」，在商務與技術開發中專用 implementation，其時間點常為未來（next quarter），故選 (A)。"},{"q":"A group of ________ from the engineering department will be stationed at Booth 402 to explain the smartwatch functionality.","o":[["A","instructors"],["B","specialists"],["C","vendors"],["D","candidates"]],"a":"(B) specialists","zh":"一組來自工程部門的專家將駐守在 402 號攤位，以解釋智慧手錶的功能。","e":"多益聽力常見的「攤位（booth）與人員」考題。駐守攤位提供技術性解釋的人員，在技術場景中多指 specialists（技術專家），故選 (B)。"}],"say":["How's the prototype for the new mobile phone coming along?","The technology conference is next month.","Engineers are finalizing a breakthrough design.","Revisions based on user feedback have created an intuitive interface.","Completed rigorous quality assurance procedures last week.","Beta testing involved 500 users.","These advancements could potentially reduce processing time by 40 percent.","Implementation begins next quarter."]},"14-1":{"tree":"【Ch14-1 就醫預約與互動：醫療服務溝通 Medical Appointments & Interactions】\n │\n ├── 🔴 S - Situation (情境確認：了解就醫需求)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 了解就醫需求、看診狀況、診所類型\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **appointment** (預約), **reschedule** (重新安排時間), **clinic** (診所), **medical center** (醫療中心)\n │    ├── 必考句型 ── \"I'm calling to reschedule my appointment.\" (我打電話要重新安排預約時間) / \"I have a physical therapy session at 2 PM.\" / \"I'm a new patient at your dental clinic.\"\n │    └── ⚠ 注意事項 ── **reschedule** = 改時間（不是取消）；**new patient** = 需要填表格；**medical center vs clinic** ＝ 規模差異\n │\n ├── 📋 T - Task (任務說明：確認病人資訊)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 確認病人資訊與病患資料\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **patient ID** (病歷號碼), **new patient forms** (新病人表格), **medical history** (病史), **receptionist** (接待員)\n │    ├── 必考句型 ── \"May I have your patient ID number?\" (可以給我您的病歷號碼嗎？) / \"Should I fill out new patient forms?\" / \"The receptionist from Greenfield Dental Clinic.\"\n │    └── 📍 資訊類型 ── **ID number** (識別號碼), **Medical questionnaire** (醫療問卷), **Insurance information** (保險資訊)\n │\n ├── 💡 A - Action (行動方案：安排就診時間)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 安排就診時間與服務項目\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **specialist** (專科醫生), **physical therapy** (物理治療), **tooth cleaning** (洗牙), **whitening procedure** (美白療程)\n │    ├── 必考句型 ── \"Could you help me book a follow-up visit with the specialist next month?\" (您能幫我預約下個月與專科醫生的回診嗎？) / \"Your tooth cleaning and whitening procedure.\" / \"Physical therapy evaluation at our rehabilitation clinic.\"\n │    └── 🔄 服務類型 ── **General check-up** (一般檢查) / **Specialist consultation** (專科諮詢) / **Dental services** (牙科服務) / **Rehabilitation** (復健治療)\n │\n ├── ✅ R - Result (結果確認：提醒注意事項)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 提醒注意事項與候診須知\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **questionnaire** (問卷), **delay** (延誤), **consultation** (諮詢), **48-hour notice** (48小時通知)\n │    ├── 必考句型 ── \"Please remember to complete the medical history questionnaire before your visit.\" (請記得在就診前填寫完病史問卷) / \"We're experiencing a slight delay, so your consultation may start 15 minutes later.\" (我們遇到延誤，所以您的諮詢可能晚15分鐘開始) / \"Please provide 48-hour notice.\"\n │    └── 📱 提醒事項 ── **Complete forms** (填寫表格) / **Arrive early** (提早到達) / **Delay warning** (延誤警告)\n │\n ├── 📅 關鍵概念一：預約時間管理 (Appointment Management)\n │    ├── 同一日兩個預約也要分開算（同日多重預約：March 25: check-up 10 AM + physical therapy 2 PM）\n │    ├── **reschedule ≠ cancel**（重新安排不等於取消）\n │    └── 時間要素 ── Tomorrow ➔ Thursday 改期；15th or 22nd 可選日期；**48-hour notice** (通知期限)\n │\n ├── 📋 關鍵概念二：新病人登記程序 (New Patient Process)\n │    ├── **New patient forms**（新病人表格）可在線上或現場填寫；**Medical history questionnaire**（病史問卷）就診前必須完成\n │    ├── **Patient ID provision**（提供病歷號）預約時需要\n │    └── 💡 解題技巧 ── new patient at dental clinic = 需要填表；do this online = 線上完成表格；before your visit = 就診前要求\n │\n ├── ⏰ 關鍵概念三：延誤通知與處理 (Delay Management)\n │    ├── **15 minutes later** (延誤15分鐘)：標準輕微延誤 (slight delay)，可能晚開始，需向病患致歉 (apologize for inconvenience)\n │    ├── **Emergency causing reschedule** (緊急情況改期)：醫生有緊急手術 (Doctor's emergency surgery)，必須重新安排預約\n │    └── 應對措施 ── Arrive 20 minutes early (提早20分鐘到) / Wait in waiting room (在候診室等) / Call to confirm (打電話確認)\n │\n ├── 🔄 同義轉換 (Paraphrase Map)\n │    ├── 預約動作 ── **appointment** = booking = scheduled visit / **reschedule** = change time = rearrange / **cancel** = call off = terminate\n │    ├── 醫療場所 ── **clinic** = medical office = healthcare facility / **medical center** = hospital = healthcare center / **dental clinic** = dentist office = dental practice\n │    ├── 表格文件 ── **new patient forms** = registration forms = intake forms / **questionnaire** = survey = form / **medical history** = health record = medical background\n │    └── 服務類型 ── **check-up** = examination = routine visit / **physical therapy** = physiotherapy = rehabilitation / **tooth cleaning** = dental hygiene = teeth cleaning\n │\n └── ⚠ 三大高頻防雷陷阱 (Common Traps)\n      ├── 1. 動作混淆 ── **reschedule** (重新安排) ≠ **cancel all** (全部取消)\n      ├── 2. 數量錯算 ── 同一日多個預約也必須「分開」計算數量與時間\n      └── 3. 時間誤判 ── **15 minutes late** (遲到/延誤15分鐘) ≠ **clinic closed** (診所關門)","quiz":[{"q":"Due to an emergency surgery, Dr. Lee has to ________ all of his dental check-ups scheduled for tomorrow afternoon.","o":[["A","cancel"],["B","register"],["C","reschedule"],["D","examine"]],"a":"(C) reschedule","zh":"由於一場緊急手術，李醫生必須重新安排明天下午所有已排定的牙科檢查。","e":"此處為多益常見的「動作混淆」陷阱。根據講義，醫生因緊急情況（emergency surgery）無法看診時，診所會採取「重新安排時間（reschedule = rearrange）」而非「直接取消不看（cancel）」，故選 (C)。"},{"q":"To ensure a smooth registration process, first-time visitors must complete the new patient forms online ________ their scheduled visit.","o":[["A","after"],["B","before"],["C","during"],["D","since"]],"a":"(B) before","zh":"為確保掛號流程順暢，初次就診的訪客必須在排定就診「之前」在線上填寫完新病人表格。","e":"新病人流程規定「填寫病史問卷與登記表」是「就診前的要求（before your visit）」，因此選擇介系詞 (B) before。"},{"q":"According to the dental clinic's email confirmation, Mr. Davies has scheduled ________ separate visits on March 25.","o":[["A","one"],["B","two"],["C","three"],["D","four"]],"a":"(B) two","zh":"根據牙科診所的電子郵件確認信，戴維斯先生在 3 月 25 日安排了兩次分開的就診。","e":"此為「數量錯算」陷阱。戴維斯先生在當天安排了 check-up (10 AM) 與 physical therapy (2 PM) 兩種不同的服務，雖然在「同一天」，但同日多重預約（Same-day multiple）在多益中「必須分開算作兩次預約」，故選 (B)。"},{"q":"The receptionist left a message stating that the doctor is currently experiencing a slight ________, so the appointment will begin 15 minutes later.","o":[["A","suspension"],["B","cancellation"],["C","reservation"],["D","delay"]],"a":"(D) delay","zh":"接待員留下一則訊息，指出醫生目前正經歷輕微的「延誤」，因此預約將會晚15分鐘開始。","e":"15 minutes later 對應的是「輕微延誤（slight delay / start late）」，此題考查專有名詞搭配，應選 (D) delay。"},{"q":"In the confirmation letter, the phrase \"scheduled visits\" is closest in meaning to which of the following?","o":[["A","canceled registrations"],["B","clinical directories"],["C","physical examinations"],["D","booked appointments"]],"a":"(D) booked appointments","zh":"在確認信中，短語「scheduled visits」（排定的看診）與下列哪一個選項的意思最接近？","e":"根據同義轉換表，scheduled visit = appointment = booking。故 (D) booked appointments 為最精準的代換。"}],"say":["I'm calling to reschedule my appointment.","I have a physical therapy session at 2 PM.","I'm a new patient at your dental clinic.","May I have your patient ID number?","Should I fill out new patient forms?","The receptionist from Greenfield Dental Clinic.","Could you help me book a follow-up visit with the specialist next month?","Your tooth cleaning and whitening procedure.","Physical therapy evaluation at our rehabilitation clinic.","Please remember to complete the medical history questionnaire before your visit.","We're experiencing a slight delay, so your consultation may start 15 minutes later.","Please provide 48-hour notice."]},"14-2":{"tree":"【Ch14-2 藥物與健康產品：藥房服務溝通 Medication & Health Products】\n │\n ├── 🔴 S - Situation (情境確認：了解用藥需求)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 了解用藥需求與配藥情境\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **prescription** (處方), **refill** (補充), **pharmacy** (藥房), **medication** (藥物)\n │    ├── 必考句型 ── \"I'm calling about my prescription.\" (我打電話是關於我的處方箋) / \"I need a refill on my allergy pills.\" (我需要補充過敏藥) / \"The pharmacy just received your monthly prescription.\"\n │    └── ⚠ 注意事項 ── **prescription** = 需要醫生開立；**refill** = 補充（不是新處方）；**monthly prescription** = 每月配藥\n │\n ├── 📋 T - Task (任務說明：確認藥物資訊)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 確認藥物資訊與規格\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **in stock** (有庫存), **dosage** (劑量), **specific brand** (特定品牌), **pharmacist** (藥劑師)\n │    ├── 必考句型 ── \"I'll see if it's in stock.\" (我來看看是否有庫存) / \"The dosage you need isn't available.\" (您需要的劑量沒有現貨) / \"That specific brand needs ordering.\" (那個特定品牌需要訂購)\n │    └── 💊 藥物類型 ── **Prescription** (處方藥) / **Over-the-counter** (非處方藥) / **Generic** (學名藥) / **Brand-name** (品牌藥)\n │\n ├── 💡 A - Action (行動方案：安排取藥方式)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 安排取藥方式與交付流程\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **order** (訂購), **shipment** (貨運), **arrive by Thursday** (週四到貨), **medical supplies** (醫療用品)\n │    ├── 必考句型 ── \"We'll need to order that specific brand, which should arrive by Thursday.\" (我們需要訂購那個特定品牌，預計週四到貨) / \"Submit refill requests online 48 hours in advance.\" (提前48小時線上提交補充申請) / \"After yesterday's shipment.\" (昨天貨運之後)\n │    └── 🔄 取藥方式 ── **Collect today** (今天領取) / **Order for Thursday** (訂購週四到) / **Online submission** (線上申請)\n │\n ├── ✅ R - Result (結果確認：提供專業服務)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 提供專業服務與用藥指引\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **side effects** (副作用), **expiration date** (有效期限), **24-hour helpline** (24小時專線), **certified pharmacy staff** (認證藥劑師人員)\n │    ├── 必考句型 ── \"Our 24-hour helpline connects you directly with certified pharmacy staff.\" (我們的24小時服務專線可讓您直接與認證藥劑師人員聯繫) / \"Can discuss side effects.\" (可以討論副作用) / \"Check the expiration date.\" (檢查有效期限)\n │    └── 📱 專業服務 ── **Consultation** (諮詢) / **Verification** (驗證) / **Professional advice** (專業建議)\n │\n ├── 📦 藥物庫存狀態 (Stock Management)\n │    ├── **In stock now (現在有貨)** ── Allergy pills (過敏藥), Seasonal medications (季節性藥物)\n │    ├── **Need to order (需要訂購)** ── Specific brand (特定品牌), Special dosage (特殊劑量)\n │    ├── **Just received (剛收到)** ── Monthly prescriptions (月處方), Yesterday's shipment (昨天到貨)\n │    └── **供貨時程** ── Arrive by Thursday (週四前到) / 48 hours advance (提前48小時)\n │\n ├── 💊 藥品種類管理 (Medication Types)\n │    ├── **Prescription medications (處方藥)** ── Allergy pills, Monthly prescription, Specific dosage\n │    ├── **Over-the-counter (非處方藥)** ── Pain relief (止痛藥), Alternative options (替代選項)\n │    └── **Supplements (營養補充品)** ── Vitamins (維他命), Check expiration (檢查有效期)\n │\n ├── 👨‍⚕ 藥劑師服務 (Pharmacist Services)\n │    ├── **24-hour helpline (24小時專線)** ── Certified staff (認證人員), Side effects discussion (副作用討論)\n │    ├── **Extended consultations (延長諮詢)** ── Monday開始, Dosage adjustments (劑量調整)\n │    └── **Online services (線上服務)** ── 48-hour advance refill (提前48小時補充)\n │\n ├── 🔄 同義轉換 (Paraphrase Map)\n │    ├── 藥物相關 ── **prescription** = Rx = doctor's order / **medication** = medicine = drug / **refill** = replenishment = renewal / **dosage** = dose = amount\n │    ├── 庫存狀態 ── **in stock** = available = on hand / **out of stock** = unavailable = need to order / **shipment** = delivery = supply / **arrive by** = come by = get here by\n │    ├── 時間表達 ── **24-hour** = round-the-clock = all day / **by Thursday** = Thursday or before = no later than Thursday / **48 hours in advance** = two days ahead = 48 hours early\n │    └── 服務動作 ── **collect** = pick up = get / **order** = request = arrange for / **verify** = check = confirm\n │\n └── ⚠ 三大高頻防雷陷阱 (Common Traps)\n      ├── 1. 需求混淆 ── **refill** (補充) ≠ **new prescription** (新處方)\n      ├── 2. 時間錯配 ── **by Thursday** (週四前) ≠ **on Thursday** (週四當天)\n      └── 3. 藥物誤判 ── **prescription** (處方藥) ≠ **over-the-counter** (非處方藥)","quiz":[{"q":"Because the requested brand-name allergy pills are currently out of stock, the pharmacist recommended ________ them from our regional supplier.","o":[["A","collecting"],["B","prescribing"],["C","ordering"],["D","cancelling"]],"a":"(C) ordering","zh":"由於所要求的品牌過敏藥目前缺貨，藥劑師建議向我們的區域供應商「訂購」。","e":"此處考查藥房在 out of stock 時的標準行動。根據講義，當藥品缺貨時應採取「訂購（ordering / order）」行動，故選 (C)。"},{"q":"The shipment of the specialized medication is scheduled to ________ our clinic no later than Thursday morning.","o":[["A","request"],["B","arrive at"],["C","order for"],["D","verify with"]],"a":"(B) arrive at","zh":"該特定藥物的貨運安排在不遲於週四早上「抵達」我們的診所。","e":"此題考查同義代換。講義在 Action 階段指出 arrive by Thursday，選項中以 arrive at 搭配時間截止片語 no later than（不遲於 = by），最符合情境，故選 (B)。"},{"q":"To discussions about potential ________ of a newly prescribed medication, clients should contact the round-the-clock helpline.","o":[["A","generic alternatives"],["B","expiration dates"],["C","service hours"],["D","side effects"]],"a":"(D) side effects","zh":"為了討論新開立藥物可能產生的「副作用」，客戶應聯繫全天候服務專線。","e":"此處考查 helpline 的專屬諮詢範疇。根據講義，24小時專線（helpline = round-the-clock line）是為了讓客戶諮詢「副作用（side effects）」，故選 (D)。"},{"q":"Customers who wish to request a prescription replenishment are required to submit their online forms ________.","o":[["A","this weekend"],["B","within three business days"],["C","48 hours in advance"],["D","starting next month"]],"a":"(C) 48 hours in advance","zh":"希望申請處方補充的客戶，被要求「提前48小時」在線上提交表格。","e":"此題針對時間限制進行設計。講義在 Action 必考句型中明確要求：Submit refill requests online 48 hours in advance，故 (C) 才是唯一正確的規定時限。"},{"q":"In the pharmacy's service notice, the phrase \"generic alternatives\" is used to refer to which of the following?","o":[["A","non-brand options"],["B","prescription documents"],["C","medical appointments"],["D","clinical equipment"]],"a":"(A) non-brand options","zh":"在藥房的服務通知中，短語「generic alternatives」（學名藥替代品）用於指代下列哪一個選項？","e":"學名藥（generic alternatives）指無專利保護、非大牌商標的藥品。在多益中常代換為 non-brand options 或 cheaper substitutes，故 (A) 正確。"}],"say":["I'm calling about my prescription.","I need a refill on my allergy pills.","The pharmacy just received your monthly prescription.","I'll see if it's in stock.","The dosage you need isn't available.","That specific brand needs ordering.","We'll need to order that specific brand, which should arrive by Thursday.","Submit refill requests online 48 hours in advance.","After yesterday's shipment.","Our 24-hour helpline connects you directly with certified pharmacy staff.","Can discuss side effects.","Check the expiration date."]},"14-3":{"tree":"【Ch14-3 健康管理與營養：飲食諮詢溝通 Health Management & Nutrition】\n │\n ├── 🔴 S - Situation (情境確認：了解健康需求)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 了解健康需求、健康目標、改善精力水平\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **nutritionist** (營養師), **wellness center** (健康中心), **energy levels** (精力水平), **meal plans** (飲食計畫)\n │    ├── 必考句型 ── \"I'm here for my appointment with the nutritionist.\" (我來赴營養師的預約) / \"I've been exploring different meal plans to improve my energy levels.\" (我一直在探索不同的飲食計畫來提升精力水平) / \"Welcome to our wellness center.\" (歡迎來到我們的健康中心)\n │    └── ⚠ 注意事項 ── **nutritionist** = 營養專家（不是醫生）；**energy levels** = 精力/活力程度；**exploring** = 嘗試不同選擇\n │\n ├── 📋 T - Task (任務說明：評估飲食現況)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 評估飲食現況、飲食習慣、特殊飲食限制\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **dietary restrictions** (飲食限制), **processed foods** (加工食品), **healthy lifestyle** (健康生活方式), **diet assessment** (飲食評估)\n │    ├── 必考句型 ── \"The specialist recommended reducing processed foods in my daily meals.\" (專家建議減少我日常飲食中的加工食品) / \"Based on dietary restrictions and healthy lifestyle goals.\" (基於飲食限制和健康生活目標) / \"Complete your diet assessment form.\" (完成您的飲食評估表)\n │    └── 📍 評估重點 ── Current eating habits (目前飲食習慣) / Health goals (健康目標) / Weight management (體重管理)\n │\n ├── 💡 A - Action (行動方案：制定營養策略)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 制定營養策略與個人化設計\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **nutrition plan** (營養計畫), **organic** (有機的), **natural ingredients** (天然成分), **healthy eating** (健康飲食)\n │    ├── 必考句型 ── \"Creating personalized nutrition plans.\" (制定個人化營養計畫) / \"Organic options with natural ingredients.\" (有機選擇配天然成分) / \"All aspects of healthy eating.\" (健康飲食的各個層面)\n │    └── 🔄 計畫內容 ── **Customized meal plans** (客製化飲食計畫) / **Organic alternatives** (有機替代品) / **Natural food choices** (天然食物選擇)\n │\n ├── ✅ R - Result (結果確認：提供專業指導)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 提供專業指導、個人化諮詢與食品標籤解讀\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **food labels** (食品標籤), **calories/protein/fat/sugar** (卡路里/蛋白質/脂肪/糖分), **wellness education** (健康教育), **personalized consultations** (個人化諮詢)\n │    ├── 必考句型 ── \"Our wellness center offers personalized consultations with certified nutrition experts.\" (我們的健康中心提供與認證營養專家的個人化諮詢) / \"How to read food labels for calories, protein, sugar, and fat.\" (如何閱讀食品標籤上的卡路里、蛋白質、糖分和脂肪) / \"You'll receive a customized plan today.\" (您今天會收到客製化計畫)\n │    └── 📱 專業服務 ── **Seven days a week** (每週七天可用) / **Certified experts** (認證專家) / **Individual sessions** (個人課程)\n │\n ├── 👩‍⚕ 營養諮詢程序 (Consultation Process)\n │    ├── **Initial appointment (初次預約)** ── Meet with nutritionist (會見營養師), Discuss energy levels (討論精力水平)\n │    ├── **Assessment phase (評估階段)** ── Diet assessment form (飲食評估表), 15 minutes early (提早15分鐘)\n │    └── **Plan delivery (計畫交付)** ── Customized plan today (今天給客製化計畫)\n │\n ├── 🥗 飲食改善策略 (Dietary Improvement)\n │    ├── **Reduce processed foods (減少加工食品)** ── Specialist recommendation (專家建議), Main workshop topic (工作坊主題)\n │    ├── **Organic & natural (有機與天然)** ── Natural ingredients (天然成分), Organic options (有機選擇)\n │    └── **Weight loss success (減重成功)** ── Lost 15 pounds (減重15磅)\n │\n ├── 🔄 同義轉換 (Paraphrase Map)\n │    ├── 專業人員 ── **nutritionist** = dietitian = nutrition expert / **specialist** = expert = professional / **certified expert** = qualified professional\n │    ├── 飲食概念 ── **meal plans** = eating plans = diet programs / **processed foods** = packaged foods = manufactured foods / **organic** = natural = chemical-free / **dietary restrictions** = food limitations = eating constraints\n │    ├── 營養成分 ── **calories** = energy units = caloric content / **protein** = muscle-building nutrients / **fat** = lipids = dietary fat / **sugar** = carbohydrates = sweeteners\n │    └── 成果描述 ── **improve** = enhance = boost / **reduce** = decrease = lower / **lost 15 pounds** = weight loss = reduced weight\n │\n └── ⚠ 三大高頻防雷陷阱 (Common Traps)\n      ├── 1. 身份混淆 ── **nutritionist** (營養師) ≠ **doctor** (醫生)\n      ├── 2. 建議錯配 ── **reducing** (減少) ≠ **eliminating** (完全消除)\n      └── 3. 時間誤判 ── **today** (今天/當天拿到) ≠ **next week** (下週)","quiz":[{"q":"To improve her daily stamina and design a proper eating program, Ms. Reed scheduled a consultation with a certified ________ at our clinic.","o":[["A","receptionist"],["B","cardiologist"],["C","pharmacist"],["D","nutritionist"]],"a":"(D) nutritionist","zh":"為了改善她的日常體力並設計合適的飲食方案，里德女士預約了我們診所的認證「營養師」進行諮詢。","e":"此處考查身分概念。題幹提及「飲食方案（eating program）與諮詢」，應選擇與營養學相關的 (D) nutritionist。其他選項皆不符合職責範疇。"},{"q":"The program guidelines highly recommend ________ the consumption of manufactured foods to support long-term heart health.","o":[["A","advertising"],["B","eliminating"],["C","reducing"],["D","manufacturing"]],"a":"(C) reducing","zh":"計畫指南強烈建議「減少」加工食品的攝取，以維持長期的心臟健康。","e":"此題考查建議動詞的錯配陷阱。專家的建議是「減少（reducing = decrease）」，而非完全禁止或「消除（eliminating）」，故選 (C)。"},{"q":"According to the email reminder, all seminar participants should arrive fifteen minutes early to finish their ________.","o":[["A","billing invoice"],["B","consent paperwork"],["C","diet assessment form"],["D","insurance policy"]],"a":"(C) diet assessment form","zh":"根據電子郵件提醒，所有研討會參與者應提早15分鐘到達，以填寫完他們的「飲食評估表」。","e":"時程與表格細節。講義在工作坊流程中明確指出提早15分鐘是為了完成「飲食評估表（diet assessment form）」，故選 (C)。"},{"q":"The front-desk supervisor assured the client that her customized wellness plan would be processed and delivered ________.","o":[["A","next week"],["B","within fifteen days"],["C","next Monday"],["D","today"]],"a":"(D) today","zh":"前台主管向客戶保證，她的客製化健康計畫將在「今天」處理並交付。","e":"時程交付陷阱。多益極常利用 next week 或 15天內等日常延遲時間來進行干擾，但本單元核心計畫是「當天取得計畫（customized plan today）」，故選 (D)。"},{"q":"In the health report, the phrase \"weight loss of 15 pounds\" can be paraphrased as which of the following?","o":[["A","total increase of 15 percent"],["B","body fat of 15 kilograms"],["C","reduced weight of 15 pounds"],["D","weekly limitation of 15 weeks"]],"a":"(C) reduced weight of 15 pounds","zh":"在健康報告中，「減重15磅」一詞可以代換為下列哪一個選項？","e":"數據代換考點。weight loss = reduced weight，數值單位 15 pounds 必須精確對應，故選 (C)。"}],"say":["I'm here for my appointment with the nutritionist.","I've been exploring different meal plans to improve my energy levels.","Welcome to our wellness center.","The specialist recommended reducing processed foods in my daily meals.","Based on dietary restrictions and healthy lifestyle goals.","Complete your diet assessment form.","Creating personalized nutrition plans.","Organic options with natural ingredients.","All aspects of healthy eating.","Our wellness center offers personalized consultations with certified nutrition experts.","How to read food labels for calories, protein, sugar, and fat.","You'll receive a customized plan today."]},"14-4":{"tree":"【Ch14-4 醫療行政與設施：保險理賠與系統管理 Medical Administration & Facilities】\n │\n ├── 🔴 S - Situation (情境確認：識別問題來源)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 識別問題來源、進行資料溯源\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **billing statement** (帳單), **copayment** (部分負擔), **insurance** (保險), **coverage** (保險給付範圍)\n │    ├── 必考句型 ── \"I'm calling about my billing statement.\" (我打電話詢問我的帳單) / \"There seems to be an error with my copayment amount.\" (我的部分負擔金額似乎有誤) / \"Your insurance has approved coverage for the upcoming procedure.\" (您的保險已批准即將進行的醫療程序給付)\n │    └── 觀念釐清 ── **copayment** = 部分負擔（非全額）；**coverage** = 保險給付範圍；**deductible** = 自付額（已達標準）\n │\n ├── 📋 T - Task (任務說明：查證資料正確)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 查證資料正確、進行病患核對\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **medical records** (病歷), **patient data** (病人資料), **digital system** (數位系統), **medical history** (病史)\n │    ├── 必考句型 ── \"Let me check your medical records in our digital system.\" (讓我在數位系統中查看您的病歷) / \"Can you provide your patient data and insurance information?\" (您能提供病人資料和保險資訊嗎？) / \"The deductible was already met.\" (自付額已經達到)\n │    └── 📍 資料類型 ── **Policy number** (保單號碼), **Lab results** (檢驗結果), **Medical history** (病史記錄)\n │\n ├── 💡 A - Action (行動方案：更新系統資料)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 更新系統資料、進行流程優化\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **electronic health record platform** (電子健康記錄平台), **consent form** (同意書), **digital system** (數位系統), **patient portal** (病患入口網站)\n │    ├── 必考句型 ── \"Please update your information in our electronic health record platform.\" (請在我們的電子健康記錄平台更新您的資訊) / \"I submitted the consent form and updated my medical history last week.\" (我上週提交了同意書並更新了病史) / \"All lab results and documents are processed faster now.\" (所有檢驗結果和文件現在處理更快)\n │    └── 🔄 計畫內容 ── **Automated delivery** (自動傳送) / **Electronic forms** (電子表單) / **Online access** (線上存取)\n │\n ├── ✅ R - Result (結果確認：確保準確處理)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 確保準確處理、進行結果審批\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **claim** (理賠申請), **facility** (設施), **patient care technology** (病患照護技術), **hospital complex** (醫院綜合大樓)\n │    ├── 必考句型 ── \"Our medical office will send it within three business days.\" (我們的醫療診所將在三個工作日內寄出) / \"Our newly renovated facility incorporates the latest patient care technology.\" (我們新裝修的設施融入了最新的病患照護技術) / \"The hospital complex billing department will also send a confirmation.\" (醫院綜合大樓的帳務部門也會寄送確認)\n │    └── 📱 改善項目 ── **Faster processing** (更快處理) / **Enhanced security** (加強安全) / **Reduced errors** (減少錯誤)\n │\n ├── 💰 保險費用結構 (Insurance Cost Structure)\n │    ├── **Copayment (部分負擔)** ── 固定金額 (Fixed amount)，每次就診支付\n │    ├── **Deductible (自付額)** ── 年度門檻 (Annual threshold)，達標後全額給付\n │    ├── **Coverage (保險給付)** ── 批准的程序，給付範圍確認\n │    └── **理賠流程** ── 1. Submit claim ➔ 2. Insurance approval ➔ 3. Coverage confirmation ➔ 4. Billing adjustment\n │\n ├── 💻 數位系統升級 (System Transition)\n │    ├── **升級項目 (This weekend)** ── 系統升級 (System upgrade), 資料轉移 (Data migration)\n │    ├── **取消項目 (Eliminated items)** ── 紙本病史表 (Paper medical history forms), 人工處理 (Manual processing)\n │    ├── **新功能 (New features)** ── 即時通知 (Instant notifications), 自助服務機 (Self-service kiosks), 自動檢驗結果 (Automated lab results)\n │    ├── 💡 解題技巧 ── **eliminated** = 已取消的、**upgraded** = 升級的、**digitized** = 數位化的\n │    └── **時程安排** ── 7月1日生效 (Effective July 1), 下個月開始 (Starting next month), 三個工作日內 (Within three business days)\n │\n ├── 🏥 醫療設施現代化 (Facility Modernization)\n │    ├── **翻新設施 (Renovated facility)** ── 最新技術 (Latest technology), 病患照護重點 (Patient care focus)\n │    ├── **醫院綜合大樓 (Hospital complex)** ── 多個部門、整合服務\n │    ├── **醫療診所 (Medical office)** ── 掛號櫃台、帳務部門\n │    └── **服務地點** ── 掛號櫃台 (實體協助)、病患入口網站 (線上)、醫療診所 (實體)\n │\n ├── 🔄 同義轉換 (Paraphrase Map)\n │    ├── 保險相關 ── **billing statement** = invoice = bill / **copayment** = copay = partial payment / **deductible** = out-of-pocket threshold / **coverage** = insurance benefit = reimbursement / **claim** = reimbursement request = insurance filing\n │    └── 設施服務 ── **medical office** = clinic = healthcare facility / **hospital complex** = medical center = healthcare campus / **renovated** = upgraded = modernized = refurbished / **patient care technology** = healthcare technology = medical equipment\n │\n └── ⚠ 三大高頻防雷陷阱 (Common Traps)\n      ├── 1. 費用混淆 ── **copayment** (部分負擔) ≠ **deductible** (自付額) ≠ **total** (各項保險費用概念不可混淆)\n      ├── 2. 時間錯配 ── **this weekend** (升級時間) ≠ **next month** (新政策生效時程)\n      └── 3. 地點誤判 ── **registration desk** (掛號櫃台求助) ≠ **billing department** (帳務部門處理費用)","quiz":[{"q":"Since Ms. Lopez has already met her annual ________, she only needs to pay a small copayment of twenty dollars for today’s clinic visit.","o":[["A","premium"],["B","deductible"],["C","reimbursement"],["D","transaction"]],"a":"(B) deductible","zh":"由於洛佩茲女士已經達到了她的年度自付額門檻，她今天的診所就診只需要支付二十美元的少額部分負擔。","e":"此處為保險費用結構題。題幹提及「看病付固定小額部分負擔（copayment），是因為年度累計的門檻已過」，對應自付額，故選 (B) deductible。"},{"q":"To improve administrative efficiency and reduce errors, the hospital complex has completely ________ paper medical history forms starting this month.","o":[["A","renovated"],["B","eliminated"],["C","registered"],["D","processed"]],"a":"(B) eliminated","zh":"為了提高行政效率並減少錯誤，醫院綜合大樓從本月開始已完全「取消」紙本病史表。","e":"此題考查系統升級的動詞搭配。取消舊紙本病歷以配合數位化，應使用消滅/取消的 (B) eliminated。"},{"q":"Although the digital platform's data migration and system upgrade will take place ________, the new electronic health record policy will not officially go into effect until starting next month.","o":[["A","within three business days"],["B","starting next month"],["C","this weekend"],["D","yesterday morning"]],"a":"(C) this weekend","zh":"雖然數位平台的資料轉移與系統升級將於「本週末」進行，但新的電子健康記錄政策要到下個月才會正式生效。","e":"此題考查時間錯配陷阱。系統升級（upgrade）是在「本週末（this weekend）」，政策生效（effect）是在「下個月（starting next month）」，故升級時間應選 (C)。"},{"q":"In the service announcement, the administrative supervisor writes: \"Our **medical office** will send the confirmation statement within three business days.\" The phrase \"**medical office**\" is closest in meaning to which of the following?","o":[["A","hospital complex"],["B","registration desk"],["C","clinic"],["D","patient portal"]],"a":"(C) clinic","zh":"在服務公告中，行政主管寫道：「我們的醫療診所將在三個工作日內寄出確認單。」短語 \"medical office\" 與下列哪一個單字的意思最接近？","e":"設施代換考點。根據同義轉換表，medical office = clinic = healthcare facility。故 (C) 為最精準的代換。"},{"q":"A patient is calling because she needs in-person assistance to update her digital consent form. According to the help guidelines, where should she go?","o":[["A","To the billing department"],["B","To the registration desk"],["C","To the hospital complex archives"],["D","To the physical therapy center"]],"a":"(B) To the registration desk","zh":"一位病患打電話來，因為她需要專人親自協助更新她的數位同意書。根據協助指南，她應該去哪裡？","e":"此處考查地點誤判陷阱。需要專人「實體協助」時，應去掛號櫃台（registration desk），而非處理費用的 billing department（帳務部門），故選 (B)。"}],"say":["I'm calling about my billing statement.","There seems to be an error with my copayment amount.","Your insurance has approved coverage for the upcoming procedure.","Let me check your medical records in our digital system.","Can you provide your patient data and insurance information?","The deductible was already met.","Please update your information in our electronic health record platform.","I submitted the consent form and updated my medical history last week.","All lab results and documents are processed faster now.","Our medical office will send it within three business days.","Our newly renovated facility incorporates the latest patient care technology.","The hospital complex billing department will also send a confirmation."]},"14-5":{"tree":"【Ch14-5 健身與健康活動：會員服務與健康計畫 Fitness & Health Activities】\n │\n ├── 🔴 S - Situation (了解需求：掌握客戶意圖)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 掌握客戶意圖、評估會員需求與資格\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **fitness center** (健身中心) / **gym** (健身房) / **membership options** (會員選項) / **wellness program** (健康計畫)\n │    ├── 必考句型 ── \"Are you interested in our membership options?\" / \"I'd like to know about your wellness program.\" / \"Join today and enjoy unlimited use.\"\n │    └── 注意事項 ── **membership** (會員資格) / **wellness program** (健康計畫) / **corporate membership** (企業會員)\n │\n ├── 📋 T - Task (確認細節：釐清具體需求)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 釐清具體需求，確認健身項目、時間、地點、器材\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **150 minutes weekly** (每週150分鐘) / **morning session** (早晨課程) / **exercise equipment** (運動器材) / **second floor** (二樓)\n │    ├── 必考句型 ── \"The program requires participants to complete 150 minutes of activity weekly.\" / \"My morning session starts at 7:30 in the main studio on the second floor.\" / \"Do I need to bring my own exercise equipment?\"\n │    └── 時間與地點框架 ── **7:30 AM 開始時間** / **每週150分鐘活動要求** / **Tuesday & Thursday 固定時段**\n │\n ├── 💡 A - Action (提供方案：展示服務優勢)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 展示服務優勢與體驗設計\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **unlimited use** (無限使用) / **yoga/aerobics/strength training** (瑜伽/有氧/重訓) / **free assessment** (免費評估) / **priority booking** (優先預約)\n │    ├── 特別優惠 ── **month-end promotion** (月底促銷) / **corporate membership** (企業會員) / **insurance discounts** (保險折扣)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── \"Join today and enjoy unlimited use of all our equipment and classes.\" / \"We offer yoga, aerobics, and strength training.\" / \"Current membership holders receive priority booking.\"\n │\n ├── ✅ R - Result (達成共識：確認行動方案)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 確認行動方案與落實方案\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **registration** (註冊) / **starting date** (開始日期) / **health fair** (健康博覽會) / **corporate code** (企業代碼)\n │    ├── 後續活動 ── **health fair** (健康博覽會) / **monthly assessment** (每月評估) / **attendance tracking** (出席追蹤)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── \"Full benefits starting July 1st.\" / \"Register at the front desk.\" / \"Contact HR for your corporate membership code.\"\n │\n ├── 💳 会員權益結構 (Membership Benefits)\n │    ├── **核心服務** ── Unlimited access (無限使用權：所有器材、課程、延長時段) / Special services (特殊服務：私人訓練、復健、評估)\n │    └── **優惠條件** ── Corporate membership (企業會員), Insurance discounts (保險折扣), Priority booking (優先預約)\n │\n ├── ⏰ 時間地點管理 (Schedule Details)\n │    ├── **固定時段** ── Morning session 早晨課程：7:30 AM開始、二樓、主教室、週二週四\n │    └── **重要日期** ── 週一啟動計畫, 下週六健康博覽會, June 20th(Part 7), July 1st完整福利生效\n │\n ├── 🏃 課程類型與規定 (Class Types & Rules)\n │    ├── **課程選項** ── Yoga (瑜伽), Aerobics (有氧), Strength training (重量訓練), Personal training (私人訓練)\n │    └── **參與要求** ── 每週150分鐘 (150 minutes weekly)：計畫要求、保險資格 (Insurance eligibility)\n │\n ├── 🔄 同義轉換 (Paraphrase Map)\n │    ├── 會員服務 ── **membership** = enrollment = subscription = registration / **join today** = sign up now = enroll immediately / **unlimited use** = full access = unrestricted entry\n │    ├── 活動課程 ── **fitness class / wellness program** = workout session / health initiative / exercise program / fitness plan / **150 minutes** = two and a half hours = 2.5 hours\n │    ├── 時間地點 ── **morning session** = AM class = early workout / **second floor** = upstairs = level 2 / **main studio** = exercise room = classroom\n │    └── 優惠權益 ── **special offer** = promotion = limited-time opportunity / **priority booking** = advance reservation = preferential scheduling / **insurance discounts** = coverage benefits = premium reductions\n │\n └── ⚠ 三大高頻防雷陷阱 (Common Traps)\n      ├── 1. 時間混淆 ── **Monday launch** (週一啟動) ≠ **Saturday fair** (下週六健康博覽會)\n      ├── 2. 數字錯配 ── **150 minutes** (每週150分鐘) ≠ **120 minutes** (兩小時)\n      └── 3. 地點誤判 ── **second floor / upstairs** (二樓/樓上) ≠ **first floor** (一樓大廳)","quiz":[{"q":"To qualify for the company's insurance discount, employees are required to participate in at least ________ of exercise weekly.","o":[["A","two hours"],["B","two and a half hours"],["C","three hours"],["D","four hours"]],"a":"(B) two and a half hours","zh":"為了符合公司的保險折扣資格，員工被要求每週至少參與「兩個半小時」的運動。","e":"此處為同義字代換計算題。講義中指出，健康計畫每週需要完成 150 分鐘，在選項中會被代換成兩個半小時（two and a half hours / 2.5 hours），120分鐘（two hours）是強烈干擾項，故選 (B)。"},{"q":"Members who sign up for the premium subscription will enjoy ________ entry to all fitness classes and exercise rooms.","o":[["A","restricted"],["B","registered"],["C","provisional"],["D","unrestricted"]],"a":"(D) unrestricted","zh":"註冊高級訂閱的會員將享有「無限制的」進入所有健身課程與健身教室的權益。","e":"此題考查「無限使用（unlimited use / access）」的同義代換。根據轉換表，unlimited 可代換為 unrestricted（無限制的），故選 (D)。"},{"q":"A client wants to attend the early workout session. According to the gym schedule, on which days is the morning session held?","o":[["A","Monday and Wednesday"],["B","Tuesday and Thursday"],["C","Friday and Saturday"],["D","Every day of the week"]],"a":"(B) Tuesday and Thursday","zh":"一位客戶想要參加清晨的健身課程。根據健身房時間表，早晨課程是在星期幾舉行？","e":"此題針對時間安排細節進行考核。講義在固定時段中明確指出，AM class / morning session 是在「週二與週四（Tuesday and Thursday）」的 7:30 AM，週一（Monday）是計畫啟動日，下週六（Saturday）是博覽會，不可混淆，故選 (B)。"},{"q":"The instructor announced that the specialized yoga class will be held in the main studio, which is located ________.","o":[["A","on the first floor"],["B","upstairs"],["C","in the lobby"],["D","outside the facility"]],"a":"(B) upstairs","zh":"教練宣布專門的瑜伽課程將在主教室舉行，該教室位於「樓上」。","e":"此題考查地點代換。講義中指出，早晨課程與主教室（main studio）皆位於「二樓（second floor）」，轉換表將其代換為 upstairs（樓上）或 level 2。一樓為干擾，故選 (B)。"},{"q":"To register for the corporate membership and receive the discount, employees must contact human resources to obtain their company ________.","o":[["A","promotion"],["B","registration"],["C","code"],["D","benefit"]],"a":"(C) code","zh":"若要註冊企業會員方案並獲得折扣，員工必須聯繫人力資源部門以取得他們的公司「代碼」。","e":"此題考查搭配詞彙。講義指出，要獲得企業會員（corporate membership）福利，需聯繫 HR 以取得「公司代碼（corporate code / company code）」，故選 (C)。"}],"say":["Are you interested in our membership options?","I'd like to know about your wellness program.","Join today and enjoy unlimited use.","The program requires participants to complete 150 minutes of activity weekly.","My morning session starts at 7:30 in the main studio on the second floor.","Do I need to bring my own exercise equipment?","Join today and enjoy unlimited use of all our equipment and classes.","We offer yoga, aerobics, and strength training.","Current membership holders receive priority booking.","Full benefits starting July 1st.","Register at the front desk.","Contact HR for your corporate membership code."]},"15-1":{"tree":"【Ch15-1 銀行與個人理財：申請與服務 Banking & Personal Finance】\n │\n ├── 🔴 S - Situation (情境確認：掌握客戶意圖與需求)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 掌握客戶意圖、貸款申請、查詢餘額\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **loan application** (貸款申請), **account status** (帳戶狀態), **current balance** (目前餘額)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── I submitted a loan application last week. / Has my application been approved yet? / Can I also apply for a credit card?\n │\n ├── 📋 T - Task (任務說明：解釋申請流程與時程)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 說明工作天數、要求補件、完成文件\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **business days** (工作天), **application review** (申請審核), **required documents** (必要文件), **approval process** (批准流程)\n │    ├── ⏰ 時間框架 ── **within 5 business days** (五個工作天內), **starting November 1st** (從11月1日開始), **for your first year** (第一年期間)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── The bank manager will review your loan application within five business days. / Your application requires additional investment statements. / Please visit our main branch to complete the paperwork.\n │\n ├── 💡 A - Action (行動方案：提供具體服務與設定)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 執行客戶要求、轉帳存款、設定網路銀行\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **transfer money** (轉帳), **withdraw cash** (提取現金), **make deposit** (存款), **check balance** (查詢餘額)\n │    ├── 📱 服務管道 ── **mobile application** (手機App), **online banking** (網路銀行), **branch ATM** (分行提款機)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── You can transfer money between accounts using our mobile application. / There's a small fee for withdrawing cash from other banks' machines. / Check your account balance online anytime.\n │\n ├── ✅ R - Result (結果確認：追蹤服務成效與優惠)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 確認批准狀態、費用減免、帳戶升級\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **approved** (已批准), **waived** (減免), **upgraded** (升級), **confirmed** (確認)\n │    ├── 📊 服務優惠 ── **interest rate 4.5%** (利率4.5%), **reduced fee from $5 to $2** (手續費從5元降至2元), **higher interest rates** (更高的利率)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── Your application was approved yesterday. / We're waiving all fees for your first year. / Your savings account has been upgraded to premium tier.\n │\n ├── 🔄 同義轉換 (Paraphrase Map)\n │    ├── 申請狀態 ── submit = file = send in = turn in / review = examine = assess = evaluate / approve = accept = authorize = grant / pending = under review = being processed\n │    └── 費用詞彙 ── waive = exempt = eliminate / reduce = lower = decrease / charge = fee = cost / free = no charge = complimentary\n │\n └── ⚠ 四大高頻防雷陷阱 (Common Traps)\n      ├── 1. 申請混淆 ── **loan application** (貸款) vs **credit card application** (信用卡) ➔ 貸款已准，但信用卡因缺投資證明仍在審核中\n      ├── 2. 費用誤解 ── **own ATM** (自家提款機提款免費) vs **other ATM** (他行提款機手續費3元) ➔ 只有在自家提款機才免費\n      ├── 3. 時間錯誤 ── **review time** (5天內審核) ≠ **start date** (新福利於11月1日生效)\n      └── 4. 狀態誤判 ── **approved** (已批准) ≠ **pending** (待審中) ≠ **rejected** (被拒絕)","quiz":[{"q":"First National Bank announced that they are ________ all transaction fees for premium tier customers during their first year of membership.","o":[["A","charging"],["B","waiving"],["C","transferring"],["D","depositing"]],"a":"(B) waiving","zh":"第一國家銀行宣布，他們將在第一年會員期間免除 premium tier 客戶的所有交易費用。","e":"此處考查費用豁免單字。waive 代表「免除、豁免手續費」，與講義中「waiving all fees for your first year」完全吻合，(B) 為正確答案。"},{"q":"The loan department clerk confirmed that the bank manager will review the loan application within five ________.","o":[["A","savings accounts"],["B","monthly statements"],["C","business days"],["D","financial records"]],"a":"(C) business days","zh":"貸款部門行員確認，銀行經理將在五個工作天內審查貸款申請案。","e":"時程時限題。多益必考審核時程為「五個工作天（five business days）」，非 savings accounts 或 statements，故選 (C)。"},{"q":"According to the bank's fee policy, withdrawals from any branch ATM are free, while transactions at other banks’ machines incur a three-dollar ________.","o":[["A","rate"],["B","return"],["C","portfolio"],["D","fee"]],"a":"(D) fee","zh":"根據銀行的手續費政策，在任何分行提款機提款皆為免費，而在其他銀行的機器進行交易則會產生 3 美元的費用。","e":"手續費搭配詞。在跨行提款時所收取的固定金額，多益專用詞彙為 fee (手續費/規費)，而 rate 通常指利率或比率，故選 (D)。"},{"q":"While Mr. Thompson's loan application has been approved, his credit card application is currently ________ because it requires additional investment statements.","o":[["A","waived"],["B","deposited"],["C","pending"],["D","upgraded"]],"a":"(C) pending","zh":"雖然湯普森先生的貸款申請已經獲准，但他的信用卡申請目前仍在「待審中」，因為該申請需要額外的投資證明。","e":"此題考查「申請混淆與狀態誤判」陷阱。信用卡因缺件（additional statements）仍在「審核中（pending / under review）」，而非已批准（approved）或已免除（waived），故選 (C)。"},{"q":"National Trust Bank announced that starting November 1st, customers can transfer money between accounts instantly using their newly updated ________.","o":[["A","initial deposit"],["B","main branch"],["C","business card"],["D","mobile application"]],"a":"(D) mobile application","zh":"國家信託銀行宣布，自 11 月 1 日起，客戶可以使用他們全新升級的手機 App 在帳戶間進行即時轉帳。","e":"管道搭配詞。轉帳（transfer money）的數位管道是透過手機應用程式（mobile application），與 initial deposit (首次存款) 或 main branch (總行) 無關，故選 (D)。"}],"say":["I submitted a loan application last week.","Has my application been approved yet?","Can I also apply for a credit card?","The bank manager will review your loan application within five business days.","Your application requires additional investment statements.","Please visit our main branch to complete the paperwork.","You can transfer money between accounts using our mobile application.","There's a small fee for withdrawing cash from other banks' machines.","Check your account balance online anytime.","Your application was approved yesterday.","We're waiving all fees for your first year.","Your savings account has been upgraded to premium tier."]},"15-2":{"tree":"【Ch15-2 企業財務管理：預算與報告 Finance Management】\n │\n ├── 🔴 S - Situation (情境確認：掌握財務狀態與季度營收)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 掌握財務狀態、季度營收、通報會議召開\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **financial report** (財務報告), **quarterly revenue** (季度收入), **budget meeting** (預算會議), **annual report** (年度報告)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── Have you finished reviewing the financial report? / The accounting department needs three more days to complete the annual report. / I'm writing to share our third-quarter results.\n │\n ├── 📋 T - Task (任務確認：明確會前工作與時程要求)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 審查費用報告、核對付款時程、安排截止日期\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **budget proposal** (預算提案), **expense reports** (費用報告), **payment schedule** (付款時程), **deadline** (截止期限)\n │    ├── 📌 任務優先順序 ── 立即任務 (review before tomorrow), 短期任務 (complete in three days), 長期任務 (submit by month end)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── Please review these expense reports before the budget meeting tomorrow. / Each department must provide detailed payment schedules. / Submit your final budget proposals by September 30th.\n │\n ├── 💡 A - Action (執行方案：採取具體行動與流程)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 檢查發票準確性、估算成本、會計部確認\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **process invoices** (處理發票), **estimate costs** (估算成本), **verify accuracy** (確認準確性), **approve budget** (核准預算)\n │    ├── 🔄 執行順序 ── check ──> review ──> approve ──> submit\n │    └── 必考句型 ── I need to check several invoices for accuracy. / I'll look at them tonight. / Accounting confirmed it yesterday.\n │\n ├── ✅ R - Result (結果確認：追蹤財務成效與利潤)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 營收超出預期、高於預測、正向增長\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **profit margin** (利潤率), **growth trend** (成長趨勢), **exceed expectations** (超出預期), **above projections** (高於預測), **positive growth** (正向成長)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── Our quarterly revenue increased more than we originally expected. / The profit margin still looks healthy despite the cost increase. / Overall profit remains 15% above projections.\n │\n ├── 🔄 同義轉換 (Paraphrase Map)\n │    ├── 數據變化 ── increase = go up = rise = grow / decrease = go down = drop = decline / exceed = surpass = above = more than expectation / estimate = projection = forecast\n │    ├── 財務術語 ── revenue = income = earnings = sales / expense = cost = expenditure = spending / profit = margin = gain = earnings / budget = financial plan\n │    └── 完成狀態 ── finished reviewing = completed the review = done with examination / almost done = nearly finished = close to completion / needs three more days = requires additional 72 hours\n │\n └── ⚠ 三大高頻防雷陷阱 (Common Traps)\n      ├── 1. 數字混淆 ── **actual** (實際值 420 萬) ≠ **estimate** (預估值 380 萬) ➔ 實際營收多出預估 40 萬美元\n      ├── 2. 時間錯置 ── **tomorrow morning** (預算會議/審查截止) ≠ **three more days** (年度報告完成時間) ➔ 報告完成是在會議之後\n      └── 3. 責任歸屬 ── **CFO** (財務長) 要求各部門經理 (Managers) 於週五前提交付款時程與提案","quiz":[{"q":"The CFO announced that the accounting department requires ________ more days to complete the annual report due to invoice processing delays.","o":[["A","three"],["B","five"],["C","ten"],["D","fifteen"]],"a":"(A) three","zh":"財務長宣布，由於發票處理延遲，會計部門需要額外三天來完成年度報告。","e":"時間細節題。根據聽力與閱讀原文指出「needs three more days (需要再三天)」，即為 (A) three。"},{"q":"Although expenses increased by 12 percent, the CFO confirmed that our ________ still looks healthy and strong.","o":[["A","check scanning"],["B","billing statement"],["C","profit margin"],["D","transaction fee"]],"a":"(C) profit margin","zh":"儘管支出增加了 12%，財務長確認我們的利潤率看起來仍然健康且強勁。","e":"財務成效單字。指出成本增加但利潤（profit margin）仍然健康的表達，與對白中「The profit margin still looks healthy despite the cost increase」相符，故選 (C)。"},{"q":"All department heads are strictly required to submit their budget proposals and ________ by Friday afternoon.","o":[["A","branch ATMs"],["B","payment schedules"],["C","savings accounts"],["D","investment portfolios"]],"a":"(B) payment schedules","zh":"所有部門主管被嚴格要求在週五下午之前提交他們的預算提案與付款時程表。","e":"主管職責搭配。主管在預算規劃時，被要求提交 budget proposals 與 payment schedules (付款時程/進度表)，故選 (B)。"},{"q":"The quarterly financial review indicated that our actual revenue reached $4.2 million, which ________ our original estimate of $3.8 million.","o":[["A","decreased"],["B","declined"],["C","dropped"],["D","exceeded"]],"a":"(D) exceeded","zh":"季度財務審查指出，我們的實際收入達到了 420 萬美元，這超出了我們原先估計的 380 萬美元。","e":"數據變化單字。420 萬大於預估的 380 萬，因此是「超出、高於（exceeded / surpassed）」，其餘選項皆為減少，故選 (D)。"},{"q":"Sarah was requested to verify several invoices for accuracy before the upcoming ________ meeting tomorrow morning at 10 AM.","o":[["A","consultation"],["B","registration"],["C","budget"],["D","orientation"]],"a":"(C) budget","zh":"莎拉被要求在明天早上 10 點即將召開的預算會議前，核對幾張發票的準確性。","e":"會議類型選擇。會前審查費用報告、成本估算是為了明天早上的「預算（budget）」會議，故選 (C)。"}],"say":["Have you finished reviewing the financial report?","The accounting department needs three more days to complete the annual report.","I'm writing to share our third-quarter results.","Please review these expense reports before the budget meeting tomorrow.","Each department must provide detailed payment schedules.","Submit your final budget proposals by September 30th.","I need to check several invoices for accuracy.","I'll look at them tonight.","Accounting confirmed it yesterday.","Our quarterly revenue increased more than we originally expected.","The profit margin still looks healthy despite the cost increase.","Overall profit remains 15% above projections."]},"15-3":{"tree":"【Ch15-3 付款與資金流：帳單與交易 Payment & Cash Flow】\n │\n ├── 🔴 S - Situation (情境確認：了解付款疑慮與帳款)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 釐清帳單金額問題、解釋額外費用與稅金\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **bill** (帳單), **charge** (收費), **tax** (稅金), **total** (總計), **additional charges** (額外費用)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── I'd like to inquire about this bill. / The total seems higher than the original price quoted. / I wasn't aware of the additional charges. / What if I need a refund later?\n │\n ├── 📋 T - Task (任務確認：明確付款期限與條件)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 明確到期日、付款方式、保留交易憑證\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **due date** (到期日), **payment terms** (付款條件), **receipt** (收據), **transaction** (交易)\n │    ├── 📌 時間要求 ── **by the fifteenth** (十五號前), **within 7-10 days** (七到十天內), **effective immediately** (立即生效)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── The payment for last month's services is due by the fifteenth. / Bills not paid by the due date will incur a late charge. / Please retain all transaction documents and receipts.\n │\n ├── 💡 A - Action (執行方案：提供折扣與退款方案)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 執行預付折扣、免除交易手續費、處理退款\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **discount** (折扣), **refund** (退款), **waive** (免除), **purchase** (購買)\n │    ├── 🔄 付款選項 ── **cash payment** (現金付款), **check payment** (支票付款), **advance payment** (預付款)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── We can offer a ten percent discount for orders paid in advance. / I can waive the transaction fee. / Your refund will be processed within seven to ten days. / We're eliminating fees for other payment methods.\n │\n ├── ✅ R - Result (結果確認：完成交易與收據管理)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 收據金額核對、預付優惠套票、辦理銷售撤銷\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **receipt** (收據), **confirmation** (確認), **processed** (已處理), **completed** (已完成)\n │    ├── 📊 交易確認 ── **receipt number** (收據號碼), **transaction ID** (交易編號), **confirmation email** (確認郵件)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── Your receipt will match the total displayed. / The sale of prepaid packages offers additional savings. / Just bring your receipt and we'll handle the sale reversal.\n │\n ├── 🔄 同義轉換 (Paraphrase Map)\n │    ├── 付款動作 ── pay = settle = clear = remit / charge = bill = invoice = debit / refund = reimburse = return = repay / purchase = buy = acquire = obtain\n │    └── 優惠描述 ── offer a discount = provide a reduction / waive fee = eliminate charge / paid in advance = prepayment / additional savings = extra discount\n │\n └── ⚠ 四大高頻防雷陷阱 (Common Traps)\n      ├── 1. 金額混淆 ── **original price** (原價，常不含稅與服務費) vs **final total** (最終總額，含加急費與稅金)\n      ├── 2. 時間誤判 ── **processing time** (退款處理需 7-10 天) vs **due date** (付款於每月的 15 號截止)\n      ├── 3. 優惠條件 ── **advance payment** (預付款) ➔ 只有「服務前預先付清」才享有九折\n      └── 4. 費用項目 ── **waived fees** (免除其他付款交易手續費) vs **remaining charges** (保留 credit card 2% 手續費)","quiz":[{"q":"According to Citywide Utilities' updated procedures, payment for all utility services is due by the ________ of each month.","o":[["A","first"],["B","fifth"],["C","tenth"],["D","fifteenth"]],"a":"(D) fifteenth","zh":"根據城市實業的最新程序，所有公用事業服務的付款截止日為每月的十五號。","e":"時間細節題。根據講義，到期日（due date）統一規定在「每月的十五號（due by the fifteenth）」，故選 (D)。"},{"q":"The customer service representative announced that we can offer a ten percent discount for orders paid in ________.","o":[["A","installment"],["B","arrears"],["C","advance"],["D","person"]],"a":"(C) advance","zh":"客服代表宣布，我們針對預先付清的訂單可以提供百分之十的折扣。","e":"折扣條件片語。多益常考「預先、提前付款（in advance / prepayment）」，「paid in advance」為標準搭配，故選 (C)。"},{"q":"In case of a purchase cancellation, please bring your receipt so that our billing department can process your ________ within seven to ten days.","o":[["A","deductible"],["B","refund"],["C","portfolio"],["D","interest"]],"a":"(B) refund","zh":"如果取消購買，請帶上您的收據，以便我們的計費部門在七到十天內處理您的退款。","e":"退款時程搭配。取消購買後帶收據辦理銷售撤銷，在 7-10 天內處理的款項是 refund (退款)，與保險自付額 (deductible) 或投資組合 (portfolio) 無關，故選 (B)。"},{"q":"Please note that any outstanding bills not paid by the established due date will automatically incur a late charge of ________ monthly.","o":[["A","1.5 percent"],["B","2.8 percent"],["C","4.5 percent"],["D","12 percent"]],"a":"(A) 1.5 percent","zh":"請注意，未在規定到期日前付清的逾期帳單，每月將會自動產生 1.5% 的滯納金。","e":"罰金比例數據。根據 Citywide Utilities 的閱讀原文規定「incur a late charge of 1.5% monthly」，故 (A) 為正確答案。而 2.8% 是 15-1 的存款利率，4.5% 是 15-1 的貸款利率，12% 是 15-2 的費用增加百分比，不可混淆。"},{"q":"While the billing system has eliminated the transaction fee for cash payments, the credit card fee of 2% will ________.","o":[["A","remain"],["B","waive"],["C","decrease"],["D","refund"]],"a":"(A) remain","zh":"雖然計費系統已取消了現金付款的交易手續費，但 2% 的信用卡費用仍將保持不變。","e":"費用項目保留陷阱。聽力獨白中特別警告：信用卡的手續費「仍保持在 2%（remain at 2%）」，只有其他付款手續費被取消（eliminating other fees），故選 (A)。"}],"say":["I'd like to inquire about this bill.","The total seems higher than the original price quoted.","I wasn't aware of the additional charges.","What if I need a refund later?","The payment for last month's services is due by the fifteenth.","Bills not paid by the due date will incur a late charge.","Please retain all transaction documents and receipts.","We can offer a ten percent discount for orders paid in advance.","I can waive the transaction fee.","Your refund will be processed within seven to ten days.","We're eliminating fees for other payment methods.","Your receipt will match the total displayed.","The sale of prepaid packages offers additional savings.","Just bring your receipt and we'll handle the sale reversal."]},"15-4":{"tree":"【Ch15-4 財務專業服務：諮詢與提案 Financial Professional Services】\n │\n ├── 🔴 S - Situation (情境確認：了解客戶與財務狀況)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 評估需求、掌握客戶現況與成長目標\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **consultant / advisor** (顧問), **client** (客戶), **objectives** (目標)\n │    ├── 諮詢類型 ── **financial planning** (財務規劃), **investment consulting** (投資諮詢), **tax advisory** (稅務顧問)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── Thank you for selecting us as your corporate advisor. / The consultation is about your upcoming financial planning. / Please bring all relevant documents and records for review.\n │\n ├── 📋 T - Task (任務確認：規劃合約服務與截止期限)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 明確服務範圍、制定協議、提醒截止日期\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **contract** (合約), **agreement** (協議), **proposal** (提案), **deadline** (截止期限)\n │    ├── 📌 時間要求 ── **before the deadline** (截止期限前), **by this Friday** (本週五前), **within two weeks** (兩週內)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── The service agreement outlines the scope of our consulting engagement. / All tax documents must be submitted before the April deadline. / The contract requires your signature before we can begin. / The deadline for signing is set for March 31st.\n │\n ├── 💡 A - Action (執行方案：提供專業建議與檔案提交)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 簡報提出三個投資選項、審查文件、安全客戶端歸檔\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **presentation** (簡報), **document** (文件), **file** (歸檔), **submit** (提交)\n │    ├── 🔄 服務流程 ── **present options** (提出選項) ──> **review materials** (審查材料) ──> **file paperwork** (歸檔文書)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── The financial consultant will present three different investment options. / We'll review all documents you've provided. / You can submit documents through our secure client portal.\n │\n ├── ✅ R - Result (結果確認：成果檢核與滿意度追蹤)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 合約簽署完成、達成合規、定案會議安排\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **signed** (已簽署), **completed** (已完成), **approved** (已批准), **finalized** (已定案)\n │    ├── 📊 成果指標 ── **compliance achieved** (達成合規), **objectives met** (目標達成), **client satisfaction** (客戶滿意)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── I received the signed documents this morning. / The proposal has been approved by management. / Everything will be finalized at next Tuesday's meeting.\n │\n ├── ⏰ 會議時程管理 (Meeting Schedule Management)\n │    ├── 會議類型 ── Initial consultation (初次諮詢), Presentation meeting (簡報會議), Review session (審查會議), Final meeting (最終定案會議)\n │    └── 安排規律 ── scheduled for next Tuesday (安排在下週二), tomorrow at 2 PM (明天下午 2 點), during today's meeting (在今天的會議中)\n │\n └── ⚠ 三大高頻防雷陷阱 (Common Traps)\n      ├── 1. 時間混淆 ── **tomorrow consultation** (明天簡報會議/初次諮詢) ≠ **next Tuesday finalization** (下週二下午定案會議)\n      ├── 2. 地點錯誤 ── **at your offices** (在客戶的辦公室開會) ➔ 絕對不是「顧問公司 (Excellent Financial) 辦公室」\n      └── 3. 文件類別 ── **tax documents** (四月截止的稅務文件，合規必需) vs **financial records** (簡報會議上需攜帶的歷史財務資料)","quiz":[{"q":"The advisor requested that the client ________ the service agreement before next Tuesday afternoon so they can proceed with the proposal.","o":[["A","resolve"],["B","finalize"],["C","reject"],["D","withdraw"]],"a":"(B) finalize","zh":"顧問要求客戶在下週二下午之前「定案」服務協議，以便他們能夠繼續進行提案。","e":"合約流程動詞。在合約（agreement）最後確認並生效，在多益中最常與 finalize (定案) 或 execute (簽署) 搭配，故選 (B)。"},{"q":"The financial consultant has prepared a comprehensive presentation to outline ________ different investment options tailored to the company's growth goals.","o":[["A","one"],["B","two"],["C","three"],["D","four"]],"a":"(C) three","zh":"財務顧問已準備了一份全面的簡報，以概述三種專為該公司增長目標量身打造的不同投資選擇。","e":"數據細節題。根據 Ch15-4 的對白、獨白與電郵，顧問均表明將會提出「三種不同的投資選擇（three different investment options）」，故選 (C)。"},{"q":"To ensure regulatory ________, all necessary tax documents must be submitted to our office before the April deadline.","o":[["A","compliance"],["B","restriction"],["C","projection"],["D","deduction"]],"a":"(A) compliance","zh":"為確保符合法規，所有必要的稅務文件必須在四月截止日期前提交至我們的辦公室。","e":"合規固定搭配詞。確保法規遵循的多益高頻字為 regulatory compliance，與講義中的「ensure compliance (確保合規)」相符，故選 (A)。"},{"q":"Clients are encouraged to submit their financial records and tax documents online through our secure client ________.","o":[["A","branch"],["B","portal"],["C","statement"],["D","invoice"]],"a":"(B) portal","zh":"我們鼓勵客戶透過我們安全的客戶入口網站，在線上提交他們的財務記錄和稅務文件。","e":"提交管道代換。安全的線上文件傳輸系統，多益專用字為 client portal (客戶入口網站)，與分行 (branch) 或發票 (invoice) 無關，故選 (B)。"},{"q":"In Robert Lee's email, the consulting advisor confirmed that the review meeting will take place tomorrow at ________ offices.","o":[["A","the bank's"],["B","Excellent Financial's"],["C","the client's (your)"],["D","the tax agency's"]],"a":"(C) the client's (your)","zh":"在羅伯特·李的電子郵件中，諮詢顧問確認審查會議明天將在客戶的（您的）辦公室舉行。","e":"此題考查「地點錯誤」陷阱。電子郵件中提及「at your offices (在您的辦公室)」，由於這封信是寄給客戶 Jennifer Williams，因此開會地點是在「客戶的辦公室（the client's offices）」，而非顧問公司辦公室，故選 (C)。"}],"say":["Thank you for selecting us as your corporate advisor.","The consultation is about your upcoming financial planning.","Please bring all relevant documents and records for review.","The service agreement outlines the scope of our consulting engagement.","All tax documents must be submitted before the April deadline.","The contract requires your signature before we can begin.","The deadline for signing is set for March 31st.","The financial consultant will present three different investment options.","We'll review all documents you've provided.","You can submit documents through our secure client portal.","I received the signed documents this morning.","The proposal has been approved by management.","Everything will be finalized at next Tuesday's meeting."]},"16-1":{"tree":"【Ch16-1 產品創新與市場競爭 Product Innovation & Market Competition】\n │\n ├── 🔴 S - Situation (評估現狀：了解市場需求)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 識別市場偏好、評估大眾對產品品質擔憂\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **new product development** (新產品開發), **market research** (市場研究), **customer feedback** (客戶回饋)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── We conducted market research before launching the product line. / The survey results show some concerns about quality.\n │\n ├── 📋 T - Task (規劃開發：制定創新策略)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 釐清研發原型改進細節、追蹤研發里程碑\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **prototype** (原型), **development team** (開發團隊), **innovation features** (創新功能), **competition** (競爭)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── The development team will test the new product design next month. / Following successful prototype completion.\n │\n ├── 💡 A - Action (執行創新：實施開發測試)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 安排內外部雙重測試機制、確實記錄測試手續\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **testing phase** (測試階段), **internal teams** (內部團隊), **selected customers** (選定客戶), **quality checks** (品質檢查)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── Testing will involve both internal teams and selected customers. / Each phase requires careful documentation.\n │\n ├── ✅ R - Result (確認成果：評估市場表現)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 鎖定目標行銷區隔對手、填補30%高性價比缺口\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **full market launch** (全面推出), **differentiator** (差異化特徵), **30% gap in the market** (30%市場缺口)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── We should be ready for a full market launch in three months. / Combining quality with affordability.\n │\n ├── ⏱ 研發時程黃金管理 (Development Cycle Timeline)\n │    ├── Research 研究階段 ── **six months of intensive research** (六個月密集研發)\n │    ├── Testing 測試階段 ── **next month** (下個月進行)\n │    └── Launch 推出階段 ── **in three months / target June** (三個月後/目標六月全面推出)\n │\n └── ⚠ 三大高頻防雷陷阱 (Common Traps)\n      ├── 1. 時間混淆 ── 研發花了 6 個月，下個月才要進行測試，3 個月後正式上市\n      ├── 2. 數據誤記 ── Part 4 聽力的調查人數是 500 人，而 Part 7 閱讀的調查人數則是 1,000 人\n      └── 3. 對象不清 ── 產品測試不是只給員工測，而是同時包含「內部團隊 (internal teams) 與選定客戶 (selected customers)」","quiz":[{"q":"Before the final launch of their upgraded software, the design team decided to test the ________ among a select group of beta users.","o":[["A","qualification"],["B","prototype"],["C","standard"],["D","competition"]],"a":"(B) prototype","zh":"在升級版軟體最終推出之前，設計團隊決定在一組精選的測試使用者中測試該原型。","e":"研發階段專有名詞。多益中「正式量產/上市前」所測試的初步樣機、樣品即為 (B) prototype。"},{"q":"The market research department’s survey included ________ participants, which helped identify critical quality concerns before production.","o":[["A","150"],["B","500"],["C","1,000"],["D","1,500"]],"a":"(B) 500","zh":"市場研究部門的調查包括了 500 名參與者，這有助於在生產前識別出關鍵的品質擔憂。","e":"此題考查 Part 4 獨白中的數據記憶。獨白中明確提及 \"The survey included 500 participants\"，故選 (B)。1000 人是 Part 7 閱讀中的數據。"},{"q":"According to the preliminary schedule, the development team will initiate the testing phase ________, with a full launch targeted in three months.","o":[["A","next month"],["B","six months ago"],["C","within two weeks"],["D","next year"]],"a":"(A) next month","zh":"根據初步時程表，開發團隊將在下個月啟動測試階段，並在三個月後實現全面推出的目標。","e":"時程管理考點。根據對話與獨白，測試安排在「下個月（next month）」進行，故選 (A)。"},{"q":"To differentiate their products from the ________, GlobalTech focus heavily on combining premium quality with affordability.","o":[["A","validation"],["B","supplier"],["C","competition"],["D","portfolio"]],"a":"(C) competition","zh":"為了使他們的產品與競爭對手區別開來，環球科技將重點重重地放在將優質品質與可負擔的價格結合上。","e":"常規搭配詞考點。與 competition（競爭對手）進行差異化區隔是企業發展最愛考的情境，differentiate from competition 完美對應，故選 (C)。"},{"q":"A recent survey revealed a ________ market gap for specialized eco-friendly appliances, which presents an excellent expansion opportunity.","o":[["A","15 percent"],["B","30 percent"],["C","40 percent"],["D","50 percent"]],"a":"(B) 30 percent","zh":"最近的一項調查揭示了專業環保家電存在百分之三十的市場缺口，這提供了一個絕佳的擴張機會。","e":"數據記憶與同義代換。Part 7 指出調查結果顯示市場中有 30% 的缺口（30% gap in the market），故選 (B)。"}],"say":["We conducted market research before launching the product line.","The survey results show some concerns about quality.","The development team will test the new product design next month.","Following successful prototype completion.","Testing will involve both internal teams and selected customers.","Each phase requires careful documentation.","We should be ready for a full market launch in three months.","Combining quality with affordability."]},"16-2":{"tree":"【Ch16-2 策略聯盟與資源整合 Strategic Alliance & Resource Integration】\n │\n ├── 🔴 S - Situation (識別機會：發現合作價值)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 技術資源共享、發掘絕佳合作合資機會\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **partnership agreement** (合作協議), **joint venture** (合資企業), **technology resources** (技術資源)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── Both companies signed a partnership agreement to share technology resources. / It's an excellent collaboration opportunity.\n │\n ├── 📋 T - Task (協商條款：制定合作框架)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 董事會收購條款審核、召開利益相關者分析\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **negotiation** (談判), **merger** (合併), **board approval** (董事會批准), **acquisition terms** (收購條款)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── We need board approval for the acquisition terms. / Months of careful negotiation with key stakeholders.\n │\n ├── 💡 A - Action (執行整合：實施聯盟計畫)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 簽署採購協議降低材料成本、擴張技術轉移網絡\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **consolidated purchasing** (統一採購), **stable resource availability** (穩定資源供應), **contract finalization** (合約定案)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── We're negotiating with several suppliers to reduce material costs. / Contract finalization is expected by month-end.\n │\n ├── ✅ R - Result (實現共贏：評估合作成效)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 目標兩年營收成長40%、整合擴展跨國供應網絡\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **revenue growth** (營收成長), **leverage** (槓桿優勢), **resource integration** (資源整合)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── Projected revenues increasing by 40% within two years. / Strengthens our market position through strategic resource integration.\n │\n ├── 📊 跨國整合關鍵數據 (Integration Key Metrics)\n │    ├── 預估營收成長 ── **40% revenue growth** within two years (兩年內成長 40%)\n │    ├── 跨國網絡規模 ── **150 suppliers** across **fifteen countries** (跨 15 國共 150 家供應商)\n │    └── 協商時間節點 ── Negotiations next Monday (下週一談判) ──> Finalization by month-end (月底完成合約)\n │\n └── ⚠ 三大高頻防雷陷阱 (Common Traps)\n      ├── 1. 談判對象不清 ── 企業是與「供應商 (suppliers)」談判統一採購降成本，而非與「利益相關者 (stakeholders)」或「董事會」談\n      ├── 2. 合作類型混淆 ── 兩家大公司簽署的是「合作/夥伴協議 (partnership)」，並非直接「合併 (merger)」或「收購 (acquisition)」\n      └── 3. 效益數據混亂 ── 40% 是「營收預計成長幅度」，材料成本的調降則是與 150 家供應商談判，兩者概念不同","quiz":[{"q":"Before TechCorp and GlobalTech can implement the joint venture, they must obtain formal ________ from the board of directors.","o":[["A","leverage"],["B","supplier"],["C","approval"],["D","acquisition"]],"a":"(C) approval","zh":"在 TechCorp 和環球科技實施合資企業之前，他們必須獲得董事會的正式批准。","e":"權限動詞搭配詞。在 T - 協商條款中，收購與合資計劃「需要董事會的核准」即為 obtain board approval，故選 (C)。"},{"q":"The proposed merger is expected to create significant business growth, with projected revenues increasing by ________ within two years.","o":[["A","15 percent"],["B","30 percent"],["C","40 percent"],["D","50 percent"]],"a":"(C) 40 percent","zh":"擬議中的合併預計將創造顯著的業務成長，兩年內預估營收將增加百分之四十。","e":"營收數據記憶題。根據 Part 7 新聞稿，合併預期在兩年內產生的營收成長為 \"increasing by 40%\"，應選 (C)。"},{"q":"By signing the consolidated purchasing agreements, the strategic alliance successfully reduced material costs by leveraging their ________.","o":[["A","combined purchasing power"],["B","separate distribution networks"],["C","human resource assets"],["D","regulatory approvals"]],"a":"(A) combined purchasing power","zh":"透過簽署統一採購協議，該策略聯盟藉由運用他們合併後的採購力，成功降低了材料成本。","e":"談判方案與效益。Part 4 講到與供應商談判降價的方法是「運用合併採購力（leveraging our combined purchasing power）」，故選 (A)。"},{"q":"The legal counsel announced that the final contract ________ is highly anticipated by month-end, pending regulatory approval.","o":[["A","negotiation"],["B","finalization"],["C","suspension"],["D","termination"]],"a":"(B) finalization","zh":"法律顧問宣布，合約預計將在月底前完成最終簽署，目前正在等待監管部門的批准。","e":"合約流程專有名詞。根據同義轉換與必考句型，月底（month-end）預期的是合約的「定案、簽署完成（contract finalization）」，故選 (B)。"},{"q":"Through extensive strategic resource integration, the alliance expanded its global network to include 150 ________ across fifteen countries.","o":[["A","competitors"],["B","suppliers"],["C","shareholders"],["D","divisions"]],"a":"(B) suppliers","zh":"透過廣泛的策略資源整合，該聯盟擴展了其全球網絡，納入了跨越 15 個國家的 150 家供應商。","e":"全球整合對象。根據新聞稿，擴展後的網絡包含 150 家「供應商（suppliers = vendors）」，故選 (B)。"}],"say":["Both companies signed a partnership agreement to share technology resources.","It's an excellent collaboration opportunity.","We need board approval for the acquisition terms.","Months of careful negotiation with key stakeholders.","We're negotiating with several suppliers to reduce material costs.","Contract finalization is expected by month-end.","Projected revenues increasing by 40% within two years.","Strengthens our market position through strategic resource integration."]},"16-3":{"tree":"【Ch16-3 營運優化與技術升級 Operations Optimization & Technology Upgrade】\n │\n ├── 🔴 S - Situation (分析現況：識別改善需求)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 克服庫存與營運績效缺口、評估自動化專案可行性\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **performance gaps** (績效缺口), **technology upgrade** (技術升級), **projections** (預估)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── Performance gaps identified in last quarter's operations review. / The assessment revealed multiple efficiency issues.\n │\n ├── 📋 T - Task (制定計畫：規劃升級方案)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 確定六週分階段上線時程、排定優先設備維護計畫\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **implementation timeline** (實施時程), **transition in phases** (分階段過渡), **monthly service checks** (每月維護)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── The implementation timeline spans six weeks. / Different departments transitioning to the new system in phases.\n │\n ├── 💡 A - Action (執行優化：實施技術方案)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 安排週末安裝避開營運、委託 TechServ 外包商提供三日系統實踐訓練\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **install** (安裝), **minimize disruption** (最小化干擾), **hands-on practice** (實踐練習), **TechServ** (外包商)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── We'll install the new system during the weekend. / Contracted with TechServ Solutions for ongoing support.\n │\n ├── ✅ R - Result (評估成效：衡量改善成果)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 提升生產力 20%、預計 8 個月內靠效率節省回收初期軟體投資\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **increase productivity by 20%** (提升20%生產力), **projected savings** (預估節省), **8 months offset** (8個月抵消)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── The new software system will increase productivity by twenty percent. / Initial implementation costs will be offset within eight months.\n │\n ├── 🔧 技術優化三大活動與時程 (Upgrade Activities & Timeline)\n │    ├── 實施時程 ── **six weeks total** (六週上線) / **three-day hands-on training** (三天操作訓練)\n │    ├── 執行順序 ── equipment maintenance (設備維護) ➔ system installation (系統安裝) ➔ staff training (員工培訓)\n │    └── 回收期程 ── **offset within eight months** (八個月內回收初始成本)\n │\n └── ⚠ 三大高頻防雷陷阱 (Common Traps)\n      ├── 1. 時間順序 ── 必須是「先維護 (maintenance)，再安裝 (installation)，最後才培訓 (training)」，順序顛倒即是雷\n      ├── 2. 實施期程 ── 軟體全面實施的期程是 6 週（six weeks），不是 6 個月\n      └── 3. 支援來源 ── 泰克服 (TechServ Solutions) 是一家「外部承包支援公司 (external contractor)」，並非公司內部 IT 單位","quiz":[{"q":"According to Thomas Park's memo, the newly implemented inventory software is projected to ________ operational productivity by twenty percent.","o":[["A","offset"],["B","increase"],["C","negotiate"],["D","establish"]],"a":"(B) increase","zh":"根據湯馬斯·朴的備忘錄，新實施的庫存軟體預計將使營運生產力提高百分之二十。","e":"多益高頻動詞搭配。營運優化的終極指標是「提高（increase = boost）生產力（productivity）」，故選 (B)。"},{"q":"The Chief Operations Officer confirmed that the entire transition process across all departments will span ________ before full deployment is achieved.","o":[["A","three days"],["B","eight months"],["C","six weeks"],["D","two years"]],"a":"(C) six weeks","zh":"營運長確認，在實現全面部署之前，所有部門的整個轉換過程將跨越六週。","e":"上線時程細節。根據 Part 4 獨白，\"The implementation timeline spans six weeks\"，故選 (C)。"},{"q":"To ensure a successful adoption, the transition program includes three days of ________ training based on real-world operation scenarios.","o":[["A","pilot testing"],["B","hands-on"],["C","regulatory"],["D","automated"]],"a":"(B) hands-on","zh":"為確保成功採用，轉換計畫包括了三天基於真實營運場景的實踐（動手）培訓。","e":"培訓方式術語。多益經典搭配詞：hands-on practice（動手操作/實踐練習）與 hands-on training 互為代換，故選 (B)。"},{"q":"The finance department estimated that the initial technology upgrade costs would be fully ________ by efficiency savings within eight months.","o":[["A","streamlined"],["B","optimized"],["C","offset"],["D","renovated"]],"a":"(C) offset","zh":"財務部門估計，初始技術升級成本將在八個月內完全被效率節省所抵消（回收）。","e":"財務回收動詞。Initial costs will be \"offset\" (抵消/回收)，故選 (C)。"},{"q":"Because TechServ Solutions is an ________ contractor, our internal staff must coordinate closely with their specialists during the weekend installation.","o":[["A","executive"],["B","external"],["C","internal"],["D","administrative"]],"a":"(B) external","zh":"由於泰克服解決方案公司是外部承包商，我們的內部員工必須在週末安裝期間與他們的專家密切協調。","e":"身分與角色區分陷阱。TechServ Solutions 是外包公司，即 external contractor，故選 (B)。"}],"say":["Performance gaps identified in last quarter's operations review.","The assessment revealed multiple efficiency issues.","The implementation timeline spans six weeks.","Different departments transitioning to the new system in phases.","We'll install the new system during the weekend.","Contracted with TechServ Solutions for ongoing support.","The new software system will increase productivity by twenty percent.","Initial implementation costs will be offset within eight months."]},"16-4":{"tree":"【Ch16-4 策略擴張與資本投資 Strategic Expansion & Capital Investment】\n │\n ├── 🔴 S - Situation (評估機會：識別成長潛力)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 克服產能不足限制、掌握新興市場與地理進出優勢\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **growth strategy** (成長策略), **warehouse access** (倉庫進出), **limitations** (限制)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── Current limitations need to be addressed. / Near the airport for better warehouse access.\n │\n ├── 📋 T - Task (制定策略：規劃擴張方案)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 明確明年 3 家分店計畫、核定多重文章之不同資金規模\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **investment budget** (投資預算), **three branches** (三家分店), **capital** (資本)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── The board approved plans to build a new distribution facility. / Opening three branches next year.\n │\n ├── 💡 A - Action (執行建設：實施投資計畫)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 啟動 18 個月大建工程、翻新老舊廠房使製造力倍增\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **construction** (建設), **factory renovation** (工廠翻新), **eighteen months** (18個月完工)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── Construction begins next month, with completion expected within eighteen months. / The factory renovation project will double our production capacity.\n │\n ├── ✅ R - Result (實現成長：評估投資成效)\n │    ├── 溝通目標 ── 兩年營收成長 30%、每季向股東定期匯報施工進度\n │    ├── 核心字彙 ── **double capacity** (產能翻倍), **30% revenue growth** (30%營收成長), **quarterly updates** (季度更新)\n │    └── 必考句型 ── Strategic planning indicates 30% revenue growth within two years. / Reduce shipping costs by consolidating distribution points.\n │\n ├── 🏗 擴張投資三大財務數據與陷阱 (Expansion Financial Metrics)\n │    ├── 資金預算 ── **Part 3 對話 = $5M** [10, 62] / **Part 4 獨白 = $10M** [11, 67] / **Part 7 閱讀 = $25M** [12, 68]\n │    ├── 完工期程 ── Construction next month ➔ Complete **within 18 months** (18 個月內竣工)\n │    └── 成長目標 ── **production capacity doubled** (產能增 100%) ➔ **30% revenue growth** within 2 years\n │\n └── ⚠ 三大高頻防雷陷阱 (Common Traps)\n      ├── 1. 金額混淆 ── 必須認清不同文章指涉的金額規模：對話 500 萬、獨白 1000 萬、閱讀備忘錄 2500 萬\n      ├── 2. 時間錯配 ── 建設是從「下個月」開始，而預期完工時間則是「18 個月內」，千萬不要混淆兩者\n      └── 3. 成長預測 ── 翻新工程使「產能/產量翻倍 (double capacity)」，而策略成效則是「兩年內營收成長 30% (30% revenue growth)」","quiz":[{"q":"According to the strategic report, GlobalTech's newly approved distribution facility will be located near the airport for better ________.","o":[["A","quality checks"],["B","warehouse access"],["C","strategic planning"],["D","project management"]],"a":"(B) warehouse access","zh":"聯邦航空配送設施將位於機場附近，以便有更好的倉庫進出通道。","e":"地點因果關係題。對話中明確指出：The location will be near the airport for better warehouse access，故選 (B)。"},{"q":"The Chief Executive Officer’s memorandum to shareholders outlines a total investment budget of ________ across all strategic projects.","o":[["A","$5 million"],["B","$10 million"],["C","$25 million"],["D","$30 million"]],"a":"(C) $25 million","zh":"執行長給股東的備忘錄概述了所有策略專案的總投資預算為 2,500 萬美元。","e":"金額比對陷阱。此題指定為「給股東的備忘錄（memorandum to shareholders）」，對應 Part 7 閱讀。閱讀中明確提到 \"The investment totals $25 million across all projects\"，故選 (C)。"},{"q":"Management expects that once the factory renovation project is successfully finalized, the manufacturing plant will ________ its production capacity.","o":[["A","double"],["B","reduce"],["C","offset"],["D","coordinate"]],"a":"(A) double","zh":"管理階層預計，一旦工廠翻新專案成功完成，該製造廠將使其實體產能翻倍。","e":"產能效益動詞。講義指出翻新工程的具體效果是「產能翻倍（double our production capacity）」，故選 (A)。"},{"q":"According to the construction timeline, the main infrastructure facility is scheduled to begin next month and reach completion within ________.","o":[["A","six weeks"],["B","eight months"],["C","eighteen months"],["D","two years"]],"a":"(C) eighteen months","zh":"根據建設時程表，主要基礎設施專案定於下個月動工，並預期在 18 個月內完工。","e":"完工時程細節。Part 4 獨白中明確提及 \"completion expected within eighteen months\"，故選 (C)。6週是 Ch16-3 的系統升級時程。"},{"q":"The project management team is required to prepare and submit ________ updates to keep all shareholders informed of the expansion’s progress.","o":[["A","monthly"],["B","quarterly"],["C","annual"],["D","bi-weekly"]],"a":"(B) quarterly","zh":"專案管理團隊必須準備並提交季度更新，以使所有股東隨時了解擴張的進度。","e":"更新頻率細節。根據 Part 7 備忘錄結尾，\"Our project management team will provide quarterly updates\"，故選 (B)。"}],"say":["Current limitations need to be addressed.","Near the airport for better warehouse access.","The board approved plans to build a new distribution facility.","Opening three branches next year.","Construction begins next month, with completion expected within eighteen months.","The factory renovation project will double our production capacity.","Strategic planning indicates 30% revenue growth within two years.","Reduce shipping costs by consolidating distribution points."]}};